{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades","id":1032843,"title":"What We Know So Far: Deviant the Renegades","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Deviant: The Renegades"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-16T12:37:33-08:00","id":1032843,"title":"What We Know So Far: Deviant the Renegades","content":"Here's a paraphrased sum-up of what's been revealed so far about Deviant the Renegades. Please do add &amp;/or correct!:<br /> <br /> Inspirations: Orphan Black, Akira, Spawn, Tetsuo, Brindlefly, Dr. Manhattan from Watchmen, Eleven from Stranger Things (lots of Cronenburg-ey protagonists mutating as a parallel to their isolations). I'd like to add Alex Mack, Dark Angel and CW's Beauty and the Beast to the list as well.<br /> <br /> Deviants (AKA Remade)<br /> People who\u2019ve been transformed into supernatural beings through the action of humans - sometimes even themselves. Unlike, say, being embraced as a vampire or Awakening as a mage, their transformation doesn't have anything guiding it. Their souls crack open under the strain, causing them to lack the ability of normal humans and most supernatural beings to define their own selfhood, and instinctively overcompensate by defining themselves through others; in game mechanics, Deviants have no Virtue/Vice traits, and use something kinda like vampire's touchstones instead. Their two Integrity traits - Loyalty and Conviction - come with touchstones that serve as both virtue/vice, and aspirations<br /> <br /> Variations: Deviants\u2019 powers.<br /> Bought in an unusual manner compared to other splat powers. Voluntary ones are rolled with Attribute + Variation\u2019s rating + Power Trait. Variation rating is not linked to XP cost. They have flat costs, the strength being decided by the player, balancing each Varation with a Scar (the downside). The strength of the Variations also determines the strength of the conspiracy hunting you. Going too long without interaction with touchstones worsens the Scars, and increasing Instability. When Scars get bad enough, their linked Variations increase or the Scar manifests new Variations. To have a human appearance requires low level Variations only OR a separate Variation that suppresses all other Variations &amp; Scars while active (Bruce Banner\u2019s human form/active camouflage). A Variation to mentally link multiple Deviants exists. All Scars and Variations can be rated 1-5 or some range within 1-5 (2-5, 3-4, etc). This ranking is not the same as the magnitude rating discussed below.<br /> From the &quot;Deviant at GenCon&quot; thread: Dave Brookshaw says Variations are grouped by Clade - along with a few universal ones (Approximately half of the Variations in the core are Universal rather than Clade Variations according to Eric Z.)- though you can take a Variation for another Clade if you can think of a way to change its appearance to suit. Scars are grouped by physical, mental, and social, and can be combined freely with Variations.<br /> From Onyx Path podcast interview Episode 40 on Feb 22, 2019:<br /> -All Variations and Scars have a Magnitude Rating. Each Variation must be balanced by a Scar of equal magnitude. Magnitude is a measure of both the power level of a given Remade or group of remade (2-15 is the range for Magnitude) and the power level of the Conspiracy/ies that is/are hunting the Remade). All players in a single DtR game should ideally stay within the same Magnitude range of each other.<br /> Clarification from Eric on page 11 of this thread: &quot;Balancing Scars and Variations: A single Scar can &quot;support&quot; multiple Variations of lower Magnitude. However, it isn't as simple as &quot;Total Magnitude of Variations = Total Magnitude of Scars.&quot; I'm going to hold back on being more specific than that at this time, though.&quot;<br /> -There are three grades of Variations and Scars:<br /> Involuntary (works w/out your control. Think Banner's emotionally fueled transformations to Hulk),<br /> Voluntary (You have control but it costs you to use it: pain, further mutation, gaining Instability, amnesia, etc.)<br /> Persistent (Permanent mutations, Always on)<br /> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/universal-variations-deviant-the-renegades/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/universal-var...the-renegades/</a><br /> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/a-collection-of-scars-deviant-the-renegades/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/a-collection-...the-renegades/</a><br /> <br /> Fuel (sort of): INSTABILITY/STABILITY<br /> &quot;you won't see Remade fuelled by any fuel stats you know\u201d So maybe brand new fuel, or even no fuel at all.<br /> -In Feb 22, 2019 podcast, Eric Zawadzki described Instability as &quot;like Clarity&quot; but if it fills with Aggravated Damage, that is when you mutate beyond your ability to survive (Character death). When not pursuing either Conviction nor Loyalty, Instability worsens.<br /> -4/18/2019 post here: Eric Zawadzki said, &quot;Stability is the &quot;health track&quot; on which Deviants take Instability as damage (minor, medium, and major). Instability makes it harder to manage your Scars (especially, but not exclusively, Involuntary Scars) and can make your Scars worse or cause/allow you to develop new Scars (&quot;allow&quot; because in order to purchase a new Variation, you have to have a Scar available that is powerful enough to entangle with the new Variation). It really isn't a fuel stat so much as a gauge of your progress toward complete destabilization (with its accompanying messy death).&quot; While not traditional fuel it is the cost paid for activating some Variations.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/stability-deviant-the-renegades/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/OPP-Metal.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/stability-deviant-the-renegades/\" target=\"_blank\"> Stability [Deviant: The Renegades] &ndash; Onyx Path Publishing </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/stability-deviant-the-renegades/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://theonyxpath.com/stability-deviant-the-renegades/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> LAST DEV BLOG BEFORE KICKSTARTER THURSDAY 9/19/19!!!<br /> <br /> Power Trait: ACCLIMATION<br /> Don\u2019t start with any dots in it. Can only be bought at major story milestones. Only goes up to 5. Supernatural Tolerance is Power Trait + HIGHEST RANKING VARIATION. Instability has been mentioned and perhaps it is a variation on the usual Power trait indicating how far out of a character's control their power is growing????<br /> -4/18/2019 post here: Eric Zawadzki confirmed that Acclimation IS the Power stat. The upper limit of 5 is indeed a way to illustrate the differentiation of power between Deviants with low ranking variations and other splats or Deviants with high ranking variations.<br /> .<br /> Integrity: Dual Stats \u2013 CONVICTION &amp; LOYALTY<br /> Conviction, like Vice, is easy to fulfill, but doesn\u2019t stave off mutation for long. It involves harassing their creators. Loyalty, like Virtue, is harder, but staves off mutation longer and can even reverse the course of a deviant\u2019s transformation in extreme circumstances. It involves finding something or someone worth protecting. If a Renegade is able to balance their loyalty and conviction, they become Guardians.<br /> Settling, or isolating oneself from all touchstones leads to steady, extreme, and ultimately lethal terminal mutations (a short period of high power, then your own Scars kill you. Word count is being set aside to handle replacing cast members during play). This is called Instability.<br /> - \u201cRemade who are still working for the conspiracies reverse the effects of Conviction and Loyalty, and will - we plan - be the subject of a sourcebook early on in Deviant's gameline.\u201d These are called the Devoted. A Devoted whose hatred drives her or him to extreme is a Nemesis, the equivalent of the Renegade Guardians.<br /> - &quot;A Feral is what a Deviant becomes if she loses all her Touchstones (or never develops any in the first place). They don't have a way to get rid of Instability, so they tend not to last very long.&quot; Indicates a possible antagonist, and hints at Instability being able to be healed by interacting with your Conviction and/or Loyalty touchstones.<br /> - Remade start with at least 3 dots of Conviction and 1 dot of Loyalty, &amp; 1 more dot based on Origin. Conviction + Loyalty = 5 dots max. the two together cannot be more than 5 total dots.<br /> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/conviction-and-loyalty-deviant-the-renegades/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/conviction-an...the-renegades/</a><br /> <br /> Origin: how you got transformed. Each Origin grants an extra dot of Conviction or Loyalty and grants a Scar Free Magnitude of either a Subtle or an Overt Variation Known Origins:<br /> 1) Exalted (Autourgic - self-made, fully aware and wishing to be changed), Speculation: +1 Loyalty, +1 Scar Free Magnitude of an Overt Variation<br /> 2) Unwilling (Exomorph - &quot;Unwilling&quot; says it all. Forced into Divergence), Speculation: +1 Conviction, +1 Scar Free Magnitude of an Overt Variation<br /> 3) Volunteer (Epimorph - Agreed to it, but not out of desire for the Divergence itself), +1 Loyalty, +1 Scar Free Magnitude of a Subtle Variation<br /> 4) Born (Genotypal - inherited, experimental conception, changed in utero), +1 Conviction, +1 Scar Free Magnitude of a Subtle Variation<br /> 5) Accident (Pathological - mentioned as part of Dave's description of a possible character - an accidental animal/human hybrid). +2 Scar Free Magnitude of Variations (unknown if both variations are subtle, overt, or one of each)<br /> The process and moment that changes a human into one of the Remade is called the Divergence.<br /> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/halloween-bonus-origins-deviant-the-renegades/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/halloween-bon...the-renegades/</a><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Clade: the kind of thing you are now. Known Clades:<br /> 1) Invasive (AKA Cyborgs - Inanimate implants: cybernetics, relics, machine grafts/prosthetics),<br /> 2) Cephalist (AKA Psychics - Mind over Matter/Psychic/Mental powers),<br /> 3) Chimerics (AKA Hybrids - Animal/Human hybrid - chimeras, I imagine Moreau Island creatures or Dark Angel),<br /> 4) Coactives (AKA Infused - bound to some otherworldly power source or concept or entity - the astral, the fae, the spirit world, the underworld, time itself, etc),<br /> 5) Mutant (AKA Grotesques. - Biological/Spiritual rejection of intended Divergence Clade can cause random mutation. has a focus on body horror and/or mutations. Bit of a catch-all).<br /> Feb 22, 2019 podcast: Eric Zawadzki mentioned &quot;Adaptations&quot; as minor effects specific to Clades (perhaps along the lines of a Seeming blessing?)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/an-introduction-to-clades-deviant-the-renegades/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/an-introducti...the-renegades/</a><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Form: much like a Vampire bloodline, or a Werewolf Lodge, this apparent z-splat further defines the Remade's new nature (symbiote, amalgam form, etc.)</span><br /> <br /> Endgame: Dying of your own uncontrolled mutations. Maybe: &quot;best you can hope for is a delicate balancing act between degeneration and keeping connected to others.&quot; I.E - Guardian renegades or Nemesis loyalists<br /> <br /> The Creating Organizations<br /> Built at character creation with points derived from how powerful the pcs are. Less Granular than Hunter\u2019s tier system. Lots of possibilities and escalation ideas. The creators of Remade are called Progenitors. Similar to Krewe creation in Geist 2e. All powers, variations and merits are tagged as Covert or Overt. Overt ones multiple a conspiracy's dice pool to notice you on their radar when you use them (tracking your bank accounts if you use Resources, picking up energy signatures of a given power or scar drawback, etc.).<br /> - From Onyx Path podcast 40 on Feb 22, 2019: &quot;Web of Pain&quot; - concept that ALL the Remade Conspiracies are connected in someway and report to each other on spotted Remade on the run.<br /> - 4/18/2019 post by Eric Zawadzki: A conspiracy's Standing is its power stat (like Krewe's Esotery), and It's &quot;superpowers&quot; are called Icons, each of which is linked to a specific &quot;Node&quot; (similiar to the Linchpins of a God-Machine Infrastructure). If the Node is converted or destroyed, the &quot;health&quot; of the conspiracy (like the Krewe's Congregation) declines and its associated Icon is lost.<br /> - Sometimes Conspiracies experiment on animals, forcing Divergence on them. Non-human animals that undergo Divergence are called Manticores.<br /> <br /> Future Books: Include Amalgams (early development name for Deviants that used to be more than one person, like Firestorm from DC comics), Loyalist Deviants and Deviants created by the other supernatural splats<br /> <br /> Feb 22, 2019 Onyx Path podcast: <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/episode-40-deviant-the-zawadski/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/episode-40-deviant-the-zawadski/</a><br /> <br /> Additional OnyxPath blog posts:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/deviant-deviant-the-renegades/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/OPP-Metal.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/deviant-deviant-the-renegades/\" target=\"_blank\"> Deviant [Deviant: The Renegades] &ndash; Onyx Path Publishing </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/deviant-deviant-the-renegades/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://theonyxpath.com/deviant-deviant-the-renegades/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/one-of-a-kind-deviant-the-renegades/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/one-of-a-kind...the-renegades/</a><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/variations-on-a-theme/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/OPP-Metal.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/variations-on-a-theme/\" target=\"_blank\"> Variations on a Theme &ndash; Onyx Path Publishing </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/variations-on-a-theme/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://theonyxpath.com/variations-on-a-theme/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> OnyxPath blog info about the playtest at Midwinter:<br /> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/deviant-at-midwinter-deviant-the-renegades/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/deviant-at-mi...the-renegades/</a><br /> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/deviant-at-midwinter-deviant-the-renegades-2/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/deviant-at-mi...e-renegades-2/</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12074,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","user":"Robert D","date":". 09-17-2019, 03:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":15}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T21:50:27-08:00","id":1033146,"title":"","content":"If I recall one of the other Clades mentioned is Parasitic/Symbiotic, a la Guyver and Venom symbiote. Animal/Human hybrid matches up with the inspiration of The Fly, but not sure if that fits under the categories of the more Cronenberg-ian category. Invisible man and of course Dr. Jekyll were mentioned for being under this game's category, though I imagine Jekyll is arguably under the hybrid category or the &quot;Hulk&quot; category if they aren't one in the same.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5557-runcible","name":"Runcible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5557_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"164"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T05:21:07-08:00","id":1033276,"title":"","content":"Symbiotes aren't a Clade, but the game will handle them","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T08:25:59-08:00","id":1033379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1033276#post1033276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Symbiotes aren't a Clade, but the game will handle them</div> </div> </div> </div>As playable options?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T12:21:24-08:00","id":1033539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1033379#post1033379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As playable options?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Maybe Symbiotes are a Variation type?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T20:38:04-08:00","id":1034427,"title":"","content":"It is every comic fan's dream to be able to say &quot;We are Venom!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3934-fetch","name":"Fetch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3934_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T15:22:56-08:00","id":1035485,"title":"","content":"IIRC, players will take on the role of Renegade Deviants by default, but a future book may give information for playing as a Loyalist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T23:34:45-08:00","id":1035637,"title":"","content":"I thought symbiotes/parasites were called out as an origin?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T08:05:59-08:00","id":1035711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Variations ... have flat costs, the strength being decided by the player, balancing each Varation with a Scar (the downside). The strength of the Variations also determines the strength of the conspiracy hunting you. </div> </div> </div>If I recall correctly, the player gets to decide whether the balance goes into Scars or conspiracies.<br /> <br /> DaveB also said that Clades were independent of the process used to make the Deviant: ie, a cyborg could just as easily be the result of a fucked up ritual involving a technology spirit as high-tech surgery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T11:21:49-08:00","id":1035766,"title":"","content":"I'd love the option of making an exile from some other reality. Off the top of my head the only examples I can think of are that Highlander movie where it was explained that the immortals were exiles from some alien planet and Rosswell High (I think that's what it was called).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T20:01:37-08:00","id":1035927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Live Bait</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1035766#post1035766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd love the option of making an exile from some other reality. Off the top of my head the only examples I can think of are that Highlander movie where it was explained that the immortals were exiles from some alien planet and Rosswell High (I think that's what it was called).</div> </div> </div> </div>You dare mention the forbidden movie? Even the later released cuts exorcised the extra-terrestrial parts...that said, we do have a lot of options for outside normal reality in CoD.<br /> <br /> Emanation realms, hisil, timeline splinters, the hedge, the underworld, the abyss, the lower depths, that space within the gauntlet, where ever quashmallium come from, the supernal, the astral, places that aren't, extra-dimensional spaces, different twilight frequencies and C!Acardia just off the top of my head.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T20:43:58-08:00","id":1035935,"title":"","content":"CIArcadia?<br /> <br /> <i>You don't remember being taken - all you remember is opening your eyes to see a Man in Black wearing deely-boppers and drug store fairy wings operating on you. Now you have an earpiece, a black suit (that you can't take off), and lungs full of hallucinogenic pixie dust that you can cough out at will.</i><br /> <br /> (I misread C!Arcadia - the imagery makes me happy though, so c'est la vie).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T21:18:49-08:00","id":1035944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1035935#post1035935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">CIArcadia?<br /> <br /> <i>You don't remember being taken - all you remember is opening your eyes to see a Man in Black wearing deely-boppers and drug store fairy wings operating on you. Now you have an earpiece, a black suit (that you can't take off), and lungs full of hallucinogenic pixie dust that you can cough out at will.</i><br /> <br /> (I misread C!Arcadia - the imagery makes me happy though, so c'est la vie).</div> </div> </div> </div>...permission to borrow this for a Lost game when 2e comes out?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T23:10:53-08:00","id":1035969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1035944#post1035944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...permission to borrow this for a Lost game when 2e comes out?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. I wouldn't know if you did or not, so knock yourself out (with your lung-fulls of LSD).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T00:22:35-08:00","id":1039295,"title":"","content":"So, I saw a writeup about this game the other day and pretty much immediately made an account here specifically for it. It reminded me of an older video game series that has a similar premise, <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0B3lHfivQMQ\" target=\"_blank\">Prototype</a>. It's pretty much one of my favorite games, so I'm hoping we can pull off something similar in this one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12921-dmw45","name":"DMW45","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T10:52:12-08:00","id":1041920,"title":"","content":"This is from Warren Ellis' introduction to the WildStorm revival. WildStorm being a comic line I thought was particularly predisposed to being like Deviant.<br /> <br /> 'I started by making a list of what I considered to be the central ideas behind the original WildStorm books. Aliens on Earth. Black ops and intel. Scientific experiments on people. Hybridization. Secret power structures.<br /> ...<br /> What does bringing WildStorm back actually give to the world? What does it have to say about the world in 2017?<br /> <br /> We're more paranoid about secret power structures in the world than ever before. And we're even hungrier for big mad stories and fantasies, because our suspension of disbelief is complex - we want the epic stories, but we want them to give us a new view of the world we're in, too.<br /> <br /> I keep coming back to two metaphors for all this. In one sense, it's like building out a cinematic universe. In another, I find myself making references to Game of Thrones. Both of these things seem to apply - in the first instance, clear and linear worldbuilding that spints out new projects. In the other, a rich and complex story that creates a broad fabric of a story universe.<br /> <br /> This, in particular, is the goal of the first and main book of the first two years, which I'm calling The Wild Storm.<br /> <br /> The Wild Storm is, essentially, about one act of selflessness destabilizing and revealing a shadow world of hidden government and secret power. The entire story reels out from that one act. It's a covert history of terrible things. There's a line from an old song that I like. 'The past is steeped in shame, but tomorrow's fair game.' The line through the first two years to the top of year three is into the dark and out again to something aspirational.<br /> <br /> And it does get dark. This is a story of the human response to secret power structures and ancient conspiracies. The proper WildStorm stuff. And it has layers. Over the two years we start with what looks like a covert intelligence org armed with breakthrough science and carte blanche at war with a worldchanging corporation. Then we reveal more. Drill down. Literally, in one case. We start with a world we know and strip it down to reveal its true nature.'<br /> <br /> EDIT: Incredibly sorry, I meant to put this in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/947212-deviant-the-renegades/page10\">the other Deviant</a> thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-04-2017, 02:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T08:49:42-08:00","id":1042973,"title":"","content":"So the Remades souls are cracked? That sounds dangerous like the wall of a nuclear reactor cracking open. I expect some kind of Disquiet-like effect at play here. All souls radiate, now some more than others it seems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7106-extant-reality","name":"Extant Reality","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7106_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T09:49:42-08:00","id":1043008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Extant Reality</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1042973#post1042973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the Remades souls are cracked? That sounds dangerous like the wall of a nuclear reactor cracking open. I expect some kind of Disquiet-like effect at play here. All souls radiate, now some more than others it seems.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure that will be the case. You could make the argument that a Deviant's Variations and Scars <i>are</i> the &quot;radiation&quot;, or at least the result of it. If they have an effect on the world around the Deviant, then that would be the effect of the radiation, and if they only effect the Deviant himself, then it is all contained within his body. To introduce a unifying mechanic by which Deviants inadvertently influence the world around them like Disquiet would be to create uniformity among them. If there is anything that I have gotten out of all the hints that have been dropped it is that even though all Deviants are broken, they are all broken in different ways. Each of them is a category of one, and the only thing they have in common is that they do not fit into other categories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty","name":"Minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T05:20:32-08:00","id":1043487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Extant Reality</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1042973#post1042973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the Remades souls are cracked? That sounds dangerous like the wall of a nuclear reactor cracking open. I expect some kind of Disquiet-like effect at play here. All souls radiate, now some more than others it seems.</div> </div> </div> </div>So far, the only mechanical effect of soul-cracking seems to be they replace their Integrity meter with Conviction and Loyalty. Which also may tie into their anchor traits (Vice &amp; Virtue). It has to do with Deviants being unable to define themselves without referencing to others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T06:34:50-08:00","id":1043514,"title":"","content":"Why did all of this somehow remind me of a lower-scale <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Comicbook/Supergod\" target=\"_blank\">Supergod?</a> What with it's superbeing creating from three extraterrestrial Fungus-fused Astraunauts, the blue skinned mix of Human DNA, AI and nanomachines called Krishna, a guy that creates his lovecraftian monsters and tools out of people etc. Which is totally worth reading, btw.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","user":"Wormwood","date":". 02-04-2017, 09:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-28T05:47:43-07:00","id":1108720,"title":"","content":"Dave just let on to an Origin. I don't know if it is the same as the In Vitrio that was mentioned earlier, but i'll add it to the front page just in case:<br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw\">Dave Brookshaw</a> replied to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1105598-mutations-causing-superhuman-mortals\">Mutations causing superhuman mortals?</a></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness\">Chronicles of Darkness</a></span></span></span></span></span><br /> <div align=\"right\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"color:#6A6A6A\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">06-20-2017, 07:09 AM</span></span></span> <span style=\"color:#6A6A6A\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><b><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Subscribed</span></b></span></span></span></span></span></span></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><i><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Originally posted by <b>nofather</b> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1105598-mutations-causing-superhuman-mortals?p=1105602#post1105602\">View Post</a></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">As far as I know there isn't already a Merit for it in second edition, but it would certainly make sense for there to be one. I imagine if it's not already in print it would pop up in Deviant.</span></span></i></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Born with it&quot; is one of the Origins (x-splats) for Deviant, covering everything from Orphan Black to the Innsmouth Look.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-28T10:47:16-07:00","id":1108823,"title":"","content":"While I like the ideas around this game I have trounle wrapping my head around how a clade comes together save for being from connected routes. Some x-men style thing maybe?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13584-horace-tabor","name":"Horace Tabor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13584_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-01T16:25:39-07:00","id":1110400,"title":"","content":"Could anyone help me with something deviant-related? in this podcast (<a href=\"http://podcast.darker-days.org/e/darker-days-presents-darkling-42-deviant-activities/\" target=\"_blank\">http://podcast.darker-days.org/e/dar...nt-activities/</a>) Dave Brookshaw is talking about Deviant,but since english is my second language i'm having a hard time understanding whaat he's saying from minute 20:50 to 22:00. cold anyone listen to this part of the podcast and tell me what dave said?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-01T17:26:00-07:00","id":1110416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1110400#post1110400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could anyone help me with something deviant-related? in this podcast (<a href=\"http://podcast.darker-days.org/e/darker-days-presents-darkling-42-deviant-activities/\" target=\"_blank\">http://podcast.darker-days.org/e/dar...nt-activities/</a>) Dave Brookshaw is talking about Deviant,but since english is my second language i'm having a hard time understanding whaat he's saying from minute 20:50 to 22:00. cold anyone listen to this part of the podcast and tell me what dave said?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Let's see trying to split the groups into five types for ease on the player types. Then that it's a bit tricky since it's not really correlated with anything from &quot;One World of Darkness&quot; (Their wording not mine) aside from something called Freak Legion or whenever the Technocracy screwed with people. Then basically that whoever is responsible for the Deviants change or whatever is refered to as the progenitor and normally their the first people to hunt the Deviant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-01T18:15:19-07:00","id":1110426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1110416#post1110416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Let's see trying to split the groups into five types for ease on the player types. Then that it's a bit tricky since it's not really correlated with anything from &quot;One World of Darkness&quot; (Their wording not mine) aside from something called Freak Legion or whenever the Technocracy screwed with people. Then basically that whoever is responsible for the Deviants change or whatever is refered to as the progenitor and normally their the first people to hunt the Deviant.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh man,i was wondering if deviant was going to be split into five types! Thank you !","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T04:33:01-07:00","id":1123401,"title":"","content":"We have lift off!!! DtR is in the First Draft stage!!!!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T09:28:20-07:00","id":1123519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horace Tabor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1108823#post1108823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I like the ideas around this game I have trounle wrapping my head around how a clade comes together save for being from connected routes. Some x-men style thing maybe?</div> </div> </div> </div>Clades represent the type of differentiation you display, but not how you get it - so a cyborg might be a result of mad science, or the result of a fusion with machine spirits. From that, I would conclude that Origin and Clade are essentially two X-splats rather than an X and Y.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T09:29:27-07:00","id":1123520,"title":"","content":"The y-splats seem to be Renegade and Loyalist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T09:44:15-07:00","id":1123528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1123520#post1123520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The y-splats seem to be Renegade and Loyalist.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Devoted (Loyalists) would be a separate supplement. The core is laser-focused on the Renegade experience.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T09:50:21-07:00","id":1123530,"title":"","content":"A bit like the separation between Forsaken and Pure? Two different groups of Y splats that are diametrically opposed? Even both subtitles point out which group is considered the default playable group.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T10:14:14-07:00","id":1123534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1123528#post1123528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Devoted (Loyalists) would be a separate supplement. The core is laser-focused on the Renegade experience.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yes, I believe Dave has made that abundantly clear. No point muddying waters in the core. But if Y is 'the group you join by choice' then it seems like they would fit. Devoted sounds better than Loyalist, regarding names, though it does suggest more than just loyalty.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11887_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11887\" data-vbnamecard=\"11887\">Tessie</a> <br /> The Pure you don't necessarily join by choice. They're their own template. It's like becoming a werewolf all over again. No x-splat there, just a y-splat of tribes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T10:14:15-07:00","id":1123535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1123528#post1123528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Devoted (Loyalists) would be a separate supplement. The core is laser-focused on the Renegade experience.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yes, I believe Dave has made that abundantly clear. No point muddying waters in the core. But if Y is 'the group you join by choice' then it seems like they would fit. Devoted sounds better than Loyalist, regarding names, though it does suggest more than just loyalty.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11887_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11887\" data-vbnamecard=\"11887\">Tessie</a> <br /> The Pure you don't necessarily join by choice. They're their own template. It's like becoming a werewolf all over again. No x-splat there, just a y-splat of tribes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T10:49:34-07:00","id":1123547,"title":"","content":"Devoted use the exat same x and y splats (Origins and Clades) as Renegades; their difference is in their Integrity traits, where Renegades treat Conviction as something like a vice and Loyalty as something like a virtue, and Devoted are the reverse.<br /> <br /> They'll get enough in DTR's core to use them as antagonists, but we envisage a Guide to the Technocracy style book to flip the game on its head and play a team of Devoted instead of a cohort of Renegades.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":14}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T10:59:30-07:00","id":1123553,"title":"","content":"Maybe it's because I practically grew up on movies with these themes but I'm really looking forward to the game, even without Devoted as a starting option.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T11:46:40-07:00","id":1123573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1123547#post1123547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Devoted use the exat same x and y splats (Origins and Clades) as Renegades; their difference is in their Integrity traits, where Renegades treat Conviction as something like a vice and Loyalty as something like a virtue, and Devoted are the reverse.<br /> <br /> They'll get enough in DTR's core to use them as antagonists, but we envisage a Guide to the Technocracy style book to flip the game on its head and play a team of Devoted instead of a cohort of Renegades.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cohort is an awesome name for a group of Renegades! Of course, I've really liked everything I've seen so far, so I suppose that there's little surprise that I'd like that as well. Do you have any plans for including other critters in the line as well? I can just imagine twisted animal experiments that were the &quot;test subjects&quot; before the Deviants were created.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T15:03:30-07:00","id":1123650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades#post1032843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Endgame: Dying of your own uncontrolled mutations. Maybe: Losing all of your mutations (cure). Otherwise, &quot;best you can hope for is a delicate balancing act between degeneration and keeping connected to others.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that Doctor Manhattan is an inspiration I'm surprised that some kind of ascension isn't an endgame possibility.<br /> <br /> Sure he has some major downsides to his godhood, but it's arguably better than simply dying and waking up as a Ghost in the Underworld.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T17:13:15-07:00","id":1123709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1123547#post1123547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Devoted use the exat same x and y splats (Origins and Clades) as Renegades; their difference is in their Integrity traits, where Renegades treat Conviction as something like a vice and Loyalty as something like a virtue, and Devoted are the reverse.<br /> <br /> They'll get enough in DTR's core to use them as antagonists, but we envisage a Guide to the Technocracy style book to flip the game on its head and play a team of Devoted instead of a cohort of Renegades.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is a small group of Renegades called a cohort in the DtR lexicon?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T20:09:05-07:00","id":1124145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1123528#post1123528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Devoted (Loyalists) would be a separate supplement. The core is laser-focused on the Renegade experience.</div> </div> </div> </div>This makes me so so so so happy. I'm already looking forward to the Devoted sb, but for me, my excitement regarding the whole experience comes from &quot;being screwed with gives you strength, which you use to fight back against the creeps who want to use your power and/or pain.&quot; This is my jam, and DtR looks to feed it in a way nothing has since Mage: the Ascension.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Heroes die. Hope is a phoenix.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2434-captain-aeon","name":"Captain Aeon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2434_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"203"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T18:05:30-07:00","id":1126128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1123650#post1123650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given that Doctor Manhattan is an inspiration I'm surprised that some kind of ascension isn't an endgame possibility.<br /> <br /> Sure he has some major downsides to his godhood, but it's arguably better than simply dying and waking up as a Ghost in the Underworld.</div> </div> </div> </div>that's really the kind of thing saved for an optional &quot;okay, you've hit the upper limits of what the template does but you want to keep going&quot; type supplement than the core, I think. I mean, Beast has it's ascensions in the core book, but other acension/apotheosis stuff, if it has mechanics at all, doesn't go in the core book I don't think.<br /> <br /> If it's possible at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T20:18:29-07:00","id":1126150,"title":"","content":"just found the 2005 flick &quot;Mosquito Man.&quot; Definitely a Deviant the Renegade story","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-09T06:16:56-07:00","id":1226063,"title":"","content":"Hiya folks! any one hear any news on DtR? Excited that it's in redlines <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-05T18:16:29-07:00","id":1232764,"title":"","content":"Very excited, especially since you can play two sides of the story just like mage the awakening, hopefully also having themes of their own while standing as an also authentic experience in it's own right","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","user":"Primordial newcomer","date":". 07-05-2018, 09:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-06T05:36:52-07:00","id":1232840,"title":"","content":"Likewise. Devoted seem like they would be rather unique among WoD factions, especially Devoted who still harbor some grievances with their creator. Hyped and hoping for more info on Clades.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24176-borne","name":"Borne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24176_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-06T07:49:03-07:00","id":1232858,"title":"","content":"Clades is my hope for the next dev blog, whenever that may be lol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-06T09:51:53-07:00","id":1232874,"title":"","content":"What I'm really hoping for borne is that, considering conviction is the hard to earn stat, that will add into that devoted are kinda dead inside, they don't like what they are doing. As you get conviction up, it shows they begin to hate the renegades for what they are doing despite the potential they have.<br /> <br /> Also claded info will be great, imagine what the symbiote could do, and the cyborgs being mistaken for demons","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-06T14:08:48-07:00","id":1232929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1123547#post1123547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They'll get enough in DTR's core to use them as antagonists, but we envisage a Guide to the Technocracy style book to flip the game on its head and play a team of Devoted instead of a cohort of Renegades.</div> </div> </div> </div>Will that include portraying the conspiracies in a more well-meaning light? There's no logical reason why a conspiracy couldn't want to help Deviants without hurting anyone, but regard them to as too dangerous - to themselves and innocent people - to be running around in the outside world. (Would they even necessarily be wrong about that last part?)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1232858#post1232858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Clades is my hope for the next dev blog, whenever that may be lol.</div> </div> </div> </div>Excellent!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-06T18:12:04-07:00","id":1232969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1232929#post1232929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Will that include portraying the conspiracies in a more well-meaning light? There's no logical reason why a conspiracy couldn't want to help Deviants without hurting anyone, but regard them to as too dangerous - to themselves and innocent people - to be running around in the outside world. (Would they even necessarily be wrong about that last part?)</div> </div> </div> </div>*whistles innocently as he turns in his draft for the Deviant part of the Light of the Sun section of Dark Eras 2...*<br /> <br /> Without attracting the attention of the NDA Death Laser (and with the caveat that we're still a long way from a final draft), I can say that we talked early on about how &quot;having people seeking you out because of your special abilities for the rest of your life&quot; doesn't always have to follow the Orphan Black (et. al.) model.<br /> <br /> Deviant is not a superhero game, but if you look at many superheroes and the organizations that recruit them through the lens of Deviant, you can find some pretty good examples of Conspiracies and Devoted. They and their backers aren't necessarily antagonists, but they aren't exactly encouraging those with remarkable abilities to settle down in some quiet town and get a job selling car insurance, either.<br /> <br /> Think of the Hulk in the MCU. Nick Fury may have the best of intentions in recruiting Bruce Banner for the Avengers, but at the end of the day, everyone expects the Big Guy to show up when things need smashing. Banner isn't always thrilled about that, because the person who most hates who Bruce Banner becomes when he's angry is Bruce Banner. But he also knows that S.H.I.E.L.D. and other organizations are never, ever going to let him out of their sight, so he might as well earn some measure of freedom for playing ball by beating up aliens and killer robots when the situation calls for it.<br /> <br /> The assumption is that anyone who has supernatural abilities should be expected to use them for the good of others - whether &quot;others&quot; means &quot;all humankind&quot; or &quot;Corporation X.&quot; In the superhero genre that sentiment is pretty standard fare, but *outside* of that genre, it is a potential source of horror. You are a tool. You know you're being used as a tool. But you also know that life outside of the Conspiracy is lonely and dangerous (both to you and anyone you meet). You *do* need a certain amount of &quot;managing&quot; to keep your powers from consuming you, but your devotion also makes you vulnerable to exploitation by those you serve.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":17}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-06T19:27:57-07:00","id":1232979,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1094\" data-vbnamecard=\"1094\">Eric Zawadzki</a>, the devoted have their conviction trait as the hard to earn but many benefits stat. What exactly would give devoted the conviction/hate to hunt down renegades, if that's ok to answer","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-06T21:52:43-07:00","id":1232996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1232979#post1232979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1094\" data-vbnamecard=\"1094\">Eric Zawadzki</a>, the devoted have their conviction trait as the hard to earn but many benefits stat. What exactly would give devoted the conviction/hate to hunt down renegades, if that's ok to answer</div> </div> </div> </div>Staying with the superhero parallel, why do the X-Men actively thwart Magneto? He gives other mutants a bad name, right? That endangers them all. He also does some seriously bad things that they feel that they must stop. He uses his powers to destroy his enemies and further himself, whereas they have chosen to serve something greater than themselves that is incompatible with Magneto's objectives and methods.<br /> <br /> To see how Devoted can be villains, through, just replace Professor X with someone whose motives are less pure and whose methods are less virtuous - Thanos, for example, or one of the top scientists working for Hydra. Even the various Top-Siders in Orphan Black are ruthless and will surely find some dirty work for their Devoted to do.<br /> <br /> Working for a conspiracy is a doubled-edged sword, but so is the life of a Renegade. Both have lots of story potential. Like Dave said, in the core the Renegades are the protagonists and the Devoted are the antagonists, but neither is a Storyteller-only faction in the grand scheme of things. There are good Devoted and bad Renegades, and bad Devoted and good Renegades, but there is ample space for shades of grey.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-06T22:23:22-07:00","id":1233000,"title":"","content":"Thanks for answering Eric. I will be looking forward to reading yalls work!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-13T23:12:47-07:00","id":1234876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1123650#post1123650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given that Doctor Manhattan is an inspiration I'm surprised that some kind of ascension isn't an endgame possibility.<br /> <br /> Sure he has some major downsides to his godhood, but it's arguably better than simply dying and waking up as a Ghost in the Underworld.</div> </div> </div> </div>How I interpreted Dr. Manhattan as a possible inspiration, was that his eventual apotheosis at the end of Watchmen comes from the loss of his last touchstones and his rejection of all humanity (his own included). Sure he is all powerful, but as an ST I would make the suggestion that the player wouldn't be able to play that character anymore. How would one even roleplay a being like that and consider it a continuance of any kind of human identity/logic? I imagined his Scars as being that all of his Social skill rolls would eventually be done at a chance die. At the level of full &quot;Instability&quot;, he may just lose all access to Social skills. Even with the Exarchs and ascended Mages they are all to some extent invested (and bound) in the Fallen World and in turn, humanity. But these are just my thoughts and I can definitely see how he seems different from the rest of the inspiration characters.<br /> <br /> I would add Solar (Valiant Comics) to the list (along with almost all of their properties). You have a character who gains very similar powers to Dr. Manhattan through an accident who eventually consumes his reality after losing control and becoming a supermassive black hole. Sure he remakes reality as a place full of superheroes and eventually becomes the protector of earth, but in a chronicle that would only occur after you kill everyone at the table and choose the characters they would become in the reality you made to live out your childhood fantasies. While this is all speculation given the lack of rules for this specific game mechanic, this ending feels like it is in the spirit of what has been spoiled thus far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","user":"lladas","date":". 07-14-2018, 04:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-15T08:06:30-07:00","id":1246343,"title":"","content":"In the Deviant at GenCon thread, Dave Brookshaw said that Variations are grouped by Clade - along with a few universal ones - though you can take a Variation for another Clade if you can think of a way to change its appearance to suit. Scars are grouped by physical, mental, and social, and can be combined freely with Variations.<br /> <br /> &quot;Types,&quot; which I'm guessing are Clades from the above referred to are Invasive, Cephalist, Chimera, and Atypic (which is getting renamed).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"tha