ng> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1280946#post1280946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also ran a Deviant playtest at Midwinter over the weekend, which went over really well!</div> </div> </div> </div>What was The Plot?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-16T17:53:02-08:00","id":1281224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meghan Fitzgerald</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1281070#post1281070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nah, I\u2019ll leave that to the developers. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Understood <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> May I ask what your favorite part of the playtest was (a clever move by the players, a fun twist in your storytelling, that sort of thing)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-16T21:20:05-08:00","id":1281250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1281224#post1281224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Understood <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> May I ask what your favorite part of the playtest was (a clever move by the players, a fun twist in your storytelling, that sort of thing)?</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't at Mid-Winter, but I ran a couple one-shots in late December, and my winner for clever use of a Variation probably goes to my second playtest group:<br /> <br /> The Mutant with Translocation could only teleport to places she could either see (difficult, given the security of the area they wanted to access) or where she had left significant traces of her DNA (some hair, blood, etc.). So, she got her hands on some gum, chewed it up good to make sure it had enough of her DNA in it, and then stuck it to the undersides of food carts, the shoes of guards, and other objects that were bound for the secure area. The Cephalist with Body-Snatcher facilitated further this by taking over a guard's body and using it to place wads of the Mutant's chewed gum anywhere she might need to access in the secure area, so she could go pretty much wherever she wanted, pocket small items in each location, and then teleport out without needing to deal with the scrutiny an exiting guard would.<br /> <br /> Although the first playtest group was the one who carefully combined the Mutant's Shadow Selves (for a distraction), the Chimeric's Bioluminescence (to blind the guards), and the Invasive's Sensor Array (to ignore the blinding light) to storm the communications tower. Any resistance the guards had left in them after that was no match for the Coactive nun with Gigantic, Natural Weapon, and Supernatural Attribute (Strength). <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> (The usual caveats apply: We just entered second drafts. Quite a number of things might still change between now and the time the game is available for public consumption. Management is not responsible for spontaneous mutation, brain damage, or death resulting from exposure to Deviant spoilers. Etc.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-16T21:27:23-08:00","id":1281252,"title":"","content":"Body snatching is always a great ability, I assume it has slight differences from possession. that teleporting ability sounds awesome though","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-16T23:45:09-08:00","id":1281262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1281250#post1281250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wasn't at Mid-Winter, but I ran a couple one-shots in late December, and my winner for clever use of a Variation probably goes to my second playtest group:<br /> <br /> The Mutant with Translocation could only teleport to places she could either see (difficult, given the security of the area they wanted to access) or where she had left significant traces of her DNA (some hair, blood, etc.). So, she got her hands on some gum, chewed it up good to make sure it had enough of her DNA in it, and then stuck it to the undersides of food carts, the shoes of guards, and other objects that were bound for the secure area. The Cephalist with Body-Snatcher facilitated further this by taking over a guard's body and using it to place wads of the Mutant's chewed gum anywhere she might need to access in the secure area, so she could go pretty much wherever she wanted, pocket small items in each location, and then teleport out without needing to deal with the scrutiny an exiting guard would.<br /> <br /> Although the first playtest group was the one who carefully combined the Mutant's Shadow Selves (for a distraction), the Chimeric's Bioluminescence (to blind the guards), and the Invasive's Sensor Array (to ignore the blinding light) to storm the communications tower. Any resistance the guards had left in them after that was no match for the Coactive nun with Gigantic, Natural Weapon, and Supernatural Attribute (Strength). <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> (The usual caveats apply: We just entered second drafts. Quite a number of things might still change between now and the time the game is available for public consumption. Management is not responsible for spontaneous mutation, brain damage, or death resulting from exposure to Deviant spoilers. Etc.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Very clever applications of Variations! and great teamwork!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-21T17:40:32-08:00","id":1282045,"title":"","content":"I just listened to some of the most recent Darker Days Radio podcast, and in it Dave Brookshaw talks a bit about the &quot;overt&quot; and &quot;covert&quot; tags. It sounds like all Variations, Scars, and Merits will be tagged either &quot;overt&quot; or &quot;covert&quot;, and that at the end of the story the Storyteller will roll for the Conspiracy to respond to your cohort with modifiers based on the overt and covert abilities you used. It seems kind of obvious in retrospect, but it's something I never considered. I guess that's why Dave is a game dev and I'm not. <br /> It also sounds like the Conspiracy rules will be similar to the Krewe rules from Geist 2e, if you want an idea of what that will be like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12738,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty","user":"Minty","date":". 01-21-2019, 08:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty","name":"Minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-21T19:42:33-08:00","id":1282059,"title":"","content":"similar to the embeds and exploits it sounds like. however I do think it is more possible that it will be less omniscient detection and more like what's physically witnessed (whether in person or caught on video)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-21T20:30:41-08:00","id":1282068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1282059#post1282059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">similar to the embeds and exploits it sounds like. however I do think it is more possible that it will be less omniscient detection and more like what's physically witnessed (whether in person or caught on video)</div> </div> </div> </div>With Embeds vs. Exploits, it was more a matter of power level. Embeds didn't have as much oomph, but they let you fly under the radar. Exploits, meanwhile, were terribly noisy, but boy could you crack some skulls with those things.<br /> <br /> Overt vs. Subtle is more about how likely your Variation or Scar is to attract the attention of eyewitnesses to you specifically and to leave tongues wagging in your wake. If your Variation can be passed off as luck, or that somehow you're just really, really good at a Skill (which no one nearby realizes you had no training in) or it just makes everyone think you're an Important Person in their organization, that's Subtle. If you're 10 feet tall or have ram's horns or shoot fire from your hands or take flight over a crowded square, that's Overt. Being 10 feet tall is pretty useful (Overt), but being able to puppet someone's body for a few hours is also useful (Subtle).<br /> <br /> Scars are similar. Are you a retired elementary school teacher who can now think of nothing but committing murder all day? That's Subtle. Do you manifest stigmata whenever you peer into the past? That's Overt. Mechanically, a little narrative blood loss (or even a level of bashing or lethal damage) isn't as much of a big deal as entering a delicate negotiation knowing that if anyone so much as makes veiled threat in your direction, you probably won't be able to resist bashing their head against a wall until it breaks open like a rotten cantaloupe.<br /> <br /> Make sense?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-21T20:39:47-08:00","id":1282072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1282068#post1282068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> With Embeds vs. Exploits, it was more a matter of power level. Embeds didn't have as much oomph, but they let you fly under the radar. Exploits, meanwhile, were terribly noisy, but boy could you crack some skulls with those things.<br /> <br /> Overt vs. Subtle is more about how likely your Variation or Scar is to attract the attention of eyewitnesses to you specifically and to leave tongues wagging in your wake. If your Variation can be passed off as luck, or that somehow you're just really, really good at a Skill (which no one nearby realizes you had no training in) or it just makes everyone think you're an Important Person in their organization, that's Subtle. If you're 10 feet tall or have ram's horns or shoot fire from your hands or take flight over a crowded square, that's Overt. Being 10 feet tall is pretty useful (Overt), but being able to puppet someone's body for a few hours is also useful (Subtle).<br /> <br /> Scars are similar. Are you a retired elementary school teacher who can now think of nothing but committing murder all day? That's Subtle. Do you manifest stigmata whenever you peer into the past? That's Overt. Mechanically, a little narrative blood loss (or even a level of bashing or lethal damage) isn't as much of a big deal as entering a delicate negotiation knowing that if anyone so much as makes veiled threat in your direction, you probably won't be able to resist bashing their head against a wall until it breaks open like a rotten cantaloupe.<br /> <br /> Make sense?</div> </div> </div> </div>makes plenty of sense. so it simply means how much the people see that there is something just plain wrong/supernatural about you. also definitely know it's now possible to make a sorta Slasher deviant","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-24T13:44:56-08:00","id":1282502,"title":"","content":"There's a bunch of cool new Deviant info in this podcast episode: <a href=\"http://podcast.darker-days.org/e/96-the-annual-dragonmeet-coffee-bar-special/\" target=\"_blank\">http://podcast.darker-days.org/e/96-...e-bar-special/</a> (starts around five minutes in)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://darker-days.org/\" target=\"_blank\">Darker Days Radio</a> - The World of Darkness Podcast<br /> <a href=\"http://historylessons.libsyn.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Unbuttoned History</a> - A History Podcast with Jokes","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/124-darker-days-mike","name":"Darker Days Mike","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar124_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-24T17:32:59-08:00","id":1282557,"title":"","content":"so a unique resource merit huh. I can understand that, but how would it work if the deviant was an already rich autoturge who has hid his condition well (though, being a deviant, I assume it's extremely hard to hide and probably ruins your mind for rational financial thought","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-24T18:41:49-08:00","id":1282565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darker Days Mike</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1282502#post1282502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a bunch of cool new Deviant info in this podcast episode: <a href=\"http://podcast.darker-days.org/e/96-the-annual-dragonmeet-coffee-bar-special/\" target=\"_blank\">http://podcast.darker-days.org/e/96-...e-bar-special/</a> (starts around five minutes in)</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-25T03:47:35-08:00","id":1282613,"title":"","content":"Can anyone condense the info from the video here?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-25T17:55:07-08:00","id":1282754,"title":"","content":"Video info on Deviant Condensed:<br /> - Organizational rules: broaden cult/secret society organizations as characters with stats and merits, much like Geist 2E's Krewes. You can simulate conflicts between organizations.<br /> - No Cover mechanic like Demon the Descent. Every power, drawback and merit is tagged as Covert or Overt (Overt ones multiply dice pool of Conspiracies to notice you based on your use of the Tagged powers, merits, drawbacks). Resources is Overt (use Resources 4 to buy out of a situation, it may be red flagged by Conspiracy, much like a fugitive's credit cards or cell phone may be monitored for by law enforcement)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12074,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","user":"Robert D","date":". 01-25-2019, 09:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-25T20:26:10-08:00","id":1282776,"title":"","content":"also, just to recall, it was said that the conspiracies are not like the God machine in that they can be omniscient in detecting odd powers. use of deviant powers simply means how obvious an ability is (if no conspiracy members are around, they want know none the wiser, until the ability is put on the internet for them to find)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-27T04:13:42-08:00","id":1283017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1282776#post1282776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">also, just to recall, it was said that the conspiracies are not like the God machine in that they can be omniscient in detecting odd powers. use of deviant powers simply means how obvious an ability is (if no conspiracy members are around, they want know none the wiser, until the ability is put on the internet for them to find)</div> </div> </div> </div>I still might borrow the Subtle/Overt rules for use with cult, Hunter and Hero antagonists in Demon &amp; Beast games on occasion. Maybe for Alchemist groups in Promethean too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T12:17:38-08:00","id":1288356,"title":"","content":"Hi everyone! Has anyone found any new insights or hints on the web about Deviant the Renegades lately?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T21:09:57-08:00","id":1288514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1288356#post1288356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi everyone! Has anyone found any new insights or hints on the web about Deviant the Renegades lately?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably not recently, but there will be more to come in the near-ish future. Let's just say I was recently given a chance to ramble spoilers for about an hour, although I don't know when or how much of that will be made public...<br /> <br /> I'll also be much less stingy with dev blog posts once we get past 2nd drafts. A lot of details are still in flux at this stage, as prone to mutation as the game's protagonists. That's likely to calm down as we move through development and playtesting, though, so I'll be able to share more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-16T04:51:13-08:00","id":1288570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1288514#post1288514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Probably not recently, but there will be more to come in the near-ish future. Let's just say I was recently given a chance to ramble spoilers for about an hour, although I don't know when or how much of that will be made public...<br /> <br /> I'll also be much less stingy with dev blog posts once we get past 2nd drafts. A lot of details are still in flux at this stage, as prone to mutation as the game's protagonists. That's likely to calm down as we move through development and playtesting, though, so I'll be able to share more.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks Eric! That's great to know!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T18:22:42-08:00","id":1290173,"title":"","content":"is there anyone that can compile the information we got from the newest video featuring deviant spoilers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T02:46:34-08:00","id":1290701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1290173#post1290173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">is there anyone that can compile the information we got from the newest video featuring deviant spoilers?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hi! If you post the link to said video I'd happily do that this weekend <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T07:21:15-08:00","id":1290753,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://onyxpathcast.podbean.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://onyxpathcast.podbean.com/</a> this should be it <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12074\" data-vbnamecard=\"12074\">Robert D</a>. if I messed up just tell me","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T12:03:43-08:00","id":1290864,"title":"","content":"Some of the notes I took from <a href=\"https://onyxpathcast.podbean.com/e/episode-40-deviant-the-zawadski/\" target=\"_blank\">this week's podcast with Eric</a>:<br /> <br /> Categories of Variations/Scars:<br /> involuntary - trigger without your control<br /> controlled - costs you in some way, drains your resources, weakens you physically, mutates you further, etc.<br /> persistent - always on<br /> <br /> Web of Pain - the conspiracies are all linked, enabling conspiracies to scale as you get more powerful.<br /> <br /> scales from 2-15 in terms of power level (and corresponding power of the conspiracy).<br /> <br /> Clades include Coactive (belonging to two worlds), Chimeric (two species), Encephalic (?) (psychic), Mutant (being something biologically 'other')<br /> <br /> Some Variations can be reskinned for multiple Clades, while others are more appropriate for a particular one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T13:31:01-08:00","id":1290893,"title":"","content":"thanks <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"51\" data-vbnamecard=\"51\">marin</a>. is it ok if I ask what you mean by power level? (like how powerful is 15?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","user":"Primordial newcomer","date":". 02-22-2019, 04:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T19:08:32-08:00","id":1290959,"title":"","content":"From what the Dev said, a 2 would be a very gritty and basic game with the corresponding conspiracy being a local group of people. He didn't say much about what precisely a 15 Renegade could do, but the corresponding conspiracy would be like if you were running from a pissed off Amazon.com that had the backing of an international mafia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3776-autodefenestrate","name":"AutoDefenestrate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3776_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T20:40:52-08:00","id":1290986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1290864#post1290864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some of the notes I took from [URL=&quot;https://onyxpathcast.podbean.com/e/episode-40-deviant-the-zawadski/&quot;]Encephalic (?) (psychic)</div> </div> </div> </div>Cephalist is the name of the Clade.<br /> <br /> Invasive was the one I didn't have a chance to mention. They're the ones that are part, um, inanimate object. Cyborgs are the obvious example (whether classic or nanotech), but it can also be an artifact that was implanted in or grafted to your body. Their Clade Variations tend to emphasize versatility. Computer-Aided Processing grants Merit dots that you can reassign each chapter, and Omnicompetence does something similar with Skills.<br /> <br /> And a member of any Clade can have any Variation. There are just some that are more likely to be associated with one Clade than with the others. In game terms, your total Magnitude of other Clades' Variations cannot exceed the total Magnitude of your Universal Variations plus the Variations of your own Clade (at least as the rules stand now). So, if you have a total of 7 Magnitude of Variations, 4 of that must come from Universal Variations and/or Variations of your Clade, while the other 3 can come from the Variations of one or more other Clades.<br /> <br /> As to the 2-15 thing, it refers to a character's starting Magnitude worth of Variations (the starting Threat Level). A game with a Magnitude 2 is really low key - not much flashier than a blue book game with a handful of Supernatural Merits per character. 5-7 is enough for one big Variation or a few smaller ones (the Mid-Winter characters were built as 7s). At 10-15, well, you're supposed to have enough firepower to give Mafia!Amazon pause when it tries to subjugate you. (Each Threat Level has its own name, by the way, not just a number.)<br /> <br /> Even at the highest tiers, you're not going to rival the versatility of a moderately powerful mage. Nor do Deviants have an equivalent to a demon Going Loud. In fact, the Remade do not have a unifying list of &quot;cool stuff everyone in this game can do&quot; as in other CofD games (Mage Sight, Pledgecrafting, shapeshifting, etc.), and most of the universal qualities of the Broken are the downsides of their condition (Scars, Loyalty/Conviction, Instability, conspiracies, etc.). What Deviants have is access to a diverse range of capabilities that are broader then Supernatural Merits or Hunter powers, if still fairly narrow in scope (although high-Magnitude Variations can be quite potent within that scope). In my opinion, it is really easy to build a character concept just by picking a Scar or Variation that interests you and running with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T21:00:55-08:00","id":1290992,"title":"","content":"ahh, so deviants no longer have a way of super powered meltdown anymore? also, as of right now, does the book talk about deviants made by other supernaturals (like the ordo dracul)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T21:23:53-08:00","id":1290996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1290992#post1290992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">ahh, so deviants no longer have a way of super powered meltdown anymore? also, as of right now, does the book talk about deviants made by other supernaturals (like the ordo dracul)</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, they can have a superpowered meltdown if they let their Instability get far enough out of hand. But there's more to that than simply having a Mag 5 Variation or two. And while Magnitude 5 Scars are supposed to make a player think hard about whether that Magnitude 5 Variation is really worth it, they won't transform you into a giant, out-of-control blob made up of hand-shaped pseudopods in themselves.<br /> <br /> We're steering clear of crossover in the core, but we'll address Deviants made by other supernatural beings in a later supplement.<br /> <br /> ETA: I just realized you were referring to my &quot;no Going Loud&quot; comment. I meant that in the sense that they can't just say &quot;F it&quot; and whip out a huge amount of power to deal with something completely unmanageable by any other means. Instability death isn't a carefully chosen moment to go down in a blaze of glory. It's the culmination of a number of bad choices and acts of desperation leading to inescapable and irreversible death. At best, it's the supernatural equivalent of strapping on a suicide vest and running toward your enemies, hoping you can get close enough to do some damage to them before they gun you down, or the homemade dynamite spontaneously explodes. *Your* demise is assured. Theirs? Not so much. So, kind of like the reverse of Going Loud (it's possible, if very difficult, to recover from it, but anyone who stands in your way when you shred your Cover is going to have a very bad day).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":1094,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","user":"Eric Zawadzki","date":". 02-23-2019, 12:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T21:29:53-08:00","id":1290998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1290996#post1290996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, they can have a superpowered meltdown if they let their Instability get far enough out of hand. But there's more to that than simply having a Mag 5 Variation or two. And while Magnitude 5 Scars are supposed to make a player think hard about whether that Magnitude 5 Variation is really worth it, they won't transform you into a giant, out-of-control blob made up of hand-shaped pseudopods in themselves.<br /> <br /> We're steering clear of crossover in the core, but we'll address Deviants made by other supernatural beings in a later supplement.</div> </div> </div> </div>understandable. if I may ask one more question, what sorta body horror are the cephalist likely to manifest?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T21:46:25-08:00","id":1291000,"title":"","content":"Cephalic: Of or relating to the head","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T22:09:32-08:00","id":1291006,"title":"","content":"well yeah. but scars are so much more than just a swollen head","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T22:12:22-08:00","id":1291008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <di