 to further mutation (to a potentially cancerous degree) and abilities commonly associated with Mutants (and fewer associated with other Clades).<br /> <br /> A Deviant's Progenitor might be able to say &quot;I was trying to produce a hybrid, but the transplant didn't take,&quot; but most conspiracies the Remade encounters aren't going to have those pages of her proprietary medical record. Instead, they will observe the Broken for telltale Clade markers - biologically expressed supernatural abilities, Clade Variations, and Adaptations - and taxonomically classify her based on that. Often, their assessments are correct, although less established conspiracies are more likely to make mistakes (or to have never encountered a member of that Clade before).</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for answering <br /> I do have a specific question. I have a specific character in mind.<br /> So,this guy's conspiracy worshipped an ancient God of storms,war and death. But such god died millennia ago.but,the conspiracy found the god's spirit and using a forbidden rite<br /> Tried to force the spirit into someone,to turn the new Deviant into a reincarnation of the God. <br /> My question is,what Clade would that be?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T09:29:38-08:00","id":1291153,"title":"","content":"I think what Eric is getting at is that a clade can be anything, no matter what transformed it.<br /> <br /> basically the guy with the storm spirit could end up mutated in body, much like a spirit claimed, or he could end up coactive, one of two worlds.<br /> <br /> EDIT: implementation is not what decides clade, the EFFECT of it does. honestly makes me happy to know that, as I had no idea what clade a born would be before other than mutant","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","user":"Primordial newcomer","date":". 02-23-2019, 12:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T09:39:10-08:00","id":1291157,"title":"","content":"That sounds Coactive to me, but again, it depends on the result. Was the transformation such that the Deviant wound up wielding powers typically attributed to that deity by drawing on his spiritual connection to the entity? Especially if many of his Variations are typical of that Clade? Coactive. If not? Possibly another Clade.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T09:56:08-08:00","id":1291164,"title":"","content":"it was mentioned the tone of deviant the renegades was simmering hate. if I remember correctly, the devoted would be getting their own supplement. do you think the tone of such a book would much more different than the renegades corebook","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T09:57:32-08:00","id":1291165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1291157#post1291157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That sounds Coactive to me, but again, it depends on the result. Was the transformation such that the Deviant wound up wielding powers typically attributed to that deity by drawing on his spiritual connection to the entity? Especially if many of his Variations are typical of that Clade? Coactive. If not? Possibly another Clade.</div> </div> </div> </div>Got it! Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T10:06:22-08:00","id":1291168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1291164#post1291164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">it was mentioned the tone of deviant the renegades was simmering hate. if I remember correctly, the devoted would be getting their own supplement. do you think the tone of such a book would much more different than the renegades corebook</div> </div> </div> </div>To be honest, I haven't had the headspace to brainstorm much for the Devoted supplement, yet. Every once in awhile I'll think of something I want for a later supplement and jot it down, but for the most part, it has been all corebook, all the time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T10:06:54-08:00","id":1291169,"title":"","content":"I have SO many questions,Y'all. I'll try to keep them minimun.<br /> So let's go; <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1094\" data-vbnamecard=\"1094\">Eric Zawadzki</a> ,if I may.<br /> 1)are there such thing as pretty Deviants? Ones remade to be seductress and tempters for instance?<br /> 2)so,Chinerics are the ones who are part-human part something else? Or did I get that wrong?<br /> 3)What is your Favorite Clade and Origin?<br /> 4)Are there mechanics For Deviants to create more Deviants?<br /> 5)Which Clade would more appropriate for a character like the Medusa? Hair made of snakes and a look that turns people in stone?<br /> 6)is time travel at all possible in this game<br /> 7)can Deviants forgive those who remade them? Is that all possible?<br /> There,7 questions. I had like,65 of them total.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24222-acopiltaczet","name":"Acopiltaczet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24222_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T11:08:53-08:00","id":1291194,"title":"","content":"So, the difference between Mutants and Chimerics is sometimes a fine one, but when outlining Deviant I had it in mind as if you can recognise where the thing comes from, it\u2019s Chimeric. A Deviant who\u2019s human except for having fur and retractable claws? chimeric, A Deviant who\u2019s Mr Tooms from the X-Files? Mutant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T11:29:50-08:00","id":1291201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1291194#post1291194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, the difference between Mutants and Chimerics is sometimes a fine one, but when outlining Deviant I had it in mind as if you can recognise where the thing comes from, it\u2019s Chimeric. A Deviant who\u2019s human except for having fur and retractable claws? chimeric, A Deviant who\u2019s Mr Tooms from the X-Files? Mutant.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you give me an example of Mutant Variations?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24222-acopiltaczet","name":"Acopiltaczet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24222_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T11:37:18-08:00","id":1291202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1291194#post1291194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, the difference between Mutants and Chimerics is sometimes a fine one, but when outlining Deviant I had it in mind as if you can recognise where the thing comes from, it\u2019s Chimeric. A Deviant who\u2019s human except for having fur and retractable claws? chimeric, A Deviant who\u2019s Mr Tooms from the X-Files? Mutant.</div> </div> </div> </div>so the mutant is alien. for example, a deviant made by the chieron group would be likely chimeric of werewolf/vampire/etc. a mutant would have stuff such as an insane height, acid spit, and perhaps more esoteric","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T12:09:02-08:00","id":1291213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acopiltaczet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1291169#post1291169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have SO many questions,Y'all. I'll try to keep them minimun.<br /> So let's go; <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1094\" data-vbnamecard=\"1094\">Eric Zawadzki</a> ,if I may.<br /> 1)are there such thing as pretty Deviants? Ones remade to be seductress and tempters for instance?<br /> 2)so,Chinerics are the ones who are part-human part something else? Or did I get that wrong?<br /> 3)What is your Favorite Clade and Origin?<br /> 4)Are there mechanics For Deviants to create more Deviants?<br /> 5)Which Clade would more appropriate for a character like the Medusa? Hair made of snakes and a look that turns people in stone?<br /> 6)is time travel at all possible in this game<br /> 7)can Deviants forgive those who remade them? Is that all possible?<br /> There,7 questions. I had like,65 of them total.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let me save some stuff for the blogs, Kickstarter preview, and final release! *laughs*<br /> <br /> 1) Not all Scars are physical. You can have a completely normal-looking Deviant, or, yes, an attractive one.<br /> <br /> 2) Dave answered this one in a bit more detail, but in summary, yes.<br /> <br /> 3) No fair asking me to pick one child as my favorite. I truly love them all!<br /> <br /> 4) Not directly, no. This isn't Vampire or Promethean where the game devotes more than a few words to the process and implications of making more of your kind. But some, rare Divergences are Transmissible.<br /> <br /> 5) Each Variation has examples of how to pair it with a Scar and Clade. I find that this makes it a lot easier to play the &quot;What Clade is X?&quot; game, but you're going to have some wiggle room.<br /> <br /> 6) Classic time travel is outside of the scope of this game, although there are definitely Variations you can reskin as jumping into alternate timelines or rewriting recent events. Deviant is so focused on the here and now, and the immediate threats of conspiracies and Instability, that I wouldn't want to hand Remade a bunch of time travel powers. That doesn't mean a *story* can't feature a time travel plot or flashbacks/flashforwards or multiple cohorts playing out interconnected stories. But Deviant isn't made for everyone to play Masters of Time, much less Time Lords.<br /> <br /> 7) The Deviant-Progenitor relationship isn't *necessarily* hostile, although that's certainly the default, especially given that the core focuses on the Renegades. Devoted are likely to have very different opinions of their Progenitors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T12:20:13-08:00","id":1291218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acopiltaczet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1291201#post1291201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Could you give me an example of Mutant Variations?</div> </div> </div> </div>Reskinning can make any Variation a Mutant Variation, but talking about specific Clade Variations, having acid/magma/liquid nitrogen for blood, which splashes out when someone cuts you, is a classic Mutant Variation. Same with the one that gives your flesh supernatural properties to anyone who eats it, temporarily granting them a Variation (even one that you yourself can't use).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T12:40:00-08:00","id":1291225,"title":"","content":"Thank you <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1094\" data-vbnamecard=\"1094\">Eric Zawadzki</a>. You rock!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24222-acopiltaczet","name":"Acopiltaczet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24222_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T13:05:29-08:00","id":1291229,"title":"","content":"another question <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1094\" data-vbnamecard=\"1094\">Eric Zawadzki</a>. many supernatural creatures have a certain strength, like vampires with being freaking tough to damage and demons being unparalleled at manipulation. what strength do deviants have as a whole have?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T13:11:28-08:00","id":1291233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1291229#post1291229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">another question <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span>. many supernatural creatures have a certain strength, like vampires with being freaking tough to damage and demons being unparalleled at manipulation. what strength do deviants have as a whole have?</div> </div> </div> </div>I know this one! Deviants are incredibly hard to suffer mind control. The same ways no one can tell a demon is lying","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24222-acopiltaczet","name":"Acopiltaczet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24222_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T13:16:18-08:00","id":1291235,"title":"","content":"oh, well unless they have something else Eric, nevermind the question. Thanks <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24222-acopiltaczet\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24222_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24222\" data-vbnamecard=\"24222\">Acopiltaczet</a>!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T13:53:04-08:00","id":1291248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acopiltaczet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1291233#post1291233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I know this one! Deviants are incredibly hard to suffer mind control. The same ways no one can tell a demon is lying</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't put it on the level of a demon's ability to lie, but they are certainly more resistant to manipulation when it would force them to act against a Touchstone. On the other hand, threatening a Loyalty Touchstone or offering an opportunity to harm a Conviction Touchstone is an easy way to manipulate them, as knowingly acting in opposition to one's Touchstones can cause the Remade to lose them.<br /> <br /> In terms of raw power (whether that's the versatility and information-gathering abilities of mages, the toughness of vampires, or the subtlety of demons), Broken are above Hunters but below other major splats. Individually, they tend to have a few neat tricks, but once an enemy is familiar with a Deviant's capabilities, the Remade has a limited capacity to surprise. Collectively, though, they are full of surprises. Even conspiracies that have studied Deviants for centuries don't have a complete catalog of Variations, and some of the ones they know of they have found extraordinarily difficult (if not impossible) to reproduce under laboratory conditions. Unfortunately for the Remade, that...does not work out in their favor. It makes them valuable tools at best and commodities at worst. Coupled with their dependence on Touchstones, which makes them particularly vulnerable to subjugation as Devoted, the Broken tend to be catnip for anyone or any organization that craves supernatural power but wants it to be under their control.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T14:22:33-08:00","id":1291254,"title":"","content":"I never even thought about taking advantage of a touchstone before, very interesting. about deviants having their souls broken, even if born in such a way. its been said they are only able to define themselves through others. how would one roleplay a Broken ones identify and sense of self?<br /> <br /> also, just how far is it needed to break a soul? the chieron group gives its agents loads of modifications and they turn better than deviants, so I'm wondering just how much worse deviants have it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T14:29:02-08:00","id":1291257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1291248#post1291248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wouldn't put it on the level of a demon's ability to lie, but they are certainly more resistant to manipulation when it would force them to act against a Touchstone. On the other hand, threatening a Loyalty Touchstone or offering an opportunity to harm a Conviction Touchstone is an easy way to manipulate them, as knowingly acting in opposition to one's Touchstones can cause the Remade to lose them.<br /> <br /> In terms of raw power (whether that's the versatility and information-gathering abilities of mages, the toughness of vampires, or the subtlety of demons), Broken are above Hunters but below other major splats. Individually, they tend to have a few neat tricks, but once an enemy is familiar with a Deviant's capabilities, the Remade has a limited capacity to surprise. Collectively, though, they are full of surprises. Even conspiracies that have studied Deviants for centuries don't have a complete catalog of Variations, and some of the ones they know of they have found extraordinarily difficult (if not impossible) to reproduce under laboratory conditions. Unfortunately for the Remade, that...does not work out in their favor. It makes them valuable tools at best and commodities at worst. Coupled with their dependence on Touchstones, which makes them particularly vulnerable to subjugation as Devoted, the Broken tend to be catnip for anyone or any organization that craves supernatural power but wants it to be under their control.</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking of powers. Is it all possible for a Deviant to learn new Variations. Like,if one can throw lightening,can he also learn to read minds?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T14:47:34-08:00","id":1291260,"title":"","content":"oh that's a good question. if they could, I assume you could say he can sense the electric impulses in the human mind enough to read it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T15:52:03-08:00","id":1291275,"title":"","content":"Deviants can develop new Variations, although more Variations means more and/or worse Scars. You'll definitely want to think about how to skin it thematically with your character concept. As wide a variety of Variations as the game offers, it's easy to turn a character into a grab bag of random powers if you don't pick new Variations with your concept in mind.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T16:00:15-08:00","id":1291277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1291275#post1291275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Deviants can develop new Variations, although more Variations means more and/or worse Scars. You'll definitely want to think about how to skin it thematically with your character concept. As wide a variety of Variations as the game offers, it's easy to turn a character into a grab bag of random powers if you don't pick new Variations with your concept in mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>Coactive question: Coactives are the ones who shared their bodies/souls/minds with other entities. Could you tell me what kind of entities are there? Like,what are they? What do they do?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24222-acopiltaczet","name":"Acopiltaczet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24222_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T16:16:28-08:00","id":1291281,"title":"","content":"I thought coactive just meant being of two worlds. like a man who drifts in and out of the spirit world<br /> <br /> EDIT: now that you mention though, I swear a symbiote clade was mentioned. could be an Z-splat though","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","user":"Primordial newcomer","date":". 02-23-2019, 07:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T16:21:50-08:00","id":1291286,"title":"","content":"I'm listening to the interview with Eric Zawadski now, and the description of Magnitudes is interesting but I'm not sure I have enough information to understand it. Will each Variation and Scar have a list of effects from Magnitude 2-15, or is it more that characters get 2-15 Magnitude to invest in Variations at the start, and each only goes from 1-5, meaning at the upper end of Magnitude characters would have to have multiple Variations?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty","name":"Minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T16:38:57-08:00","id":1291290,"title":"","content":"to add onto magnitudes, will deviants basically need to be of similar magnitude? otherwise you have deviants dealing with unequal threats from conspiracies","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T16:46:39-08:00","id":1291295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1291281#post1291281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought coactive just meant being of two worlds. like a man who drifts in and out of the spirit world<br /> <br /> EDIT: now that you mention though, I swear a symbiote clade was mentioned. could be an Z-splat though</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct on both counts. Being infused with otherworldly energy makes a Coactive. Sharing your body with another intelligence (human, alien, or otherwise) is a Symbiote.<br /> <br /> Minty: Scars and Variations are rated from 1-5. Not all of them go all the way from 1-5, although many do. Some are 1-4, 2-5, 1-3, etc. The 2-15 is the combined Magnitude of each character's Variations. So yes, multiple Variations are the norm and, in fact, a necessity above 5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T17:04:40-08:00","id":1291304,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the response! I'm actually really excited to hear that not all Variations go from 1-5 because that means that some are treated as inherently more powerful (those that start at 2+) and that the ones that are weaker or have fewer effects don't pad things out and spread their abilities thin across 5 levels. It was also really nice to hear the comparison to Memento and Phantom of the Opera, and how Loyalty Touchstones can flip to Conviction very easily. It really helped me grasp just what kind of mental state the Remade are put in by their broken existence and helps me get away from superheroes.<br /> <br /> You talked about Clade-specific Variations - are there Clade-specific Scars?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty","name":"Minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T17:24:02-08:00","id":1291318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1291295#post1291295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Correct on both counts. Being infused with otherworldly energy makes a Coactive. Sharing your body with another intelligence (human, alien, or otherwise) is a Symbiote.<br /> <br /> Minty: Scars and Variations are rated from 1-5. Not all of them go all the way from 1-5, although many do. Some are 1-4, 2-5, 1-3, etc. The 2-15 is the combined Magnitude of each character's Variations. So yes, multiple Variations are the norm and, in fact, a necessity above 5.</div> </div> </div> </div>What do Magnitude 5 Variations usually do?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T17:42:55-08:00","id":1291328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1291295#post1291295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Correct on both counts. Being infused with otherworldly energy makes a Coactive. Sharing your body with another intelligence (human, alien, or otherwise) is a Symbiote.<br /> <br /> Minty: Scars and Variations are rated from 1-5. Not all of them go all the way from 1-5, although many do. Some are 1-4, 2-5, 1-3, etc. The 2-15 is the combined Magnitude of each character's Variations. So yes, multiple Variations are the norm and, in fact, a necessity above 5.</div> </div> </div> </div>symbiotes are like the other clades, or are they specialized like bloodlines and legacies? will their be tips in the corebook to portray the otherworldly creature? If not, it shouldn't be problem","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T18:07:44-08:00","id":1291336,"title":"","content":"I believe Symbiote is one of the Forms, which I guess would be sort of like Bloodlines for Vampires. I don't think we have heard much about Forms, other than that they are supposed to allow for more fine tuning than what Clades can model, and that they will not be in the core book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty","name":"Minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T18:25:23-08:00","id":1291343,"title":"","content":"thanks for the input <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12738\" data-vbnamecard=\"12738\">Minty</a>. I'm surprised they may be in supplement (since we dont hear about Z-splat books nowadays)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T20:03:24-08:00","id":1291405,"title":"","content":"A few more questions, and then I should back off for a bit, but I promise to reveal more details soon.<br /> <br /> There aren't Clade-specific Scars.<br /> <br /> We haven't had a chance to playtest, yet, so I'm going to demure on specific Magnitude Variation effects, for now. I'd love to believe we're going to get the balance of everything perfect before playtesters see it, but I know better. Something always breaks, and it's almost never what you expect.<br /> <br /> Symbiote is a Form, which is a Z-splat similar to kiths. There will be a few in the core and likely more in later supplements. Forms are non-exclusive. You can actually have multiple Forms on the same character, so if you want to be your own Progenitor with a contagious, self-aware Divergence (requiring three different Forms), that's possible.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I'm glad to see people so excited about Deviant. I'm pretty excited about it myself, in case you haven't noticed! :-)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T20:16:01-08:00","id":1291408,"title":"","content":"so you can have many Forms, that's very interesting (and accumulating lots of scars)<br /> <br /> thanks for answering our questions, we all very much appreciate it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T20:50:08-08:00","id":1291418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1291405#post1291405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A few more questions, and then I should back off for a bit, but I promise to reveal more details soon.<br /> <br /> There aren't Clade-specific Scars.<br /> <br /> We haven't had a chance to playtest, yet, so I'm going to demure on specific Magnitude Variation effects, for now. I'd love to believe we're going to get the balance of everything perfect before playtesters see it, but I know better. Something always breaks, and it's almost never what you expect.<br /> <br /> Symbiote is a Form, which is a Z-splat similar to kiths. There will be a few in the core and likely more in later supplements. Forms are non-exclusive. You can actually have multiple Forms on the same character, so if you want to be your own Progenitor with a contagious, self-aware Divergence (requiring three different Forms), that's possible.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I'm glad to see people so excited about Deviant. I'm pretty excited about it myself, in case you haven't noticed! :-)</div> </div> </div> </div>One final question! A complex one if you don't mind. So. I'm planning to storytell my first deviant game pitting the players against against another Deviant. One of the Elect,a guy who became a Deviant by choice,and his power allows him absorb the Variations of Deviants he kills. The classic PowerStealer villain. I'd love to know,is VariationStealing at all possible?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T22:01:47-08:00","id":1291427,"title":"","content":"Do Scars also have Magnitude?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty","name":"Minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T06:13:18-08:00","id":1291512,"title":"","content":"What\u2019s a Magnitude?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T09:27:08-08:00","id":1291551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1291512#post1291512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What\u2019s a Magnitude?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the measure of a Variation's power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T09:34:18-08:00","id":1291552,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12738\" data-vbnamecard=\"12738\">Minty</a> From what I remember in the podcast Scars all have Magnitudes too and you've got to match each Variation to a Scar of an equal Magnitude and balance things out that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3776-autodefenestrate","name":"AutoDefenestrate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3776_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T13:07:00-08:00","id":1291586,"title":"","content":"Can you pool Variations under a Scar? For instance, take 1 and 2 Magnitude Variations, and then one 3 Magnitude Scar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24176-borne","name":"Borne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24176_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T13:20:53-08:00","id":1291588,"title":"","content":"Supernatural Beings (something like Kamen Rider Black) and Aliens Can Create Deviants?<br /> <br /> Is it possible for the emergence of Deviants Cults for some purpose or faith?<br /> <br /> How would classic characters in literature such as Griffyn (Invisible Man), Dr. Jekyll, and Dorian Gray be classified within the game?<br /> <br /> Can deviants arise without a sudden sharp event but by chronic exposure to edge science or the supernatural?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":641,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/641-ben-linus","user":"Ben Linus","date":". 02-24-2019, 05:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/641-ben-linus","name":"Ben Linus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T13:32:24-08:00","id":1291591,"title":"","content":"not to be rude, but deviants, not desviants. deviants can be created by other supernaturals yes. I'm fairly sure a human can slowly be turned deviant. <br /> <br /> (I'm only answering these because I think Eric is done answering questions for now)<br /> <br /> EDIT: I could see Jekyll as an elect mutant/symbiote","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T17:56:03-08:00","id":1291668,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3776-autodefenestrate\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3776_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3776\" data-vbnamecard=\"3776\">AutoDefenestrate</a> I kind of meant &quot;do Scars have scaling Magnitude refund like Variations have scaling Magnitude cost&quot; but I worded it really poorly. Thanks for answering, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty","name":"Minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-28T07:44:19-08:00","id":1292761,"title":"","content":"New preview is up! Thanks to the developer as well as Meghan and Dixie","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-28T08:56:35-08:00","id":1292780,"title":"","content":"size 10 just like that? I'm gonna love Deviant","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-28T09:18:37-08:00","id":1292786,"title":"","content":"I had to crack open my CofD book to check what size 10 actually compares to and... I still can't really tell. There's a lot of wiggle room between moose, motor boat, and sports car.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty","name":"Minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-28T09:44:14-08:00","id":1292794,"title":"","content":"I just assume it's like the hulk","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-28T10:06:22-08:00","id":1292801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1292794#post1292794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just assume it's like the hulk</div> </div> </div> </div>That's... also not a really clear example. Hulk varies from 6'5&quot; (Lou Ferrigno in green paint) to 9' tall and something over 1400 lbs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty","name":"Minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-28T10:18:08-08:00","id":1292807,"title":"","content":"well the marvel cinematics version","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-28T22:29:24-08:00","id":1292946,"title":"","content":"A few more answers before I crash tonight:<br /> <br /> Power-stealing: This has always been one of those effects that can cause a lot of problems in a game. I'm making an effort to include one, but as with all things, whether it survives depends on playtester feedback.<br /> <br /> Balancing Scars and Variations: A single Scar can &quot;support&quot; multiple Variations of lower Magnitude. However, it isn't as simple as &quot;Total Magnitude of Variations = Total Magnitude of Scars.&quot; I'm going to hold back on being more specific than that at this time, though.<br /> <br /> The core isn't going to discuss supernatural/alien beings that make Deviants or the rules for them doing so. The game's antagonists are humans, human conspiracies, and other Remade. That said, there's plenty of material and potential to work with in a future supplement. It seems ripe for a Storytellers Guide chapter.<br /> <br /> &quot;Gradual Divergence&quot; isn't addressed in the core. Not saying its impossible. In fact, I can imagine it being the equivalent of metal fatigue that affects the soul. One day, it finally cracks.<br /> <br /> Size 10 just like that (and at Magnitude 3, in the current draft). <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-28T22:38:03-08:00","id":1292947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1292946#post1292946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A few more answers before I crash tonight:<br /> <br /> Power-stealing: This has always been one of those effects that can cause a lot of problems in a game. I'm making an effort to include one, but as with all things, whether it survives depends on playtester feedback.<br /> <br /> Balancing Scars and Variations: A single Scar can &amp;quot;support&amp;quot; multiple Variations of lower Magnitude. However, it isn't as simple as &amp;quot;Total Magnitude of Variations = Total Magnitude of Scars.&amp;quot; I'm going to hold back on being more specific than that at this time, though.<br /> <br /> The core isn't going to discuss supernatural/alien beings that make Deviants or the rules for them doing so. The game's antagonists are humans, human conspiracies, and other Remade. That said, there's plenty of material and potential to work with in a future supplement. It seems ripe for a Storytellers Guide chapter.<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;Gradual Divergence&amp;quot; isn't addressed in the core. Not saying its impossible. In fact, I can imagine it being the equivalent of metal fatigue that affects the soul. One day, it finally cracks.<br /> <br /> Size 10 just like that (and at Magnitude 3, in the current draft). <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>power stealing could be great. I hope it makes it (perhaps with limits and big scar)<br /> <br /> glad to hear about balance of scars not simply be having tons of scars along with variations<br /> <br /> hmm, I really thought it was said it could happen gradually.<br /> <br /> I'm gonna love that size variation. is it ok if I ask if it was a coactive variation? It really sounds mutant, but then again I dont exactly understand what coactive is","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-28T23:43:12-08:00","id":1292953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1292946#post1292946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The core isn't going to discuss supernatural/alien beings that make Deviants or the rules for them doing so. The game's antagonists are humans, human conspiracies, and other Remade. That said, there's plenty of material and potential to work with in a future supplement. It seems ripe for a Storytellers Guide chapter.</div> </div> </div> </div>But maybe mark in <b>Deviant</b> core small frame about <i>possibility</i> of using other supernatural creatures as progenitors for Remade? Cause we will have all the 'problems' like where with Constructs not mentioned in first drafts of <b>Promethean: The Created</b> 2E. Frame in corebook solved that those options <i><u>are</u></i> in main game, they just will be presented in later source books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-01T05:17:48-08:00","id":1292989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1292947#post1292947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm gonna love that size variation. is it ok if I ask if it was a coactive variation? It really sounds mutant, but then again I dont exactly understand what coactive is</div> </div> </div> </div>Sister Laura was a Coactive. Gigantic is a Universal Variation, as are about half of all the Variations in the core.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-01T05:33:52-08:00","id":1292992,"title":"","content":"I'm getting a strong urge to run a Misfits of Science game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-01T07:31:46-08:00","id":1293020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1292946#post1292946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Size 10 just like that (and at Magnitude 3, in the current draft). <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>While being Magnitude 3 does not necessarily mean that there are two higher levels of Gigantic, the <i>possibility</i> of there being two forms BIGGER than Size 10 makes me happy","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty","name":"Minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-02T16:55:49-08:00","id":1293369,"title":"","content":"it really makes me think that while generally weaker than most templates, they have powers that definitely make them creatures to fear","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-03T13:47:28-08:00","id":1293542,"title":"","content":"Where can I find a complete rundown of Deviant's content?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7106-extant-reality","name":"Extant Reality","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7106_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-03T13:52:39-08:00","id":1293544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Extant Reality</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1293542#post1293542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where can I find a complete rundown of Deviant's content?</div> </div> </div> </div>Post 1 on page 1 of this thread got updated over the last few days to include everything found or shared on this thread and from the Onyx Path podcast last week.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-03T16:06:17-08:00","id":1293562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1293544#post1293544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Post 1 on page 1 of this thread got updated over the last few days to include everything found or shared on this thread and from the Onyx Path podcast last week.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh! Thank you, Robert D.<br /> <br /> I went over the first post of this thread and I gotta say, it's lookin' pretty good. It's got all the right pro-Genius self-transformative vibes I like and it also got a self-made Changeling vibe too. Actually that is a good character hook, some idiot finds a leftover Arcadian realm and inadvertently turns himself in a simulacrum of the Lost. Hehehe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7106,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7106-extant-reality","user":"Extant Reality","date":". 03-03-2019, 07:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7106-extant-reality","name":"Extant Reality","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7106_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-03T18:10:25-08:00","id":1293598,"title":"","content":"Eric, could you explain Coactive a little more? It\u2019s confusing especially since supernatural creators will be held off for a supplement. \u201cOf two worlds\u201d is vague, but I\u2019m interested in the idea of a character who can interact with ephemeral creatures or, maybe, travel into other worlds, such as the Shadow, Underworld, or custom realms.<br /> <br /> Does any or all of that fall under Coactive?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-03T22:11:56-08:00","id":1293662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1293598#post1293598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eric, could you explain Coactive a little more? It\u2019s confusing especially since supernatural creators will be held off for a supplement. \u201cOf two worlds\u201d is vague, but I\u2019m interested in the idea of a character who can interact with ephemeral creatures or, maybe, travel into other worlds, such as the Shadow, Underworld, or custom realms.<br /> <br /> Does any or all of that fall under Coactive?</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a Coactive Variation that lets the Deviant interact with a class of otherworldly being (spirits, fae, ghosts, etc) in various ways. Like time travel, outright world-hopping is outside of Deviant's scope. Conspiracies made up of ordinary people are not much of a threat to someone who can hole up in the Shadow, after all.<br /> <br /> Another Coactive Variation makes the Remade highly resistant to the powers of a certain class of supernatural being (vampires, mages, werewolves, etc.), and at high Magnitude, she can turn these powers against those who attempt to use them on her.<br /> <br /> Chance encounters with the supernatural can produce Coactives, but so can intentional contact with occult byproducts (the ashes of a vampire destroyed by sunlight, for example, or exposure to the energies of a Verge/Avernian Gate/Infrastructure/etc. under the right circumstances). Nor is it necessarily a form of energy that is covered by the other game lines. A meteorite that gives off a form of hitherto-unknown radiation that infuses those exposed to it in a way that gives them soul-breaking special abilities (instead of, you know, radiation sickness or cancer). In any case, the process of creating a Deviant is never clean and safe process. Conspiracies who learn the trick of it might be able to achieve an &quot;assembly line Divergence,&quot; complete with choosing the victim's initial Scars and Variations, but their methods are still crude, and more subjects die on the operating table (or soon thereafter) than become Remade. In the world of occult sciences, Progenitors are 19th century doctors trying to cure ailments with leeches and enemas, not modern day surgeons. You'll note that none of these examples involve a supernatural Progenitor. After all, why would an acclaimed brain surgeon take an interest in something as obviously fake as E.S.P.?<br /> <br /> (Caution: Mostly thinking aloud ahead, so take it with a grain of salt): Among supernatural beings who dabble in manipulating or empowering human servants/allies, creating one of the Broken is the sort of thing more likely to happen when an actually useful, stable process goes bad. Why would you want a servant with a cracked soul whose slavish devotion to you could turn into an unrelenting enmity the first time she thinks you betrayed her, when you could have a ghoul or Proximus? You wouldn't, would you? Except sometimes the Divergence produces a Deviant who is capable of something that even the Wise/Unchained/etc. didn't realize was possible and have reason to covet (or fear). He's a largely ordinary human (Scars and cracked soul aside), but he knows the sympathetic/real/true name of everyone he meets (think of the possibilities if your enemies are mages!). Or she always arrives at the moment you need her most, even if neither of you knew when that moment might be. Or he can see the future with such clarity that as long as you stick to the original plan, a prophesized event will unfold precisely as he predicted. All of these are (high-Magnitude) Coactive Variations, and all of them are the sorts of abilities that might tempt even supernatural creatures to experiment with the Divergence - like respected brain surgeons who became obsessed with studying E.S.P. after a fumble with a scalpel granted a patient telepathic powers. All Deviants have to contend with conspiracies of ordinary humans attempting to tether them in order to gain access to their powers, but Coactive Variations are much more likely to put a Remade on a collision course with one or more kinds of supernatural being (whether as an ally, a pawn, or a weapon a conspiracy wishes to use against them). The core isn't going to flesh that out much (this isn't an out-of-the-box crossover game like Hunter or Beast), but Coactive Variations lay a foundation for a chronicle that features other supernatural beings as allies, antagonists, or forces of nature. We'll address that in greater detail in a future supplement, but it's something that is already in my mind when I think about this Clade.<br /> <br /> Does that help?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-04T00:42:40-08:00","id":1293678,"title":"","content":"The human torch is coactive. Electro is coactive. the frikken Hulk is coactive<br /> <br /> <i>Buffy</i> is coactive (she\u2019s powered by demonic energy)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-04T02:24:36-08:00","id":1293684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1293662#post1293662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is a Coactive Variation that lets the Deviant interact with a class of otherworldly being (spirits, fae, ghosts, etc) in various ways. Like time travel, outright world-hopping is outside of Deviant's scope. Conspiracies made up of ordinary people are not much of a threat to someone who can hole up in the Shadow, after all.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> The core isn't going to flesh that out much (this isn't an out-of-the-box crossover game like Hunter or Beast)...</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, thank you so much. I suppose what I had really wanted to know was how much the game can support or interact with occult forces like ghosts, spirits, or magic because, while Buffy is an example Deviant, it seems the overwhelming majority of source media is more mad science than strange occult workings.<br /> <br /> So having example Variations that interact with supernatural forces or be resistant to them, and Remade that might be Broken by exposure to occult energies, or Conspiracies might up of rogue mages or whatever <i>is</i> what I was interested in. The character I began imagining is an amateur blood mage who ended up channeling rather dark powers and Broke herself, and so I'm thinking Coactive is definitely her thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-04T05:00:49-08:00","id":1293701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1293678#post1293678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The human torch is coactive. Electro is coactive. the frikken Hulk is coactive<br /> <br /> <i>Buffy</i> is coactive (she\u2019s powered by demonic energy)</div> </div> </div> </div>Most of these make sense to me, but I don't really understand why Electro is coactive. Admittedly, I don't know a lot about him, but from what I understand he's a guy who was electrocuted but instead of dying he gained the ability to store and discharge electricity. What makes him coactive over, say, a mutant?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty","name":"Minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-04T06:19:13-08:00","id":1293723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Minty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1293701#post1293701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most of these make sense to me, but I don't really understand why Electro is coactive. Admittedly, I don't know a lot about him, but from what I understand he's a guy who was electrocuted but instead of dying he gained the ability to store and discharge electricity. What makes him coactive over, say, a mutant?</div> </div> </div> </div>Possibly the player's preference for the Coactive Adaptations over Mutant ones? You could make a case for either. Did his body respond in an unusual way to electrocution (Mutant), or did the electricity in some way enter his body and never really leave (Coactive)? Recall also that Clade is decided less by genotype (what caused the Divergence) than by phenotype (what Variations and Adaptations you have). Even if the Divergence is the result of a sort of immune response to electrocution, if the Adaptations are those of a Coactive (Electrokinesis is Universal), conspiracies are going to classify him as a Coactive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-04T06:33:32-08:00","id":1293731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1293723#post1293723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Possibly the player's preference for the Coactive Adaptations over Mutant ones? You could make a case for either. Did his body respond in an unusual way to electrocution (Mutant), or did the electricity in some way enter his body and never really leave (Coactive)? Recall also that Clade is decided less by genotype (what caused the Divergence) than by phenotype (what Variations and Adaptations you have). Even if the Divergence is the result of a sort of immune response to electrocution, if the Adaptations are those of a Coactive (Electrokinesis is Universal), conspiracies are going to classify him as a Coactive.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's going to be difficult to this amount of &quot;you can do anything you want if you justify it&quot; but it's precisely that aspect of the game that drew me to the game in the first place. Thanks for the response!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty","name":"Minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-04T06:50:55-08:00","id":1293737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1293662#post1293662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There is a Coactive Variation that lets the Deviant interact with a class of otherworldly being (spirits, fae, ghosts, etc) in various ways. Like time travel, outright world-hopping is outside of Deviant's scope. Conspiracies made up of ordinary people are not much of a threat to someone who can hole up in the Shadow, after all.<br /> <br /> Another Coactive Variation makes the Remade highly resistant to the powers of a certain class of supernatural being (vampires, mages, werewolves, etc.), and at high Magnitude, she can turn these powers against those who attempt to use them on her.<br /> <br /> Chance encounters with the supernatural can produce Coactives, but so can intentional contact with occult byproducts (the ashes of a vampire destroyed by sunlight, for example, or exposure to the energies of a Verge/Avernian Gate/Infrastructure/etc. under the right circumstances). Nor is it necessarily a form of energy that is covered by the other game lines. A meteorite that gives off a form of hitherto-unknown radiation that infuses those exposed to it in a way that gives them soul-breaking special abilities (instead of, you know, radiation sickness or cancer). In any case, the process of creating a Deviant is never clean and safe process. Conspiracies who learn the trick of it might be able to achieve an &amp;quot;assembly line Divergence,&amp;quot; complete with choosing the victim's initial Scars and Variations, but their methods are still crude, and more subjects die on the operating table (or soon thereafter) than become Remade. In the world of occult sciences, Progenitors are 19th century doctors trying to cure ailments with leeches and enemas, not modern day surgeons. You'll note that none of these examples involve a supernatural Progenitor. After all, why would an acclaimed brain surgeon take an interest in something as obviously fake as E.S.P.?<br /> <br /> (Caution: Mostly thinking aloud ahead, so take it with a grain of salt): Among supernatural beings who dabble in manipulating or empowering human servants/allies, creating one of the Broken is the sort of thing more likely to happen when an actually useful, stable process goes bad. Why would you want a servant with a cracked soul whose slavish devotion to you could turn into an unrelenting enmity the first time she thinks you betrayed her, when you could have a ghoul or Proximus? You wouldn't, would you? Except sometimes the Divergence produces a Deviant who is capable of something that even the Wise/Unchained/etc. didn't realize was possible and have reason to covet (or fear). He's a largely ordinary human (Scars and cracked soul aside), but he knows the sympathetic/real/true name of everyone he meets (think of the possibilities if your enemies are mages!). Or she always arrives at the moment you need her most, even if neither of you knew when that moment might be. Or he can see the future with such clarity that as long as you stick to the original plan, a prophesized event will unfold precisely as he predicted. All of these are (high-Magnitude) Coactive Variations, and all of them are the sorts of abilities that might tempt even supernatural creatures to experiment with the Divergence - like respected brain surgeons who became obsessed with studying E.S.P. after a fumble with a scalpel granted a patient telepathic powers. All Deviants have to contend with conspiracies of ordinary humans attempting to tether them in order to gain access to their powers, but Coactive Variations are much more likely to put a Remade on a collision course with one or more kinds of supernatural being (whether as an ally, a pawn, or a weapon a conspiracy wishes to use against them). The core isn't going to flesh that out much (this isn't an out-of-the-box crossover game like Hunter or Beast), but Coactive Variations lay a foundation for a chronicle that features other supernatural beings as allies, antagonists, or forces of nature. We'll address that in greater detail in a future supplement, but it's something that is already in my mind when I think about this Clade.<br /> <br /> Does that help?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmmmmm,that makes me wonder about another Clade. The Cephalist.<br /> What makes a Cephalist a part of this particular Clade? Like,do all Deviants with psychic abilities are Cephalists? Do they need to be able to read minds? What is the detail that make a conspiracy say &quot;that's a cephalist&quot; after studying a Remade?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-04T08:04:46-08:00","id":1293752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1293662#post1293662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Conspiracies made up of ordinary people are not much of a threat to someone who can hole up in the Shadow, after all.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Changelings can hop into the Hedge in any moment or place. They rarely do without serious consideration even when hiding or running from a threat, because there is no way to know <b><i>what </i></b>may be awaiting for them in the other side. <br /> The Shadow isn\u00b4t any nicer, specially to a weird freak who has no business there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2411,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","user":"Raistlin","date":". 03-04-2019, 12:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-04T09:17:23-08:00","id":1293787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1293737#post1293737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmmmmmm,that makes me wonder about another Clade. The Cephalist.<br /> What makes a Cephalist a part of this particular Clade? Like,do all Deviants with psychic abilities are Cephalists? Do they need to be able to read minds? What is the detail that make a conspiracy say &quot;that's a cephalist&quot; after studying a Remade?</div> </div> </div> </div>It sounds like the answer to &quot;what makes a Clade X&quot; is having Clade X's Variations and &quot;Adaptations&quot;, though we haven't really heard about what Adaptations are. My assumption is that they are some kind of innate powers that members of a Clade have access to, possibly ways of handling Instability.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty","name":"Minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-04T09:20:04-08:00","id":1293790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Minty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1293787#post1293787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It sounds like the answer to &amp;quot;what makes a Clade X&amp;quot; is having Clade X's Variations and &amp;quot;Adaptations&amp;quot;, though we haven't really heard about what Adaptations are. My assumption is that they are some kind of innate powers that members of a Clade have access to, possibly ways of handling Instability.</div> </div> </div> </div>That makes a lot of sense","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-04T11:04:09-08:00","id":1293829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1293752#post1293752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Shadow isn\u00b4t any nicer, specially to a weird freak who has no business there.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Shadow is also a <i>very different set of problems</i> to the ones life in the material world on its own represents. It doesn't matter that a Jaggling might eventually eat you or hobgoblin deals might eventually fuck you up when the momentary issue you came in from can be briefly resolved by straight-up <i>vanishing</i>.<br /> <br /> &quot;This supernatural character can enter a fully fleshed-out different dimension without needing to engage with a rolodex of esoteric and individualized rituals&quot; is generally limited to monsters with constant collective cause for business with a given otherworld for a reason.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-05T15:12:56-08:00","id":1294185,"title":"","content":"All of this talk about &quot;Clades&quot; and Variants reminds me of the Orion's Arm community.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7106-extant-reality","name":"Extant Reality","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7106_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T11:32:23-08:00","id":1294462,"title":"","content":"Deviants are considered Kin in the classification of Beasts? Or is it impossible to have Family Ties with them (as with demons)?<br /> <br /> Is it possible deviants to be conspirators (I am not talking about making other deviants, but about forming an organization of their own, unlike the purposes that created them, with some sinister purpose they think correct)?<br /> <br /> And that's my main question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/641-ben-linus","name":"Ben Linus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T12:02:48-08:00","id":1294467,"title":"","content":"Deviants are Kin to Beasts, Deviants who are conspirators are called the Devoted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T12:26:31-08:00","id":1294475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1294467#post1294467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Deviants who are conspirators are called the Devoted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not quite. Devoted are Deviants who still work for or with their creators. A sinister group of Deviants would just be an evil Cohort.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24176-borne","name":"Borne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24176_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T12:43:47-08:00","id":1294481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Borne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1294475#post1294475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not quite. Devoted are Deviants who still work for or with their creators. A sinister group of Deviants would just be an evil Cohort.</div> </div> </div> </div>A person who works for conspirators may, in fact, equally be called a conspirator. The Devoted are part of the conspiracies that made them, ergo.<br /> <br /> Think things through.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T12:58:08-08:00","id":1294485,"title":"","content":"From the initial question, emphasis mine.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ben Linus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1294462#post1294462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it possible deviants to be conspirators (<b>I am not talking about making other deviants</b>, but about forming an organization of their own, <b>unlike the purposes that created them</b>, with some sinister purpose.</div> </div> </div> </div>If they are not part of the Conspiracy that created them, they are not conspirators. Therefore, they would not necessarily qualify as Devoted. Your argument does not follow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24176-borne","name":"Borne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24176_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T13:26:53-08:00","id":1294496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1294467#post1294467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Deviants are Kin to Beasts, Deviants who are conspirators are called the Devoted.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've always been kind of hazy on what makes something Kin or not, why are Deviants Kin? Is it just because they are &quot;supernatural&quot; but not Demons?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty","name":"Minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T13:28:53-08:00","id":1294497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Minty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1294496#post1294496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've always been kind of hazy on what makes something Kin or not, why are Deviants Kin? Is it just because they are &quot;supernatural&quot; but not Demons?</div> </div> </div> </div>All supernatural beings are Kin unless something makes them an exception. There's no reason for deviants to be an exception. (Not that the reason for demons being an exception is particularly well explained, imo.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T13:44:14-08:00","id":1294502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1294497#post1294497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> All supernatural beings are Kin unless something makes them an exception. There's no reason for deviants to be an exception. (Not that the reason for demons being an exception is particularly well explained, imo.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, at first I thought Demons are not Kin because they were never human to begin with, but Prometheans are Kin, so that doesn't really work. I thought Deviants might not be Kin because they are all kind of one-offs and don't have any unifying force or patron that can be derived from the Dark Mother, but I really don't understand the concept very well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty","name":"Minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T13:44:17-08:00","id":1294503,"title":"","content":"I Wonder if I can build a high powered deviant using a Infernal Exalted as inspiration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T13:55:51-08:00","id":1294504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1294497#post1294497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> All supernatural beings are Kin unless something makes them an exception. There's no reason for deviants to be an exception. (Not that the reason for demons being an exception is particularly well explained, imo.)</div> </div> </div> </div>demons aren't kin because they are utterly alien. they are bio-mechanical things with no connection to humanity, something that every other template has. you could argue for prometheans, but they are part of the divine fire, a force that effects humans into making monsters that also supernaturally horrify people (similar to the hero phenomena). changelings are kin because despite also being created, they do represent humanity and its dreams.<br /> <br /> I wouldnt be surprised if abysmal creatures were not kin either. they are, afterall, divorced from humanity<br /> <br /> EDT: I wouldn't be surprised if deviants were so varied some cant be kin (like a stigmatic like deviant). if all deviants are considered kin, it could be that the force of their agony is so horrible it effects the primordial dream. or the soul breaking is (to beasts) similar to the devouring<br /> <br /> FINAL EDIT: I think the real reason demons cant be kin is simply because they are completely alien. every other supernatural is tied to the chronicles of darkness in a supernatural but cohesive way. everyone except demons and their mythology of it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","user":"Primordial newcomer","date":". 03-06-2019, 05:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T17:24:49-08:00","id":1294543,"title":"","content":"I think I'll leave the Kin question to a Beast developer.<br /> <br /> As to the definition of Devoted, however, I wanted to clarify that Devoted are Deviants who serve a conspiracy, not necessarily the one that created them. Some conspiracies have Devoted who rise high in their ranks. Others relegate Remade to supporting roles. Most actively recruit Broken, partially because it's a whole lot easier than initiating new Divergences. We'll cover Devoted in much more detail in a later supplement, but that's sort of the executive summary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T17:33:15-08:00","id":1294546,"title":"","content":"will the supplement also explain why loyalty and conviction switch places when it comes to renegade and devoted","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T05:08:08-08:00","id":1294679,"title":"","content":"What's the main difference between Chimeric Variations and Mutant Variations? I see the flavor differences, but how are they mechanically distinct? They seem like the two closest Clades to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24176-borne","name":"Borne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24176_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T12:00:07-08:00","id":1294812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Borne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1294679#post1294679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's the main difference between Chimeric Variations and Mutant Variations? I see the flavor differences, but how are they mechanically distinct? They seem like the two closest Clades to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mutant Variations are great if you want alien biology (whether that means you don't bleed or that you bleed acid). Chimeric Variations are about blending in or being a blend of two creatures - avoiding traps and trackers, concealing their Deviant nature, blending in socially with any species or clique, and shapeshifting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T12:12:11-08:00","id":1294817,"title":"","content":"so chimerics are the social splat? able to to go espionage with other supernaturals? and mutants are sorta the ones filled with surprises.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T12:55:31-08:00","id":1294843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1294817#post1294817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">so chimerics are the social splat? able to to go espionage with other supernaturals? and mutants are sorta the ones filled with surprises.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Social splat&quot; might be too strong a word (Remade really are *highly* variable, even within the same Clade), but you know the trope of the hunters hunting the monster that is hunting them back (raptors, Ghost in the Darkness, that one early X-Files episode with the invisible creature in the woods)? Tracking a Hybrid with a lot of Chimeric Variations is a bit like that. They could turn up anywhere. You might walk right past them and not realize it, or think you have them pinned, and then they turn a corner and are just gone, leaving you alone with an alley cat.<br /> <br /> Mutants are indeed full of surprises. You can study one for months, monitoring her via a network of tracking devices, but when you try to capture her, she will still pull some new trick out of nowhere. If Chimerics are known for slipping the proverbial net, Mutants are known for tearing free of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T13:06:18-08:00","id":1294848,"title":"","content":"that's very interesting, so chimerics are sorta the most &quot;monsters among us&quot;, while mutants are full of &quot;it did WHAT&quot;. final question for today, are deviants ever considered successes, or are they universally considered useful but failed experiments","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T13:17:19-08:00","id":1294855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1294848#post1294848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">that's very interesting, so chimerics are sorta the most &quot;monsters among us&quot;, while mutants are full of &quot;it did WHAT&quot;. final question for today, are deviants ever considered successes, or are they universally considered useful but failed experiments</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh they're absolutely considered successes a good deal of the time! Sure, you have your accidents and catastrophes, but producing Remade is the *goal* of most Progenitors. Some conspiracies have gotten pretty good at causing the Divergence (albeit not without some fatalities) and can even exercise some control over the Variations and Scars a subject is likely to manifest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T13:37:12-08:00","id":1294865,"title":"","content":"How much do Progenitors and/or Conspiracies typically know about the, for lack of a better term, metaphysics of Divergence? It doesn't sound to me like it works the way the Divine Fire compels people to make Prometheans, but at some point someone has to figure out that they need to &quot;crack the soul&quot; of someone to force Divergence, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty","name":"Minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T14:09:54-08:00","id":1294879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1294855#post1294855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh they're absolutely considered successes a good deal of the time! Sure, you have your accidents and catastrophes, but producing Remade is the *goal* of most Progenitors. Some conspiracies have gotten pretty good at causing the Divergence (albeit not without some fatalities) and can even exercise some control over the Variations and Scars a subject is likely to manifest.</div> </div> </div> </div>oh ok. well that's cool to hear, so real progress has been made on the making of deviants (and now that I think of it, scars are a good source of keeping them on a leash).<br /> <br /> as it turns out, I have time to type one more question. what's the defining aspect of the Accidents","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T22:12:43-08:00","id":1294972,"title":"","content":"Two clades that were quoted at the beginning and did not see in the last interviews talking are the Cyborgs and Amalgrams. Have they been in another clade, been suppressed or will they still be in the game?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/641-ben-linus","name":"Ben Linus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T01:59:35-08:00","id":1294997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ben Linus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1294972#post1294972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Two clades that were quoted at the beginning and did not see in the last interviews talking are the Cyborgs and Amalgrams. Have they been in another clade, been suppressed or will they still be in the game?</div> </div> </div> </div>If memory serves, Amalgams will be Forms (Z-splat like Kiths or Lodges or Bloodlines) rather than Clades. the Invasive clade would be the closest to cyborgs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T02:09:39-08:00","id":1294998,"title":"","content":"&quot;Cyborg&quot; is the Invasive Clade's nickname.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T05:52:08-08:00","id":1295025,"title":"","content":"Besides cyborgs, what kind of characters does the Invasive Clade actually cover? Similarly, besides psychics, what kinds of characters would be Cephalists?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty","name":"Minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T06:14:57-08:00","id":1295030,"title":"","content":"it was mentioned earlier by Eric that it could also be stuff like relics put into you. other than that I can only guess it also covers stuff like experimental parasites and such (and that could end up just being chimeric and more)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T10:30:18-08:00","id":1295078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Minty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1295025#post1295025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Besides cyborgs, what kind of characters does the Invasive Clade actually cover?</div> </div> </div> </div>Essentially, any Deviant who finds themselves empowered by an inanimate object that is now permanently part of their body. This is basically the Clade for non-living implants and prosthetics. Or those people with mystical/alien/super-science artifacts that're now permanently attached. Or someone stuck in a supersuit/armor that's fused to them. Or...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T13:07:20-08:00","id":1295114,"title":"","content":"Chimerics sound heavily influenced by Dark Angel, which is great to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T19:18:17-08:00","id":1295177,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1094\" data-vbnamecard=\"1094\">Eric Zawadzki</a>, is the z-splat side of things fleshed out as far as clades are or are they still subject to big changes","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T19:20:51-08:00","id":1295179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Minty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1294865#post1294865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How much do Progenitors and/or Conspiracies typically know about the, for lack of a better term, metaphysics of Divergence? It doesn't sound to me like it works the way the Divine Fire compels people to make Prometheans, but at some point someone has to figure out that they need to &quot;crack the soul&quot; of someone to force Divergence, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's going to vary a *lot* from conspiracy to conspiracy. Also, the cracking soul is a bit of a chicken-and-egg question. Does the power tapped by a successful Divergence crack the soul, or does the cracking of the soul allow the Remade to tap the power of the Divergence? Also, a soul can crack without a successful Divergence, and what cracks one victim's soul may not crack another's, so there are other variables beyond that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1294879#post1294879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's the defining aspect of the Accidents</div> </div> </div> </div>Not entirely sure what you mean, I'm afraid. Accidents are those whose Divergence was the result of chance, rather than something intentional. An Origin has two effects - whether the Remade gets an extra Loyalty or an extra Conviction, and whether they receive a Scar-free Magnitude of a Subtle Variation or an Overt Variation. Accidents are weird among the Origins in that they don't get any bonus Loyalty/Conviction but start with two Scar-free Magnitude of Variations (leaving a couple details out, here, but that's the short version).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1295177#post1295177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1094\" data-vbnamecard=\"1094\">Eric Zawadzki</a>, is the z-splat side of things fleshed out as far as clades are or are they still subject to big changes</div> </div> </div> </div>Z-Splats are pretty fleshed out. We have just a handful in the core. As with most of the character creation side of the game's mechanics, Forms are designed to add more modularity to the game. We want players to be able to model a lot of different character concepts under the very large tent of &quot;people on the lam from the ones who did something terrible to them.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":1094,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","user":"Eric Zawadzki","date":".  Answering another question 03-08-2019, 10:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T20:22:27-08:00","id":1295199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1295179#post1295179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An Origin has two effects - whether the Remade gets an extra Loyalty or an extra Conviction, and whether they receive a Scar-free Magnitude of a Subtle Variation or an Overt Variation. Accidents are weird among the Origins in that they don't get any bonus Loyalty/Conviction but start with two Scar-free Magnitude of Variations (leaving a couple details out, here, but that's the short version).</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that gives us a pretty solid guess at how the Elect and the Unwilling shake out and a question mark the size of the Empire State Building about the Born, filtering the Origins blog post through this information. Does the described variety of attitudes Genotypal Remade hold toward their Conspiracies reflect the Origin's mechanics?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T21:13:47-08:00","id":1295207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1295199#post1295199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, that gives us a pretty solid guess at how the Elect and the Unwilling shake out and a question mark the size of the Empire State Building about the Born, filtering the Origins blog post through this information. Does the described variety of attitudes Genotypal Remade hold toward their Conspiracies reflect the Origin's mechanics?</div> </div> </div> </div>Born: +1 Subtle; +1 Conviction","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T21:31:59-08:00","id":1295208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1295207#post1295207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Born: +1 Subtle; +1 Conviction</div> </div> </div> </div>Had a feeling, but wasn't sure if making my guess based off of symmetry/process of elimination was the right line of thinking. Thanks for the confirmation!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-09T01:59:47-08:00","id":1295265,"title":"","content":"Eric, if you don't mind answering, what are some things a Renegade might hold as a Conviction if not a Conspiracy? I guess I'm wondering if, for example, Buffy's Conviction was geared towards vampire hunting rather than fighting the Watchers?<br /> <br /> Also, is it plausible that a Renegade hunted by Conspiracy A could team up with a Devoted of Conspiracy B to fight Conspiracy A?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-09T07:52:21-08:00","id":1295313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1295179#post1295179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's going to vary a *lot* from conspiracy to conspiracy. Also, the cracking soul is a bit of a chicken-and-egg question. Does the power tapped by a successful Divergence crack the soul, or does the cracking of the soul allow the Remade to tap the power of the Divergence? Also, a soul can crack without a successful Divergence, and what cracks one victim's soul may not crack another's, so there are other variables beyond that.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Not entirely sure what you mean, I'm afraid. Accidents are those whose Divergence was the result of chance, rather than something intentional. An Origin has two effects - whether the Remade gets an extra Loyalty or an extra Conviction, and whether they receive a Scar-free Magnitude of a Subtle Variation or an Overt Variation. Accidents are weird among the Origins in that they don't get any bonus Loyalty/Conviction but start with two Scar-free Magnitude of Variations (leaving a couple details out, here, but that's the short version).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Z-Splats are pretty fleshed out. We have just a handful in the core. As with most of the character creation side of the game's mechanics, Forms are designed to add more modularity to the game. We want players to be able to model a lot of different character concepts under the very large tent of &amp;quot;people on the lam from the ones who did something terrible to them.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>on the latter for accidents, that's exactly what I meant. sorry I wasn't direct about it.<br /> <br /> as for the Z-splats, that's great to hear. are any of them homages to things like the invisible man and dr Jekyll and Mr hyde (and were either of those books inspirations for deviant?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-09T08:11:48-08:00","id":1295316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1295265#post1295265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eric, if you don't mind answering, what are some things a Renegade might hold as a Conviction if not a Conspiracy? I guess I'm wondering if, for example, Buffy's Conviction was geared towards vampire hunting rather than fighting the Watchers?<br /> <br /> Also, is it plausible that a Renegade hunted by Conspiracy A could team up with a Devoted of Conspiracy B to fight Conspiracy A?</div> </div> </div> </div>Conspirators are the most common Conviction Touchstones among Renegades, but Remade can find plenty of other objects for their rage. It need not even be anyone associated with the Divergence. It can be the dirty cop who has been shaking down the Broken's neighborhood, or the asshole ex who has been stalking the Deviant's Loyalty Touchstone, or that bully from high school who *really* needs to get what he deserves, or those fools at the university who laughed at his outlandish theories. If the Storyteller wants to bring in antagonists from other gamelines (or just monsters of the week), these can also become Conviction Touchstones. So, there is a wide range of options available, which should make it easy to fine-tune the game's vengeance stories - from heroic (if violent) vigilantes, to angry victims of circumstance fighting back (the default), to really freaking dark anti-heroes (or outright antagonists, in a non-Deviant chronicle).<br /> <br /> Team-ups are also perfectly plausible, in cases where Devoted and Renegades have a mutual enemy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-09T09:05:14-08:00","id":1295325,"title":"","content":"If question slots are still open, I wanted to ask about Eugene Tooms from X-files. He's been cited as part of the mission statement, but his activities seem to be based on hunting and hibernating, rather than vengeance or protectiveness. How do his Virtues and Stability look like mechanics-wise?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-09T09:54:03-08:00","id":1295334,"title":"","content":"Dear <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1094\" data-vbnamecard=\"1094\">Eric Zawadzki</a> . I'd love to know,does the corebook gives examples on how to create youw own Forms and Variations in the case the ones in the book doesn't fit my character concept?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-09T10:01:05-08:00","id":1295336,"title":"","content":"I have created a account just to ask deviant questions. i have 4,so far<ul><li>Since we know the 5 clades,and one form,could you tell me more about forms,maybe reveal some more?</li> <li>Are magical weapons present in deviant? like &quot;this remade can create a mystical axe,and this one is a incarnation of death itself,so he has a scythe&quot;?</li> <li>Can Chimerics have symbolic traits associated with animals istead of physical traits,&quot;this deviant doesn' has te claws of a lion,but is brave like a lion. Another Deviant has the sttubornnes of a elephant&quot;?</li> <li>Could you give more examples of invasive variations?</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25119-willofthed","name":"WillOfTheD","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-09T12:30:45-08:00","id":1295371,"title":"","content":"RE Tooms: Dave uses Tooms to illustrate the difference between Chimeric Variations and Mutant Variations. In short, if you explain your body-stretching powers as coming from having your DNA spliced with that of an octopus, you're a Chimeric. If you just have the ability to stretch and squeeze your body in impossible ways because that's what your body can do, you're a Mutant. A Deviant of any Clade can have the Boneless Variation, but how that looks will be very different from Clade to Clade (or even from Deviant to Deviant of the same Clade).<br /> <br /> RE Custom Variations/Forms Rules: Rules for building your own Variations/Forms is outside of the scope of the core. We'll address it in a later supplement (either as a stretch goal or as part of the Deviant Players Guide). That said, you'll find a *lot* of options in the core. Part of that is some effects that fall under separate powers in other gamelines are collapsed into a handful that you can reskin to fit your character concept. For example, Lash covers all your damaging ranged (Athletics/Firearms) attacks, and Natural Weapon covers all your hand-to-hand (Brawl/Weaponry) attacks. A Natural Weapon can be the usual claws/fangs/horns, but it can also be the fiery sword you summon when battle is joined.<br /> <br /> RE Forms: I had thought Dave spoiled these awhile ago, but the Forms in the core are Amalgam (two or more minds in one body), Self-Made (sometimes you have only yourself to blame), Symbiote (your powers have a mind of their own, and you have to bargain with them), Transmissible (your Divergence is contagious), and Devoted (have Loyalty/Conviction flipped).<br /> <br /> RE Magical Weapons: See my previous answer. Granted, if your Natural Weapon manifests as a weapon like and axe or scythe, you're not going to be able to just hand it off to someone to borrow (although a clever reskinning of Sacred Flesh might allow you to justify doing so on a temporary basis).<br /> <br /> RE Symbolic Chimerics: There's nothing saying you couldn't go this route.<br /> <br /> RE Invasive Variations: Invasive Variations tend to make them Swiss army knives - floating Merit dots, floating Skill ratings (what do I need to have 3 dots in right now?&quot;), sensory abilities that they can re-calibrate to observe different phenomena, and hidden compartments with all kinds of useful items.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-09T12:58:23-08:00","id":1295376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1295371#post1295371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">RE Tooms: Dave uses Tooms to illustrate the difference between Chimeric Variations and Mutant Variations. In short, if you explain your body-stretching powers as coming from having your DNA spliced with that of an octopus, you're a Chimeric. If you just have the ability to stretch and squeeze your body in impossible ways because that's what your body can do, you're a Mutant. A Deviant of any Clade can have the Boneless Variation, but how that looks will be very different from Clade to Clade (or even from Deviant to Deviant of the same Clade).<br /> <br /> RE Custom Variations/Forms Rules: Rules for building your own Variations/Forms is outside of the scope of the core. We'll address it in a later supplement (either as a stretch goal or as part of the Deviant Players Guide). That said, you'll find a *lot* of options in the core. Part of that is some effects that fall under separate powers in other gamelines are collapsed into a handful that you can reskin to fit your character concept. For example, Lash covers all your damaging ranged (Athletics/Firearms) attacks, and Natural Weapon covers all your hand-to-hand (Brawl/Weaponry) attacks. A Natural Weapon can be the usual claws/fangs/horns, but it can also be the fiery sword you summon when battle is joined.<br /> <br /> RE Forms: I had thought Dave spoiled these awhile ago, but the Forms in the core are Amalgam (two or more minds in one body), Self-Made (sometimes you have only yourself to blame), Symbiote (your powers have a mind of their own, and you have to bargain with them), Transmissible (your Divergence is contagious), and Devoted (have Loyalty/Conviction flipped).<br /> <br /> RE Magical Weapons: See my previous answer. Granted, if your Natural Weapon manifests as a weapon like and axe or scythe, you're not going to be able to just hand it off to someone to borrow (although a clever reskinning of Sacred Flesh might allow you to justify doing so on a temporary basis).<br /> <br /> RE Symbolic Chimerics: There's nothing saying you couldn't go this route.<br /> <br /> RE Invasive Variations: Invasive Variations tend to make them Swiss army knives - floating Merit dots, floating Skill ratings (what do I need to have 3 dots in right now?&amp;quot<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />, sensory abilities that they can re-calibrate to observe different phenomena, and hidden compartments with all kinds of useful items.</div> </div> </div> </div>on forms, what separates the elect from being Self Made? it seems like it would fairly common they would have that form. amalgams remind me of Jekyll and Mr hyde, symbiotes Venom, and if self made basically means &quot;no one convinced you, you didnt go crazy, it's just you&quot; I think the invisible man (easily a villainous renegade deviant)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-09T13:17:43-08:00","id":1295378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1295376#post1295376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> on forms, what separates the elect from being Self Made? it seems like it would fairly common they would have that form. amalgams remind me of Jekyll and Mr hyde, symbiotes Venom, and if self made basically means &quot;no one convinced you, you didnt go crazy, it's just you&quot; I think the invisible man (easily a villainous renegade deviant)</div> </div> </div> </div>Captain America is Elect (but not Self-Made). The Hulk is Self-Made Accidental. Dr. Jekyll is Self-Made Amalgam Elect. Dr. Schreber from Dark City is Self-Made Unwilling (thought that combination was impossible, didn't you? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-09T13:25:25-08:00","id":1295380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1295378#post1295378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Captain America is Elect (but not Self-Made). The Hulk is Self-Made Accidental. Dr. Jekyll is Self-Made Amalgam Elect. Dr. Schreber from Dark City is Self-Made Unwilling (thought that combination was impossible, didn't you? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />).</div> </div> </div> </div>on that last part, I didnt think it possible at all. you have impressed me. i think i understand now. the Elect are simply people who wanted to be changed (unlike volunteers who didnt really understand what they were signing if for), self made is where you yourself did the work. I'm guessing Vaptain america could also be a Devoted (and also, devoted being a form technically makes renegades a form correct? unless renegade is thought to be the &quot;default&quot; mindset the Broken have)<br /> <br /> EDIT: would Eddie brock/Venom actually be amalgram symbiote? considering it's also it's own mind?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","user":"Primordial newcomer","date":". 03-09-2019, 04:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-09T13:34:09-08:00","id":1295381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1295371#post1295371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">RE Tooms: Dave uses Tooms to illustrate the difference between Chimeric Variations and Mutant Variations. In short, if you explain your body-stretching powers as coming from having your DNA spliced with that of an octopus, you're a Chimeric. If you just have the ability to stretch and squeeze your body in impossible ways because that's what your body can do, you're a Mutant. A Deviant of any Clade can have the Boneless Variation, but how that looks will be very different from Clade to Clade (or even from Deviant to Deviant of the same Clade).<br /> <br /> RE Custom Variations/Forms Rules: Rules for building your own Variations/Forms is outside of the scope of the core. We'll address it in a later supplement (either as a stretch goal or as part of the Deviant Players Guide). That said, you'll find a *lot* of options in the core. Part of that is some effects that fall under separate powers in other gamelines are collapsed into a handful that you can reskin to fit your character concept. For example, Lash covers all your damaging ranged (Athletics/Firearms) attacks, and Natural Weapon covers all your hand-to-hand (Brawl/Weaponry) attacks. A Natural Weapon can be the usual claws/fangs/horns, but it can also be the fiery sword you summon when battle is joined.<br /> <br /> RE Forms: I had thought Dave spoiled these awhile ago, but the Forms in the core are Amalgam (two or more minds in one body), Self-Made (sometimes you have only yourself to blame), Symbiote (your powers have a mind of their own, and you have to bargain with them), Transmissible (your Divergence is contagious), and Devoted (have Loyalty/Conviction flipped).<br /> <br /> RE Magical Weapons: See my previous answer. Granted, if your Natural Weapon manifests as a weapon like and axe or scythe, you're not going to be able to just hand it off to someone to borrow (although a clever reskinning of Sacred Flesh might allow you to justify doing so on a temporary basis).<br /> <br /> RE Symbolic Chimerics: There's nothing saying you couldn't go this route.<br /> <br /> RE Invasive Variations: Invasive Variations tend to make them Swiss army knives - floating Merit dots, floating Skill ratings (what do I need to have 3 dots in right now?&amp;quot<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />, sensory abilities that they can re-calibrate to observe different phenomena, and hidden compartments with all kinds of useful items.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sacred Flesh sounds really really awesome,what does it do?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-09T13:49:57-08:00","id":1295385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1295380#post1295380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">on that last part, I didnt think it possible at all. you have impressed me. i think i understand now. the Elect are simply people who wanted to be changed (unlike volunteers who didnt really understand what they were signing if for), self made is where you yourself did the work. I'm guessing Vaptain america could also be a Devoted (and also, devoted being a form technically makes renegades a form correct? unless renegade is thought to be the &quot;default&quot; mindset the Broken have)</div> </div> </div> </div>You've got it. And yeah, Cap would be Devoted, as well. Granted, we've got to be a little bit careful about slotting superheroes as Deviants (MCU Captain America is decidedly lacking in Scars, for example), but they make for easily accessible examples. Renegade is the game's default, so there isn't a Renegade Form as an opposite to Devoted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-09T14:04:38-08:00","id":1295388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1295385#post1295385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You've got it. And yeah, Cap would be Devoted, as well. Granted, we've got to be a little bit careful about slotting superheroes as Deviants (MCU Captain America is decidedly lacking in Scars, for example), but they make for easily accessible examples. Renegade is the game's default, so there isn't a Renegade Form as an opposite to Devoted.</div> </div> </div> </div>great! and that makes sense for superheroes when you have ones like cap and spiderman. I understand on the renegade not being considered a form<br /> <br /> from the sounds of it, forms are really for providing more narrative and individualism to a story. will every form also have mechanical advantages and disadvantages","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-09T14:29:56-08:00","id":1295391,"title":"","content":"- Will we have variations that will deal with immortality or longevity?<br /> <br /> - Can scars include the need to steal body parts to maintain their shape?<br /> <br /> &quot;Do we have something that simulates a collective mind of a small-scale Borg queen?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;How would the Invisible Man and Dorian Gray be classified?&quot; Did your books influence the game?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/641-ben-linus","name":"Ben Linus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-09T15:07:33-08:00","id":1295399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ben Linus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1295391#post1295391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Will we have variations that will deal with immortality or longevity?<br /> <br /> - Can scars include the need to steal body parts to maintain their shape?</div> </div> </div> </div>- Achievable with Anomalous Biology 1.<br /> <br /> - The Dependency Scar has you covered. Take Maintenance, too, if you want there to be a chance of your stolen flesh getting infected.<br /> <br /> With that, I should probably return to actually working on the game, since I now have the second draft I needed to finish the second draft of one of my sections. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-09T15:22:24-08:00","id":1295405,"title":"","content":"good luck on your work!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-09T16:24:15-08:00","id":1295410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1295316#post1295316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Conspirators are the most common Conviction Touchstones among Renegades, but Remade can find plenty of other objects for their rage. It need not even be anyone associated with the Divergence. It can be the dirty cop who has been shaking down the Broken's neighborhood, or the asshole ex who has been stalking the Deviant's Loyalty Touchstone, or that bully from high school who *really* needs to get what he deserves, or those fools at the university who laughed at his outlandish theories. If the Storyteller wants to bring in antagonists from other gamelines (or just monsters of the week), these can also become Conviction Touchstones. So, there is a wide range of options available, which should make it easy to fine-tune the game's vengeance stories - from heroic (if violent) vigilantes, to angry victims of circumstance fighting back (the default), to really freaking dark anti-heroes (or outright antagonists, in a non-Deviant chronicle).<br /> <br /> Team-ups are also perfectly plausible, in cases where Devoted and Renegades have a mutual enemy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool, man. Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-09T21:05:43-08:00","id":1295472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1295381#post1295381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sacred Flesh sounds really really awesome,what does it do?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I might be able to answer this. It got brought up somewhere and I want to say it was the podcast. Someone will probably have to correct me, but here's what I recall. It's a kind of meta Variation that I want to say is Mutant on the gross factor that allows you to take a tumor of your other variation and let people consume it to have temporary access to that variation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3776-autodefenestrate","name":"AutoDefenestrate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3776_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-09T21:05:43-08:00","id":1295473,"title":"","content":"Okay... double post. So to differentiate things, I've said it before but everything I hear about this makes me more convince that Mattew Swift and the Blue Electric Angels is a Deviant. They are an Elect Coactive Amalgam, possibly with a bit of Symbiote thrown in depending on if the Angels have had fairy dust recently.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3776,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3776-autodefenestrate","user":"AutoDefenestrate","date":".  Weird double post 03-10-2019, 12:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3776-autodefenestrate","name":"AutoDefenestrate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3776_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-09T21:24:16-08:00","id":1295483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AutoDefenestrate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1295472#post1295472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I might be able to answer this. It got brought up somewhere and I want to say it was the podcast. Someone will probably have to correct me, but here's what I recall. It's a kind of meta Variation that I want to say is Mutant on the gross factor that allows you to take a tumor of your other variation and let people consume it to have temporary access to that variation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you AD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T10:00:33-07:00","id":1298627,"title":"","content":"Given that the Chileans and the two Conspiracies mentioned in Ankara look pretty high power, are there ways to play a 1-2 Magnitude Renegade from a high-powered Conspiracy? Are you just beneath their notice until you get stronger?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24176-borne","name":"Borne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24176_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T10:48:58-07:00","id":1298656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Borne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1298627#post1298627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given that the Chileans and the two Conspiracies mentioned in Ankara look pretty high power, are there ways to play a 1-2 Magnitude Renegade from a high-powered Conspiracy? Are you just beneath their notice until you get stronger?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> At the very least, you could have been created by a Conspiracy controlled by the higher-power Conspiracy. So, after you bring down the Conspiracy that directly created you, you could find out they were funded and controlled by this bigger one, which you now want to take down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T10:57:22-07:00","id":1298662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Borne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1298627#post1298627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given that the Chileans and the two Conspiracies mentioned in Ankara look pretty high power, are there ways to play a 1-2 Magnitude Renegade from a high-powered Conspiracy? Are you just beneath their notice until you get stronger?</div> </div> </div> </div>For context, these were revealed in <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/episode-44-our-new-developer-chris-allen/\" target=\"_blank\">this week's Onyx Pathcast</a> - Chile is the Deviant-focused location in the Contagion Chronicle, while Ankara is one of the locations in the Deviant core.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":51,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","user":"marin","date":".  Word order derp 03-22-2019, 03:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T11:33:52-07:00","id":1298683,"title":"","content":"Both the settings sounded particularly cool (and conspiracy-heavy), and as they pointed out Contagion will be our first glimpse at Deviant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T11:46:03-07:00","id":1298688,"title":"","content":"so Contagion wont leave out deviants? sounds great!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T12:26:48-07:00","id":1298700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1298688#post1298688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">so Contagion wont leave out deviants? sounds great!</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. It's been known for a while that none of the major CofD gamelines would be left out, including the ones whose second edition versions haven't officially been released (Geist, Hunter, Mummy, Deviant).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T12:45:37-07:00","id":1298705,"title":"","content":"ahh ok, will be definitely looking forward to it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T13:41:33-07:00","id":1298733,"title":"","content":"Will Deviants be getting their own version of the Great Work/Inheritance for their unstable condition? Or is their fate sealed? A good part of Horror is having Hope in your soul or in this case a undefined, wounded mass of ephemera.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7106-extant-reality","name":"Extant Reality","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7106_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T14:34:51-07:00","id":1298749,"title":"","content":"from what we know, deviants dont have that. they live an incredibly hard life and can only hope to either stay sane and not get captured or break down","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T14:45:24-07:00","id":1298752,"title":"","content":"Basically, being a Deviant is its own form of permanent disability - you can manage to find some balance, find a way to live with it, but you're vulnerable to being destabilized and losing it again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T15:44:39-07:00","id":1298773,"title":"","content":"I believe that in his interview on the pathcast Eric Zawadski mentioned Memento in that, much in the same way Leonard Shelby had to make a new target for himself once he 'got' his revenge just to give himself something to move toward, a Renegade could potentially dismantle their Conspiracy but they would find themselves with a fundamental need to just replace their anger toward that group with another to fill that void. (One long, incredibly unbroken sentence, moving from topic to topic, so that no one had a chance to interrupt, it was really quite hypnotic)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3776-autodefenestrate","name":"AutoDefenestrate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3776_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T21:13:41-07:00","id":1298840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1298683#post1298683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Both the settings sounded particularly cool (and conspiracy-heavy), and as they pointed out Contagion will be our first glimpse at Deviant.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've had occasion to peek at sections of Contagion Chronicle three times as part as my work on other projects, and every single time has only made me more excited for that supplement. I'm actually a little disappointed that I didn't get to do any work on it, because it looks amazing.<br /> <br /> And yeah, both of the Deviant settings Chris did work on are showstoppers. Ankara's *1st draft* immediately made me want to run a game there, to the point where I, um, stole elements of it for the Exalted game I'm currently running. Granted, the other settings are also really cool, but if you judge them by weirdness factor alone, Ankara is the clear winner.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T21:37:52-07:00","id":1298844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1298840#post1298840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yeah, both of the Deviant settings Chris did work on are showstoppers. Ankara's *1st draft* immediately made me want to run a game there, to the point where I, um, stole elements of it for the Exalted game I'm currently running. Granted, the other settings are also really cool, but if you judge them by weirdness factor alone, Ankara is the clear winner.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gods, hearing that makes me so happy...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-04T15:12:07-07:00","id":1302655,"title":"","content":"Hey! New Deviant info!<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/deviant-at-midwinter-deviant-the-renegades-2/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/OPP-Metal.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/deviant-at-midwinter-deviant-the-renegades-2/\" target=\"_blank\"> Deviant at Midwinter [Deviant: The Renegades] &ndash; Onyx Path Publishing </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/deviant-at-midwinter-deviant-the-renegades-2/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://theonyxpath.com/deviant-at-midwinter-deviant-the-renegades-2/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T05:58:00-07:00","id":1302804,"title":"","content":"Every breadcrumb dropped about this game brings my hype for it to the forefront. Given the amount of Variations these characters have and the knowledge that the version of Gigantic the Sister has is Magnitude 3, do you think it's fair to assume that these characters are in the neighborhood of 5-7 Magnitudes of Variations each?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty","name":"Minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T10:34:50-07:00","id":1302860,"title":"","content":"I oddly like the underlying theme we have with Aleksandr, that he's ultimately just a goon. Really ties into how powerful Conspiracies are, that it turns out the billionaire who lives on private islands and cruise ships is just a dumbass who took loans he shouldn't with a gun - and a torpedo - to his head. It also shows just how unsatisfying revenge can be, no matter how justified; this man singlehandedly ruined Natalie's life, and he's likely barely aware of how his own magic works, let alone what it did to her. He's a chump, in the best way possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T16:15:54-07:00","id":1302949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Minty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1302804#post1302804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Every breadcrumb dropped about this game brings my hype for it to the forefront.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good. That means it's working. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And yes, I built them with 7 dots of Magnitude (which I believe I mentioned on the Pathcast awhile back), so your guess was right on.<br /> <br /> Regarding Aleksandr, I'm glad you liked that aspect. Conspiracies are built so that taking out an antagonist like him takes out one of the conspiracy's capabilities but doesn't eliminate the entire conspiracy. It's a little bit reminiscent of Doors or Clues, where overcoming the opposition isn't something you do with a single, decisive strike. You have to work up to that final confrontation, destroying labs, sabotaging projects, and taking out key players like Aleksandr until you can finally tear out the conspiracy's throat. And even if you take out an entire conspiracy, there's a whole Web of Pain out there to contend with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T16:47:16-07:00","id":1302954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1302949#post1302949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Good. That means it's working. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And yes, I built them with 7 dots of Magnitude (which I believe I mentioned on the Pathcast awhile back), so your guess was right on.<br /> <br /> Regarding Aleksandr, I'm glad you liked that aspect. Conspiracies are built so that taking out an antagonist like him takes out one of the conspiracy's capabilities but doesn't eliminate the entire conspiracy. It's a little bit reminiscent of Doors or Clues, where overcoming the opposition isn't something you do with a single, decisive strike. You have to work up to that final confrontation, destroying labs, sabotaging projects, and taking out key players like Aleksandr until you can finally tear out the conspiracy's throat. And even if you take out an entire conspiracy, there's a whole Web of Pain out there to contend with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eric,could you share the logic behind each character's Clades? Why Sister Laura is Coactive for instance?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T16:57:31-07:00","id":1302959,"title":"","content":"I know I\u00b4m not the first to make this question, but can you build Venom as a Deviant?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T17:13:12-07:00","id":1302966,"title":"","content":"yes, yes you can.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T17:28:07-07:00","id":1302970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1302954#post1302954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eric,could you share the logic behind each character's Clades? Why Sister Laura is Coactive for instance?</div> </div> </div> </div>Her powers are demonic in nature - not in the &quot;a demon's liver transplanted into your body&quot; sense but in a &quot;you have the mystical essence of a demon inside of you, its power straining to be unleashed on the world.&quot; (Note that this is probably something native to a Lower Realm, rather than one of the Unchained).<br /> <br /> Hrm. I suppose I could see about putting up some spoilers for Clades on the blog, soon-ish...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T17:29:27-07:00","id":1302971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1302970#post1302970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Her powers are demonic in nature - not in the &amp;quot;a demon's liver transplanted into your body&amp;quot; sense but in a &amp;quot;you have the mystical essence of a demon inside of you, its power straining to be unleashed on the world.&amp;quot; (Note that this is probably something native to a Lower Realm, rather than one of the Unchained).<br /> <br /> Hrm. I suppose I could see about putting up some spoilers for Clades on the blog, soon-ish...</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh that'd be quite amazing","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T18:03:43-07:00","id":1302977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1302970#post1302970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Her powers are demonic in nature - not in the &quot;a demon's liver transplanted into your body&quot; sense but in a &quot;you have the mystical essence of a demon inside of you, its power straining to be unleashed on the world.&quot; (Note that this is probably something native to a Lower Realm, rather than one of the Unchained).<br /> <br /> Hrm. I suppose I could see about putting up some spoilers for Clades on the blog, soon-ish...</div> </div> </div> </div>I wonder what the lucifuge would think of this... (and I'm sorry if you would rather me not bring up another gameline)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T20:16:42-07:00","id":1302988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1302977#post1302977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wonder what the lucifuge would think of this... (and I'm sorry if you would rather me not bring up another gameline)</div> </div> </div> </div>It's inevitable. I own at least the core of every CofD line, so in my own chronicles I've brought in splats from other lines as antagonists or allies, or used them to inspire modifications to the current game's metaphysics, on countless occasions. So, if I demure on a question like that, it isn't because I believe no one should ever cross the streams. However, I'm not the dev for Hunter (have not even written for it), so nothing I say can really be deemed &quot;official&quot; for that line.<br /> <br /> With that caveat in mind, it intrigues me that the big C Conspiracies of Hunter are, in many ways, doing some things that the little c conspiracies in Deviant are doing. Both have ways of giving supernatural powers to ordinary people (or at least unlocking that potential), but whereas Hunter Conspiracies do so in a way that is nominally safe, Deviant conspiracies shatter souls in the process. I think that creates a lot of opportunity for crossover between the two lines, as rogue factions of a Conspiracy turn out to be part of the Web of Pain conspiracies. The Wintergreen Process, for example, sounds like a method of triggering the Divergence, and while we hear plenty about the success stories who come back with psychic powers that make them super-detectives, I don't think anything specifically addresses what happens to the failures, and that strikes me as an opportunity for a story within either game line. With Hunter's emphasis on being the ones who protect humanity from the monsters, there would certainly be an irony to a Hunter Conspiracy finding itself in the crosshairs of a cohort of Renegades who regard that Conspiracy as something sinister.<br /> <br /> Something like the question of what Lucifuge would think of the demonic power lurking in Sister Laura is probably unanswerable, at least beyond &quot;what do you think would be most interesting in *your* chronicle?&quot; It's not much different than asking what Lucifuge would think of Fractals. They're neat questions with the potential to drive excellent stories, but the answers are going to vary from troupe to troupe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T20:41:37-07:00","id":1302995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quo