active for Larry Trainor, Mutant for Rita Farr, and Coactive or Cephalist for Jane. Gar from Titans would definitely be a Chimeric. Origin-wise: Cliff, Larry and Rita would be Accidentals, Gar a Volunteer, Jane an Unwilling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-09T15:58:32-07:00","id":1303842,"title":"","content":"Absolutely. They were one of the first big groups of comic 'deviants,' coming out just before the X-men. And you can probably toss in some of the antagonists as Deviants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-09T17:03:49-07:00","id":1303847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iceblade44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1303063#post1303063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When the book gets released. Very little to talk about when we dont know anything</div> </div> </div> </div>How unfortunate. Ah well, life is life after all. Now another question: the Deviants are metaphysically unstable and could go into soul meltdown if they push their Scars too far, so could there be a set of state-altering paths they might undertake like Beast's Inheritances? The goal of possibly being to define one's self again is a worthy end game goal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7106-extant-reality","name":"Extant Reality","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7106_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-09T17:14:36-07:00","id":1303849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Extant Reality</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1303847#post1303847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How unfortunate. Ah well, life is life after all. Now another question: the Deviants are metaphysically unstable and could go into soul meltdown if they push their Scars too far, so could there be a set of state-altering paths they might undertake like Beast's Inheritances? The goal of possibly being to define one's self again is a worthy end game goal.</div> </div> </div> </div>so far the best a deviant can hope for is basically &quot;I need to be stable for as long as possible&quot;. deviant is a game that seems to not have an end state of being like promethean or Beast","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-09T20:53:28-07:00","id":1303879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1303849#post1303849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> so far the best a deviant can hope for is basically &quot;I need to be stable for as long as possible&quot;. deviant is a game that seems to not have an end state of being like promethean or Beast</div> </div> </div> </div>So the Deviant is damaged beyond any hope of self repair? Well that is the horror of being a Deviant isn't it?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7106-extant-reality","name":"Extant Reality","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7106_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-09T20:59:00-07:00","id":1303884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Extant Reality</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1303879#post1303879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So the Deviant is damaged beyond any hope of self repair? Well that is the horror of being a Deviant isn't it?</div> </div> </div> </div>well as far we know. and yup, the horror is the utter brokenness of being a deviant","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-09T21:40:34-07:00","id":1303885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1303849#post1303849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> so far the best a deviant can hope for is basically &quot;I need to be stable for as long as possible&quot;. deviant is a game that seems to not have an end state of being like promethean or Beast</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Which is kind of disappointing, because usually in stories that feature being turned into a science experiment gone wrong, the narrative involves the renegade trying to overcome what's been done to them, and not allowing their creators to dictate their purpose in life.<br /> <br /> But Deviant seems to have avoided that, in favor of making the character depend on others to validate their existence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-10T05:02:17-07:00","id":1303918,"title":"","content":"well most of those stories, they never get a cure. even the hulk just learns how better to control his condition","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-10T05:32:13-07:00","id":1303921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1303885#post1303885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Which is kind of disappointing, because usually in stories that feature being turned into a science experiment gone wrong, the narrative involves the renegade trying to overcome what's been done to them, and not allowing their creators to dictate their purpose in life.<br /> <br /> But Deviant seems to have avoided that, in favor of making the character depend on others to validate their existence.</div> </div> </div> </div>From what I remember, Renegades can actually reach a state of relative stability by increasing their Loyalty above their Conviction, at which point they are called Guardians. Depending on how it works, this could be thought of as &quot;finding their own purpose&quot; as opposed to finding a new bogeyman to fight constantly, though it is not a permanent state and needs to be maintained or they will fall right back into it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty","name":"Minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-10T09:03:12-07:00","id":1303961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1303918#post1303918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">well most of those stories, they never get a cure. even the hulk just learns how better to control his condition</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And that's fine. I'm not saying they have to figure out a way to become human again. But learning to utilize their newfound abilities for the sake of their own reasons, instead of what others tell them they should be used for would be a more traditional fit for this kind of story. Like the scene from Ghost Rider, when Johnny tells the devil that he's going to use the power of his curse to fight against him, rather than become his servant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-10T09:11:42-07:00","id":1303965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1303961#post1303961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And that's fine. I'm not saying they have to figure out a way to become human again. But learning to utilize their newfound abilities for the sake of their own reasons, instead of what others tell them they should be used for would be a more traditional fit for this kind of story. Like the scene from Ghost Rider, when Johnny tells the devil that he's going to use the power of his curse to fight against him, rather than become his servant.</div> </div> </div> </div>That starts his life as a renegade.<br /> <br /> From there he gets harassed by the minions of hell and heaven as he tries to do what he wants to do, and find that using his powers in any way are going to affect his personal life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-10-2019, 12:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-10T10:01:38-07:00","id":1303982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1303965#post1303965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That starts his life as a renegade.<br /> <br /> From there he gets harassed by the minions of hell and heaven as he tries to do what he wants to do, and find that using his powers in any way are going to affect his personal life.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1394_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1394\" data-vbnamecard=\"1394\">Nyrufa</a> is referring to deviants having to define themselves through others. personally, I think deviants being trapped in such a life adds to the horror. the fact they cant ever escape their state of being makes it all the more tragic (though to be honest, I dont think every gameline needs its supernaturals to have a happy ending in terms of ascending their condition)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-10T17:28:01-07:00","id":1304051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1303961#post1303961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And that's fine. I'm not saying they have to figure out a way to become human again. But learning to utilize their newfound abilities for the sake of their own reasons, instead of what others tell them they should be used for would be a more traditional fit for this kind of story.</div> </div> </div> </div>To my understanding this is literally one of the main ways Loyalty Touchstones work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-10T18:16:14-07:00","id":1304059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1304051#post1304051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To my understanding this is literally one of the main ways Loyalty Touchstones work.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Except &quot;Loyalty&quot; sounds to me like they simply pledge themselves in service to a different master, instead of finding their own reason for living. Not saying that devotion to somebody else can't be a possible reason. But it should not be the only option available to those who become Renegades.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-10T18:33:06-07:00","id":1304061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1304059#post1304059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Except &amp;quot;Loyalty&amp;quot; sounds to me like they simply pledge themselves in service to a different master, instead of finding their own reason for living. Not saying that devotion to somebody else can't be a possible reason. But it should not be the only option available to those who become Renegades.</div> </div> </div> </div>to me, loyalty sounds not like a pledge and more like &quot;this person/group treats me well. I'm going to protect them&quot;. how this takes is what matters. a touchstone may never know a deviant protects them until it kills his local bully (and by bully, I mean &quot;guy who makes my life hell, not life endangering). a deviant renegade is a DANGEROUS guardian to have","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-10T21:41:33-07:00","id":1304101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1304059#post1304059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Except &quot;Loyalty&quot; sounds to me like they simply pledge themselves in service to a different master, instead of finding their own reason for living.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2026 <i>really</i> don't care what it &quot;sounds like&quot; to you, because the first post in this thread \u2014 updated as recently as <i>last month</i> \u2014 recaps what we've been told about what it <i>is</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades#post1032843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Integrity: Dual Stats \u2013 Conviction &amp; Loyalty<br /> Conviction, like Vice, is easy to fulfill, but doesn\u2019t stave off mutation for long. It involves harassing their creators. Loyalty, like Virtue, is harder, but staves off mutation longer and can even reverse the course of a deviant\u2019s transformation in extreme circumstances. It involves finding something or someone worth protecting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Loyalty is one of those places where the &quot;<a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/episode-40-deviant-the-zawadski/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant is not a superhero game, but superhero media flaws can help understand Deviant</a>&quot; thing seems to live.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-10T22:41:04-07:00","id":1304107,"title":"","content":"Loyalty is not an obligation to others. It's saying these people are <i>yours</i>. Like any lay to claim, that requires <i>maintenance</i>. If you can't keep it, even to such that it rebels against you, it ain't <i>yours</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-12T09:46:57-07:00","id":1304456,"title":"","content":"Since Deviant is a major template, how are they compared with the others in terms of power?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-12T09:51:36-07:00","id":1304458,"title":"","content":"The devs have said above Hunter, below everything else (more or less, it can vary a bit with different Variations)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-12T11:36:01-07:00","id":1304472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1304458#post1304458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The devs have said above Hunter, below everything else (more or less, it can vary a bit with different Variations)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't know. It sounds like magnitude 7 PCs were pretty powerful in the Mid-Winter game. I'd imagine characters at max Magnitude are going to be very powerful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-12T11:39:29-07:00","id":1304474,"title":"","content":"I thought magnitude can only go up to five?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-12T11:50:28-07:00","id":1304478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iceblade44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1304474#post1304474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought magnitude can only go up to five?</div> </div> </div> </div>Per Eric in the Pathcast, the Magnitude range is from 2 to 15.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-12T12:22:23-07:00","id":1304484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iceblade44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1304474#post1304474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought magnitude can only go up to five?</div> </div> </div> </div>Variations only go up to Magnitude 5; characters can start with between 2 and 15 Magnitudes","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty","name":"Minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-12T12:52:41-07:00","id":1304488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1304472#post1304472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I don't know. It sounds like magnitude 7 PCs were pretty powerful in the Mid-Winter game. I'd imagine characters at max Magnitude are going to be very powerful.</div> </div> </div> </div>to clarify, Eric said that while deviants usually wont be too powerful, they CAN develop powers that are extremely useful (he listed some examples such as a deviant who could learn true names instinctively, a powerful boon to Mages)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-16T09:53:54-07:00","id":1305287,"title":"","content":"From what I remember Deviant's power stat only goes up to 5, starts, at 0, and you only gain it at narrative intervals. Since other splats' maximum stats and skills are tied to power stat, specifically only allowing you to go above 5 dots at power stat 6+, do you think that means that Remade top out at a maximum of 5 in stats and skills (barring Variations)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty","name":"Minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-16T11:06:10-07:00","id":1305302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Minty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1305287#post1305287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From what I remember Deviant's power stat only goes up to 5, starts, at 0, and you only gain it at narrative intervals. Since other splats' maximum stats and skills are tied to power stat, specifically only allowing you to go above 5 dots at power stat 6+, do you think that means that Remade top out at a maximum of 5 in stats and skills (barring Variations)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps they use Supernatural Tolerance instead of the unnamed power trait? It's calculated as the power trait plus highest ranking Variation. Since all other splats except Demon has their power trait as their Supernatural Tolerance it becomes the de facto trait cap.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-16T11:13:19-07:00","id":1305303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1305302#post1305302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Perhaps they use Supernatural Tolerance instead of the unnamed power trait? It's calculated as the power trait plus highest ranking Variation. Since all other splats except Demon has their power trait as their Supernatural Tolerance it becomes the de facto trait cap.</div> </div> </div> </div>That could be interesting. I thought they might end up at a maximum of 5 because they are supposed to be a bit lower powered than other splats, but tying their max attributes to narrative milestones sounds like a good way to gate power level and also tie it to the narrative.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty","name":"Minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-17T06:22:40-07:00","id":1305454,"title":"","content":"FYI; the latest Contagion setting (Santiago) has a write of a Deviant in it, and what I presume is a 'creator' conspiracy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-17T09:30:58-07:00","id":1305498,"title":"","content":"Based on the stat block given in the Santiago chapter, it would appear that Deviant's power stat is called &quot;Acclimation&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty","name":"Minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-17T18:37:42-07:00","id":1305613,"title":"","content":"And Stability, based on the KS preview and various postings here is where Variation cost in damage are scored. &quot;take a minor Instability&quot; may be the same as taking bashing damage on the Stability track (like Changeling Clarity, though the Integrity role is being taken by the dual anchors of Conviction and Loyalty, as both had scores, making Stability a damage track replacing the traditional 'fuel' role)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-17T22:27:55-07:00","id":1305642,"title":"","content":"It looks like Deviant's Conspiracies are going to give us a lot more organizational goodies to play with. Geist's Krewe mechanics were noted to be the debut of the bare bones versions of these rules, and I'm rather intrigued by what &quot;nodes&quot; are. So, new things we know about Conspiracies:<ul><li>Conspiracies have a <b>Virtue and a Vice</b>, which all members of the Conspiracy might be able to draw on (this would be in line with the Krewe mechanics)</li> <li>Conspiracies have <b>Principles </b>instead of Doctrine, short sentences that are kind-of-sort-of Aspirations and outline what the Conspiracy finds important.</li> <li>Conspiracies use the <b>simplified Attributes</b> Ephemeral Beings use. No change from the Krewe mechanics there.</li> <li>Conspiracies have something called <b>N</b><b>odes</b>. They are separated into four categories: <b>Hierarchal, Temporal, Exploitative, and Structural.</b> Individual nodes appear to be connected to things like facilities, branches of government, and other resources at the disposal of the Conspiracy. Rather notably, each node is tied to a specific named character, who'll likely be fleshed out in some capacity.</li> <li>Conspiracies have <b>Icons</b>. These appear to be the same sort of thing as Regalia in the Krewe mechanics, but they seem to have some more flexibility in their construction and use. One example Icon allows you to temporarily take on Variations, another simply provides the 8-again quality to a roll, while the third is possibly world-ending. Namely, allowing Santiago's Contagion strain to spread across all Chile and possibly beyond.</li> <li>Conspiracies appear to be missing <b>Merits</b>. Unlike Krewes, Conspiracies don't appear to have Merits. Maybe nodes pull double duty on that end, who knows.</li> <li>Conspiracies don't have a <b>Power Stat</b>. Unlike Krewes, Conspiracies don't appear to have a Power Stat that limits their growth and capabilities. Unless &quot;Standing&quot;, is the Conspiracy power stat.</li> </ul>In general? I'm really excited to see what the full Conspiracy rules are. Tinkering with mechanics for organizations in the CofD has been one of my more consistent projects lately, and having a whole bunch of new toys for the toolkit does put a smile on my face.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":4152,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","user":"Arcanist","date":".  Corrected the information on Conspiracy/Deviant Power Stat speculation courtesy of @Satchel 04-18-2019, 02:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-17T22:54:55-07:00","id":1305646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1305642#post1305642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless &quot;Standing&quot;, the Deviant power-stat, is shared with the Conspiracy that made them. It has been said before that powerful Deviants come from powerful Conspiracies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Standing is not the Deviant power-stat, as evidenced by El Centinela not having it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-18T04:16:09-07:00","id":1305684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1305642#post1305642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It looks like Deviant's Conspiracies are going to give us a lot more organizational goodies to play with. Geist's Krewe mechanics were noted to be the debut of the bare bones versions of these rules, and I'm rather intrigued by what &quot;nodes&quot; are. So, new things we know about Conspiracies:<ul><li>Conspiracies have a <b>Virtue and a Vice</b>, which all members of the Conspiracy might be able to draw on (this would be in line with the Krewe mechanics)</li> <li>Conspiracies have <b>Principles </b>instead of Doctrine, short sentences that are kind-of-sort-of Aspirations and outline what the Conspiracy finds important.</li> <li>Conspiracies use the <b>simplified Attributes</b> Ephemeral Beings use. No change from the Krewe mechanics there.</li> <li>Conspiracies have something called <b>nodes</b>. They are separated into four categories: Hierarchal, Temporal, Exploitative, and Structural. Individual nodes appear to be connected to things like facilities, branches of government, and other resources at the disposal of the Conspiracy. Rather notably, each node is tied to a specific named character, who'll likely be fleshed out in some capacity.</li> <li>Conspiracies have <b>Icons</b>. These appear to be the same sort of thing as Regalia in the Krewe mechanics, but they seem to have some more flexibility in their construction and use. One example Icon allows you to temporarily take on Variations, another simply provides the 8-again quality to a roll, while the third is possibly world-ending. Namely, allowing Santiago's Contagion strain to spread across all Chile and possibly beyond.</li> <li>Conspiracies appear to be missing <b>Merits</b>. Unlike Krewes, Conspiracies don't appear to have Merits. Maybe nodes pull double duty on that end, who knows.</li> <li>Conspiracies don't have a <b>Power Stat</b>. Unlike Krewes, Conspiracies don't appear to have a Power Stat that limits their growth and capabilities. Unless &quot;Standing&quot;, the Deviant power-stat, is shared with the Conspiracy that made them. It has been said before that powerful Deviants come from powerful Conspiracies.</li> </ul><br /> In general? I'm really excited to see what the full Conspiracy rules are. Tinkering with mechanics for organizations in the CofD has been one of my more consistent projects lately, and having a whole bunch of new toys for the toolkit does put a smile on my face.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Perhaps Standing is the Conspiracy power stat (it was listed at the top of the Conspiracy entry instead of with the rest of the traits)?<br /> The Nodes remind me of the Krewe Congregation and God-Machine Linchpins. You can reduce a Conspiracy by removing one of these nodes.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-18T20:21:07-07:00","id":1305890,"title":"","content":"It's fun to watch you folks jump on these little tidbits. You can see what I mean about Santiago, now, can't you? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Acclimation is indeed the Deviant &quot;power stat,&quot; rated from 0 to 5. One of the subtle ways that the Remade are less powerful than other splats is the resultant &quot;Clash of Wills gap.&quot;<br /> <br /> Stability is the &quot;health track&quot; on which Deviants take Instability as damage (minor, medium, and major). Instability makes it harder to manage your Scars (especially, but not exclusively, Involuntary Scars) and can make your Scars worse or cause/allow you to develop new Scars (&quot;allow&quot; because in order to purchase a new Variation, you have to have a Scar available that is powerful enough to entangle with the new Variation). It really isn't a fuel stat so much as a gauge of your progress toward complete destabilization (with its accompanying messy death).<br /> <br /> Standing describes a conspiracy's power level on a scale from 1 to 10.<br /> <br /> Icons are the conspiracy's &quot;superpowers,&quot; each attached to a specific Node - and yes, originally based on Regalia.<br /> <br /> The approach to krewes was a definite precursor to Deviant's conspiracy mechanics, and kind of also an incremental evolution of the concept of God-Machine Infrastructure - the sort of thing where I wish we had come up with this when I was explaining how Infrastructure and God-Machine projects work. Nodes indeed represent a collection of resources available to the conspiracy. Each has a Linchpin (see?), which is a character that is essential to that Node. If you take out (kill, convert, etc.) that character, you take the Node down with them. You can also destroy a Node in other ways, but it's generally more complicated, since it often involves large scale arson, mass murder, or a really effective reveal of the Node's malfeasance sufficient to get law enforcement or public opinion to shut it down. Taking out Nodes is the most obvious way of dealing damage to a conspiracy (which has a damage track nearly identical to that of Congregation).<br /> <br /> Conspiracy rules in the core are focused on them as antagonist organizations. I definitely want to expand on them in a supplement that features Devoted, who really should have some ability to influence and make use of the conspiracy's resources in interesting ways. However, I haven't spent a huge amount of time brainstorming what that will look like beyond knowing that I really, really, really want to expand those mechanics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-18T21:04:21-07:00","id":1305896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1305890#post1305890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The approach to krewes was a definite precursor to Deviant's conspiracy mechanics, and kind of also an incremental evolution of the concept of God-Machine Infrastructure - the sort of thing where I wish we had come up with this when I was explaining how Infrastructure and God-Machine projects work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Something to remember when the time comes for CofD 3e? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-18T21:25:03-07:00","id":1305898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1305896#post1305896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Something to remember when the time comes for CofD 3e? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Seems likely, yeah. I'm going to have to pick up a copy of The Contagion Chronicle (or stop prevaricating and just back it already), as from what I've seen of it, that concept is not going to vanish if and when the next edition cycle starts. Such a cool idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T02:08:22-07:00","id":1305935,"title":"","content":"The org mechanics were invented for a Mummy: The Curse 2e pitch some four or five years ago, and have been slowly working their way into games since.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t know if Mummy 2e is even using them for Cults, as the person who wrote that pitch isn\u2019t developing it, but they served our purposes for Geist and Deviant. You never know what\u2019s going to get traction - every game now uses a system invented for Mekhet shadow cults as Mystery Initiation!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T03:05:00-07:00","id":1305943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1305890#post1305890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's fun to watch you folks jump on these little tidbits. You can see what I mean about Santiago, now, can't you? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Acclimation is indeed the Deviant &quot;power stat,&quot; rated from 0 to 5. One of the subtle ways that the Remade are less powerful than other splats is the resultant &quot;Clash of Wills gap.&quot;<br /> <br /> Stability is the &quot;health track&quot; on which Deviants take Instability as damage (minor, medium, and major). Instability makes it harder to manage your Scars (especially, but not exclusively, Involuntary Scars) and can make your Scars worse or cause/allow you to develop new Scars (&quot;allow&quot; because in order to purchase a new Variation, you have to have a Scar available that is powerful enough to entangle with the new Variation). It really isn't a fuel stat so much as a gauge of your progress toward complete destabilization (with its accompanying messy death).<br /> <br /> Standing describes a conspiracy's power level on a scale from 1 to 10.<br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>We've all gotten a great deal of joy from jumping into the Mysteries of the tidbits <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Thank you for confirming and correcting some of our speculations! If I might ask a few more questions: <br /> <br /> 1) Does Acclimation by chance influence how large a Stability track a Remade has? (Guessing out of left field that the more acclimated one becomes to one's Divergence the more stable their physical and metaphysical state)<br /> <br /> 2) I recall hints of the Magnitude (2-15) of a Deviant's (or rather the average magnitude of a cohort of deviant's) Variations is what determines the initial Standing of a conspiracy. Is there a link between Acclimation and the total Magnitude of a Deviant? <br /> <br /> 3) I recall mention that Voluntary Variations can cause Instability. Do some Involuntary or Persistent Variations cause Instability as well?<br /> <br /> 4) last one (for now lol) I promise. How does one heal Instability on the Stability track?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T03:06:43-07:00","id":1305944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1305935#post1305935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The org mechanics were invented for a Mummy: The Curse 2e pitch some four or five years ago, and have been slowly working their way into games since.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t know if Mummy 2e is even using them for Cults, as the person who wrote that pitch isn\u2019t developing it, but they served our purposes for Geist and Deviant. You never know what\u2019s going to get traction - every game now uses a system invented for Mekhet shadow cults as Mystery Initiation!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Mystery Initiation is an awesome mechanic! I love how it has developed into the Krewe creation rules and Deviant Conspiracies! I do hope that Mummy 2e will have a further iteration. I thought I detected hints of these group building mechanics in the WtF2e book the Pack, and really loved it!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T09:09:12-07:00","id":1306011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1305943#post1305943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We've all gotten a great deal of joy from jumping into the Mysteries of the tidbits <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Thank you for confirming and correcting some of our speculations! If I might ask a few more questions:<br /> <br /> 1) Does Acclimation by chance influence how large a Stability track a Remade has? (Guessing out of left field that the more acclimated one becomes to one's Divergence the more stable their physical and metaphysical state)<br /> <br /> 2) I recall hints of the Magnitude (2-15) of a Deviant's (or rather the average magnitude of a cohort of deviant's) Variations is what determines the initial Standing of a conspiracy. Is there a link between Acclimation and the total Magnitude of a Deviant?<br /> <br /> 3) I recall mention that Voluntary Variations can cause Instability. Do some Involuntary or Persistent Variations cause Instability as well?<br /> <br /> 4) last one (for now lol) I promise. How does one heal Instability on the Stability track?</div> </div> </div> </div>1) Great guess, and correct. Not its sole effect, but an important one.<br /> <br /> 2) Total Magnitude of Variations determines Threat Level, and thus the Standing of your starting conspiracy. Acclimation doesn't enter into the equation at all, and you can have dozens of dots of Variations without ever raising Acclimation. Variations come with Scars, however, which provide a different sort of limiting factor.<br /> <br /> 3) Instability usually comes from either a dramatic failure on an attempt to use a Variation (or resist its Scar) or failing to act on the dictates of Conviction or Loyalty (Faltering, as it's called). There are also a handful of other circumstances that cause Instability, such as using certain very powerful Variations multiple times in a story or falling into a Variation-specific failure state (teleporting into a solid object, having your astral form killed, etc.).<br /> <br /> 4) Healing Stability involves Touchstones (or being a Guardian, which sort of gives you a slow regeneration of Stability, while the condition lasts). The more severe the Instability, the more extreme the actions required to clear it. Clearing a minor Instability can involve any noteworthy progress toward defeating your Conviction Touchstones, but healing a major Instability usually involves successfully killing a Conviction Touchstone. The current version of the rules also allows you to heal some Instability by developing a new Scar, which is sort of the metaphysical equivalent of cutting off your own arm to keep from dying of gangrene.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T17:13:39-07:00","id":1306113,"title":"","content":"Do Clades have anything to do with the size of your Stability track or how you mitigate Instability and/or Scars? And is there a limit to how many new Scars you can pick up to fend off Instability? Or rather, I think there would have to be - is this also based on Acclimation, or perhaps your Conviction/Loyalty?<br /> It was said before that Scars don't balance Variations on a 1-to-1 basis, though El Centinela's stat block in the Chilean chapter of the Contagion Chronicle made it look like besides the free Origin Magnitude there was a balance on the numbers for Variations and Scars. Do the tags on Variations such as &quot;Toggled&quot; and &quot;Subtle&quot; have any impact on what Scars you are allowed to balance them with, or do the Scars say what they can balance against?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty","name":"Minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T17:43:17-07:00","id":1306121,"title":"","content":"with the overt persistent scars that seem difficult to disguise such as huge size (I think you mentioned a scar where the deviant was ridiculously tall?), how will deviants avoid constant checks against suspicion evidence?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T17:45:49-07:00","id":1306122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1306121#post1306121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">with the overt persistent scars that seem difficult to disguise such as huge size (I think you mentioned a scar where the deviant was ridiculously tall?), how will deviants avoid constant checks against suspicion evidence?</div> </div> </div> </div>Blame the demon in the crowd?<br /> <br /> (It's a question I'm mildly wondering about.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T17:51:24-07:00","id":1306123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1306122#post1306122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Blame the demon in the crowd?<br /> <br /> (It's a question I'm mildly wondering about.)</div> </div> </div> </div>truly, a flawless cover story","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T17:58:09-07:00","id":1306124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1306121#post1306121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">with the overt persistent scars that seem difficult to disguise such as huge size (I think you mentioned a scar where the deviant was ridiculously tall?), how will deviants avoid constant checks against suspicion evidence?</div> </div> </div> </div>Stay out of sight, I'd guess. Keep to the alleys, keep to the shadows, keep out of the cameras' gaze.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24176-borne","name":"Borne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24176_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T18:12:24-07:00","id":1306129,"title":"","content":"I suppose (goes with the allegory as homeless in a way, right?) but I bet you can do more than that","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T18:25:59-07:00","id":1306134,"title":"","content":"You could always disguise yourself as two children in a trench coat","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty","name":"Minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T18:44:43-07:00","id":1306137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1306121#post1306121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">with the overt persistent scars that seem difficult to disguise such as huge size (I think you mentioned a scar where the deviant was ridiculously tall?), how will deviants avoid constant checks against suspicion evidence?</div> </div> </div> </div>Say you have a Fucked up Birth defect?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T19:32:48-07:00","id":1306144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Minty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1306113#post1306113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do Clades have anything to do with the size of your Stability track or how you mitigate Instability and/or Scars? And is there a limit to how many new Scars you can pick up to fend off Instability? Or rather, I think there would have to be - is this also based on Acclimation, or perhaps your Conviction/Loyalty?<br /> It was said before that Scars don't balance Variations on a 1-to-1 basis, though El Centinela's stat block in the Chilean chapter of the Contagion Chronicle made it look like besides the free Origin Magnitude there was a balance on the numbers for Variations and Scars. Do the tags on Variations such as &quot;Toggled&quot; and &quot;Subtle&quot; have any impact on what Scars you are allowed to balance them with, or do the Scars say what they can balance against?</div> </div> </div> </div>- No. Sort of. Yes.<br /> <br /> - Yes. There are rules concerning how many &quot;un-entangled Scars&quot; you can have, for the sake of gaming table sanity. I want to see them in playtests before I talk about them more than that, though. Acclimation and Loyalty/Conviction don't currently figure into those mechanics, however.<br /> <br /> - It is possible to create a character with a 1-to-1 balance of Variations and Scars, just not a requirement. More to come on this topic, eventually.<br /> <br /> - Keywords provide some clarity around when a Variation is active or inactive, and the activation method (Controlled, Involuntary, or Persistent) can make these keywords more or less relevant. For example, Toggled only applies to Variations entangled with Persistent Scars, meaning that they're something the Deviant &quot;toggles on,&quot; as opposed to Perpetual, which means that if it's attached to a Persistent Scar, it is always active (since Toggled agelessness would be meaningless, while Overt Variations are a huge problem if they're always active). It is possible to fiddle with these keywords within the system, as it currently stands, such that you can have a Toggled version of Gigantic (hulking out only when you want to) or a Perpetual one (this is just how big you are, now, with all the attention that comes with being, say, Size 10). But if you've attached Gigantic to a Controlled Scar (making it a Controlled Variation), Toggled is irrelevant to you, since the very definition of a Controlled Variation is that you have to activate it before it benefits/hoses you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T18:08:15-07:00","id":1307083,"title":"","content":"Deviant it's officialy in development. I can feel the ks coming in a few months. Halloween KS would be my guess","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T18:30:23-07:00","id":1307089,"title":"","content":"So basically you can pick your own hard mode?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T20:00:13-07:00","id":1307115,"title":"","content":"being able to set your own difficulty level through scars and complimenting conspiracy seems like it will be very fun. will deviants also come with it's own villains other than fellow deviants, devoted, and conspiracies? whether introduced in the corebook or through a possible supplement","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"ke