:"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-23T22:26:02-07:00","id":1313993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1313991#post1313991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I understand there's an organization system, to represent organizations in a better way than Mummy 1e's cults and the Mystery Cult Merit. Is it the same as, or more in depth than, the krewe structure in Geist 2e?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I remember Dave saying something about Geist being the first gameline that the organization rules of Deviant appeared in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-23T23:00:18-07:00","id":1313994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1313993#post1313993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I remember Dave saying something about Geist being the first gameline that the organization rules of Deviant appeared in.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup!<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1232455#post1232455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, the Krewe rules are the first use of the Chronicles' bright new organization-level subsystem.</div> </div> </div> </div>(And of course, because of the vagaries of memory and linear time and search engine result refinement, I can't find the original mention that Deviant's conspiracy rules would be the second place those mechanics would show up, from which the guess arose that prompted the above confirmation.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-23T23:04:56-07:00","id":1313995,"title":"","content":"Thanks. I wasn't sure if it was just a part of the rules in Geist and we'd see the full breadth of them in Deviant or what. Looking over it seems pretty comprehensive. Though I'm not sure if the Regalia aspect is a Krewe thing or something all organizations with Esotery have. Presumably we'll get a more baseline system in Deviant that can then be tooled for things like Mummy or Werewolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-24-2019, 02:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-24T02:22:01-07:00","id":1314014,"title":"","content":"It could probably easily be retrofitted to Werewolf by fans (especially since the organisation membership creation rules are already included), but since it wasn't developed in time for the Pack I don't think there'll be any supplements for a while where it would be fitting to include the organisation system. Possibly if there's a Players' Guide style book on the horizon.<br /> <br /> As for Mummy, I think it was confirmed to be used in second edition but I might be misremembering. Either way I'm expecting the organisation system to return since a lot of the game is focused around cults due to their importance to the eponymous characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-24T09:13:59-07:00","id":1314100,"title":"","content":"IIRC The Pack\u2019s pack mechanics are basically a rough prototype of the Krewes-and-onward ones or at least quite a few bits of the former ended up going into the latter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-24T19:23:56-07:00","id":1314223,"title":"","content":"Organization mechanics in Deviant assume conspiracies take on a much more antagonistic role than do Krewes in Geist. Rival/antagonist Krewes are possible, but not the default the way hostile conspiracies are. However, I definitely want to expand conspiracy rules when we dig into Devoted some more in a later supplement, since Devoted are going to have access to conspiracy resources far more often than Renegades will.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-25T06:48:31-07:00","id":1314283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1313971#post1313971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know that guy that makes every tabletop game an exercise in their personal fetishes?<br /> <br /> Konradleijon does this in every subforum. From trying very hard to make Dominatrix Beasts (or was it Mages?) to asking very genuine questions about whether or not various supernaturals have periods, to this. I'd report, but I don't actually think it's against any of the forum rules, so I just blocked instead.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That was not intended to Be a Lactation Fetish.<br /> <br /> The Story of Drinking special Breast Milk to give you powers are pretty old see the Story of Hercules.<br /> <br /> Edit and this <a href=\"https://isiopolis.com/2013/01/26/milk-the-magic-of-isis/\" target=\"_blank\">https://isiopolis.com/2013/01/26/mil...magic-of-isis/</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23952,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","user":"Konradleijon","date":".  Added link 05-25-2019, 09:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-26T05:08:08-07:00","id":1314503,"title":"","content":"Wasn't that mostly just his heritage?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23543-penguinbowler","name":"Penguinbowler","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-26T10:54:12-07:00","id":1314560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1314223#post1314223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Organization mechanics in Deviant assume conspiracies take on a much more antagonistic role than do Krewes in Geist. Rival/antagonist Krewes are possible, but not the default the way hostile conspiracies are. However, I definitely want to expand conspiracy rules when we dig into Devoted some more in a later supplement, since Devoted are going to have access to conspiracy resources far more often than Renegades will.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the clarification, I suppose at the least seeing Deviant's take will give us some comparison for them and see what should be done to juryrig them for other groups.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-03T21:25:49-07:00","id":1316366,"title":"","content":"Will the Conspirators have their elite agents? Basically humans in smaller temple like the old dormant technocratic agents (in the old WoD), mad scients, ctulhian cultists?<br /> <br /> Will there be experiments of the conpirations that will reshape in little rational beings, deviants flawed? Basically the equivalent of promethean pandoras?<br /> <br /> Will there be any minor temple of dis Deviants servants?<br /> <br /> It will be possible to command a hive mind of servants (who retain some of their mind yet, but have their mind in them and a pretty subconscious connection from the minds of one servant to another servant for quick exchange of information) as Eveline does in Resident Evil 7 ? I imagine that the scar would be slow disoersonalizaci\u00f3n and some thoughts of the victim cross to the other side which makes if losing badly ever in the own hive created.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/641-ben-linus","name":"Ben Linus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-04T09:58:07-07:00","id":1316448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ben Linus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1316366#post1316366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Will the Conspirators have their elite agents? Basically humans in smaller temple like the old dormant technocratic agents (in the old WoD), mad scients, ctulhian cultists?<br /> <br /> Will there be experiments of the conpirations that will reshape in little rational beings, deviants flawed? Basically the equivalent of promethean pandoras?<br /> <br /> Will there be any minor temple of dis Deviants servants?<br /> <br /> It will be possible to command a hive mind of servants (who retain some of their mind yet, but have their mind in them and a pretty subconscious connection from the minds of one servant to another servant for quick exchange of information) as Eveline does in Resident Evil 7 ? I imagine that the scar would be slow disoersonalizaci\u00f3n and some thoughts of the victim cross to the other side which makes if losing badly ever in the own hive created.</div> </div> </div> </div>can you please be more clear. also its template not temple","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-04T10:38:32-07:00","id":1316452,"title":"","content":"I'm sorry, I'll try to be clearer and more direct.<br /> <br /> Are conspiracies just normal people or can they have human beings with powers that come from the experiences (magical or scientific) that they do? In other words, their experiences only produce deviants or can they generate small advantages for some of their human operatives? Like in a more magical conspiracy, is it possible for any member of her to have access to some spells?<br /> <br /> Is there anything like Faltering Deviants, who are born without any any human trait, they are already monsters ?<br /> <br /> Will there be any way for Deviants to force servants for themselves by their powers or condition?<br /> <br /> Something like Eveline from Resident Evil 7, who manages to create collective minds of their victims and control them on some level is it possible?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":641,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/641-ben-linus","user":"Ben Linus","date":". 06-04-2019, 01:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/641-ben-linus","name":"Ben Linus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-04T19:30:23-07:00","id":1316531,"title":"","content":"Most individual antagonists are Baselines (ordinary humans). Some are Devoted. Manticores serve as support troops, spies, and quirky side-characters. New templates might appear in a future supplement, but I haven't thought about how those might look, yet.<br /> <br /> Conspiracies serve as the main enemies. That their component parts are almost all Baselines provides a few additional layers of potential horror:<br /> <br /> 1) They are numerous. Killing one conspirator or burning down one shady AF clinic may feel good, but there's always more mad scientists and evil cultists, more shady AF clinics and corrupt police precincts, and, once the current conspiracy is gone, more conspiracies connected to it in the seemingly endless Web of Pain. There is a sense of disposability about them, and a Storyteller probably shouldn't get toooo attached to any one Baseline enemy (they're pretty much dead meat, once the cohort catches up with them), but the supply is effectively infinite.<br /> <br /> 2) They don't have the &quot;excuse&quot; of being driven by supernatural urges, but how good does it feel to kill someone who is just in it for a paycheck, or who is trying to cure a disease, or who wants to arm humanity against the supernatural horrors lurking in the shadows, or whose family is being held hostage to ensure their cooperation? Taken as a whole, conspiracies are clear villains and harbor and enable the worst impulses of many individual villains. But some individual conspirators are dupes, wage slaves, or outright hostages of the conspiracies they serve. Killing them as a means of defeating the conspiracy is messy and complicated - far from black-and-white.<br /> <br /> 3) They look like everyone else. In a recent playtest, a pair of exterminators sent by the landlord caught the cohort &quot;at home.&quot; The Renegades, understandably, assumed the worst - that these two were agents of the conspiracy sent to poke their noses in vacant apartments in search of the Deviants. By the time the Broken had firmly established that the exterminators had no idea who or what these squatters were, it was too late. The two had seen the talking squirrel and the tentacled monster living in the apartment. They would surely tell someone what they had seen - whether it was their boss, or a friend after a night spent drinking. The cohort ended up killing them both. That was an ugly, awful crime committed against two innocent people who had nothing to do with the conspiracy, and it wouldn't have been possible in a game where the typical antagonist was a fellow mage/vampire/werewolf or an ephemeral entity.<br /> <br /> 4) Mundane technology goes a long way. Most Deviants don't have any special immunity to getting the s*** kicked out of them with knives, guns, or hypodermic syringes filled with strong sedatives. Even those who are optimized for combat were probably created by organizations that have access to plenty of other military hardware (beyond the Broken themselves). Surveillance is increasingly ubiquitous, and virtually every human activity in modern life leaves a paper trail that can lead enemies to the Deviant's door.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying supernaturally enhanced enemies (beyond Devoted) aren't a thing in Deviant, but I think it's important not to disregard Baselines as antagonists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-04T19:42:23-07:00","id":1316535,"title":"","content":"But will there be improved conspirators?<br /> Not much, but a supernatural quality or a quality of small scientific modification? Nothing that affects your humanity or creates grooves in your soul, of course, small thing.<br /> <br /> Can mad scientists and evil cultists be considered templehouses in the future?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/641-ben-linus","name":"Ben Linus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-05T06:01:53-07:00","id":1316612,"title":"","content":"It was mentioned by Eric Z that Conspiracies would have &quot;Icons&quot;: resources that can 'enhance operatives' temporarily, be it artifacts, temporary treatments, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-05T09:47:13-07:00","id":1316654,"title":"","content":"sorta like endowments in the idea, but the execution will (likely) be very different","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-06T07:10:08-07:00","id":1316815,"title":"","content":"NEW POST: <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/an-introduction-to-clades-deviant-the-renegades/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/an-introducti...the-renegades/</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-06T09:59:47-07:00","id":1316854,"title":"","content":"It's always cool to hear something new on this game. I was surprised at how potent the healing got in the sample variation, but it's a good surprise. Is Scar Power the numerical level of the Scar entangled with a given Variation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty","name":"Minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-06T12:23:15-07:00","id":1316875,"title":"","content":"I would guess that you are correct concerning the Scar Power term used on the post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-06T19:18:31-07:00","id":1316924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Minty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1316854#post1316854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is Scar Power the numerical level of the Scar entangled with a given Variation?</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, no. Every Scar is either Mental, Physical, or Social (some can be two or any of these, but you have to decide which one when you develop the Scar). Every Variation's type matches its entangled Scar's. Scar Power, Scar Finesse, and Scar Resistance refer to the appropriate Power/Finesse/Resistance Attribute of the Scar - Intelligence/Wits/Resolve for Mental, Strength/Dexterity/Stamina for Physical, and Presence/Manipulation/Composure for Social. Because exactly which Attribute a Variation might call upon is based on the entangled Scar, Scar Power will mean Strength if tied to a Physical Scar, Intelligence if entangled with a Mental Scar, or Presence if linked to a Social Scar.<br /> <br /> For example, Glitch is a Mental Scar that causes you to hallucinate or have mental hiccups, and its effects worsen when you spend Willpower (as well as at higher Magnitude). Any Variations entangled with it is a Mental Variation. Whenever the entangled Variation invokes &quot;Scar Power,&quot; it means &quot;Intelligence,&quot; Wits for Scar Finesse, and Resolve for Scar Resistance. On the other hand, if the Scar were Fragility (a Physical Scar), it would instead use Strength for Scar Power, Dexterity for Scar Finesse, and Stamina for Scar Resistance.<br /> <br /> Scar Power/Finesse/Resistance are used as variables in Variation/Scar calculations or are included in relevant dice pools. In broad terms, Scar Power determines the raw potency of a Variation and is often used for things like calculating the maximum Size of objects you can lift with Telekinesis or the damage bonus of your Lash. Scar Finesse measures your degree of control over the Variation and most frequently comes into play when you need to activate or target it. Scar Resistance allows you to mitigate the effects of the Scar, such as to prevent an Involuntary Scar from activating at an inopportune moment or losing control over your body to an Alternate Persona.<br /> <br /> Now, not every Variation/Scar combination will make use of all three Attributes. Some Variations don't use Scar Power (you'll note Rapid Healing doesn't except at Magnitude 5). Most Scars don't allow Scar Resistance rolls to reduce their effects, although some of them do. Even Scar Finesse, which is vital to Controlled, Involuntary, and some Persistent Variations, doesn't come into play for most Persistent Variations (particularly ones with the Perpetual keyword).<br /> <br /> This structure reinforces the idea that the Divergence robs the Remade of something by which they once defined themselves. For example, those with strong Mental Attributes (which incentivize players to assign Mental Scars to them to get the best possible Scar Power/Finesse/Resistance traits) are the ones who labor under curses that reduce the effectiveness of their mental faculties - whether it's a phobia, amnesia, or a Willpower cost for activating their Variation. Picking Scars attached to your tertiary Attributes, on the other hand, only reinforces your existing shortcomings (while also reducing your Variations' mechanical effectiveness). The game's protagonists are indeed Broken.<br /> <br /> It's also slightly harder to &quot;dump stat&quot; within any Attribute category. Resistance is the only one you can easily get away with (by choosing Scars that don't use it, since they're less common than Variations that don't use Power or Finesse), and CofD rules do <i>not</i> naturally incentivize <i>that</i>!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-06T20:16:22-07:00","id":1316927,"title":"","content":"That is a really clever way to reinforce fluff with crunch, of which I am always a fan. I'm a little confused on Persistent vs Perpetual. Could you give an example of something that would be Persistent without being Perpetual, or at least explain why Perpetual is its own keyword when Persistent is already a Variation/Scar type?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty","name":"Minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-06T20:53:37-07:00","id":1316930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Minty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1316927#post1316927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is a really clever way to reinforce fluff with crunch, of which I am always a fan. I'm a little confused on Persistent vs Perpetual. Could you give an example of something that would be Persistent without being Perpetual, or at least explain why Perpetual is its own keyword when Persistent is already a Variation/Scar type?</div> </div> </div> </div>There are two kinds of Persistent Variations - Perpetual ones and Toggled ones. Persistent essentially just means &quot;I can use this whenever I want,&quot; as opposed to Controlled Variations that require an instant action and a roll to activate. Let's take Camouflage. Toggled Camouflage means you can turn invisible whenever you want and without a roll, but you're not <i>always</i> invisible. Perpetual Camouflage means you're <i>always</i> invisible and can't make yourself visible except with a Variation or Adaptation that temporarily suppresses the entire Scar that you've entangled with Camouflage. Some Persistent Variations that make no sense unless &quot;always on&quot; are Perpetual by default (this is the case with Rapid Healing). If you're always gigantic or glowing or have huge fangs (Overt Variations), however, that's a step worse for you than merely being capable of becoming/having those things, so you get a small discount on those Variations if you make them Perpetual. On the other hand, being continually invisible, well, it has its ups and downs, so the mechanic that lets you make Camouflage a Perpetual Variation still works, but it doesn't change the Magnitude &quot;cost&quot; of the Variation. Not all Persistent Variations can be made Perpetual, but most can.<br /> <br /> Perpetual Variations also fall into the &quot;permanent supernatural effect&quot; category on ye olde Clash of Wills chart, so a Perpetual Variation grants you a +5 bonus on Clash of Wills rolls involving it. You are invisible <i>by nature</i>, so even a powerful sorcerer (or other supernatural creature) is going to have a hard time making you visible to the naked eye. Toggled Variations don't enjoy this bonus, but they have the significant advantage of not attracting the constant attention of everyone you encounter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-06T21:16:50-07:00","id":1316936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1316930#post1316930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Perpetual Camouflage means you're <i>always</i> invisible and can't make yourself visible except with a Variation or Adaptation that temporarily suppresses the entire Scar that you've entangled with Camouflage. <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>Jack</i> Griffin. </span></span></span>I found you.<br /> <br /> Just missing Hyde / Dr. Henry Jekyll. Chinese mummies (who came out of conspiracy by Taoist Alchemists to give eternal life) - I kind of know how to make these characters with everything that has been revealed.<br /> <br /> Eveline (RE7) and Dorian Gray (who have no idea how to make them).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/641-ben-linus","name":"Ben Linus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-07T05:49:15-07:00","id":1316969,"title":"","content":"Do Remade add Scar Resistance or Scar Power to Clash of Wills?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty","name":"Minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-07T09:24:26-07:00","id":1316997,"title":"","content":"I would just like you thank you Eric for that post on clades. it did a really good job of explaining how they work and you even zeroed in on mutants since everyone was interested in them","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-07T13:01:20-07:00","id":1317047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Minty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1316969#post1316969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do Remade add Scar Resistance or Scar Power to Clash of Wills?</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m expecting Deviants\u2019 CoW pool to be Acclimation + Variation Rating since that\u2019s the standard for dot-rated powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-07T15:33:37-07:00","id":1317065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1317047#post1317047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I\u2019m expecting Deviants\u2019 CoW pool to be Acclimation + Variation Rating since that\u2019s the standard for dot-rated powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Variations may have Magnitudes but they don't necessarily go from 1 to 5, though I suppose that could also show the power disparity between Deviants and other splats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty","name":"Minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-15T22:03:13-07:00","id":1318799,"title":"","content":"As I apply playtester feedback to the current draft, I'm considering potential topics for another blog entry. Is there anything folks are itching to see? Another Origin or Clade? Some Universal Variations? A few Scars? Something else entirely?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-15T22:24:30-07:00","id":1318801,"title":"","content":"I would love to see some Scars and more Variations. I think I remember from one of the interviews that you said you took command of the whole Variations chapter, so if you could talk a bit about your design philosophy with those when you give examples that would be really cool. I'm also really curious about how conspiracy creation works, and how conspiracies take action in game. Maybe something about your current playtest group would make for a good blog entry? Really, though, I'm interested to see anything you are willing to show off. I've been looking forward to this game for a long time so it's nice to see it gaining steam.<br /> <br /> Oh right, and Forms! We know a little bit about some of them from this thread, but I don't think I've seen anything about Self-Made and Transmissible besides the name, so I'm curious about those ones, too, though for people who haven't read through the thread it might be good just to introduce them as a concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12738,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty","user":"Minty","date":". 06-16-2019, 07:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty","name":"Minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-16T03:33:11-07:00","id":1318826,"title":"","content":"variations and scars would be my top choices. Would to see more of what the Remade are capable of <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. If you go Origin, I'd vote for the Genotypal. If you go Clade, I'd vote for Coactive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-16T04:58:19-07:00","id":1318832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1318799#post1318799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I apply playtester feedback to the current draft, I'm considering potential topics for another blog entry. Is there anything folks are itching to see? Another Origin or Clade? Some Universal Variations? A few Scars? Something else entirely?</div> </div> </div> </div>Could we have sort of like a breakdown of a single, sample character? This would kinda let us see more about Clades, Origins, Variations, <i>and</i> Scars, and also maybe kinda their relationship to their Conspiracy. It wouldn't be a character creation walkthrough, just a breakdown of one already made up.<br /> <br /> Otherwise I'm kinda interested in how the Forms work, especially self-made.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-16T07:10:09-07:00","id":1318853,"title":"","content":"I'd be most interested in Variations, as the freedom they allow while still keeping the power level grounded seems like quite the feat of design.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24176-borne","name":"Borne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24176_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-16T10:24:28-07:00","id":1318888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1318832#post1318832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could we have sort of like a breakdown of a single, sample character? This would kinda let us see more about Clades, Origins, Variations, <i>and</i> Scars, and also maybe kinda their relationship to their Conspiracy. It wouldn't be a character creation walkthrough, just a breakdown of one already made up.<br /> <br /> Otherwise I'm kinda interested in how the Forms work, especially self-made.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seconded, but I\u2019m happy with any of those being better explained as a stand-alone thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-16T10:49:09-07:00","id":1318895,"title":"","content":"Would love to see Variations!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-17T16:10:21-07:00","id":1319145,"title":"","content":"I think I\u2019m more interested in Scars than Variations. We all know how powers work even if Deviant is taking a novel (for CofD) approach to them and can imagine what a lot of them might be, so instead let\u2019s see just how f\u2019ed up a Remade can end up in exchange for being stronger.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-17T16:37:47-07:00","id":1319155,"title":"","content":"Much though I'd love to see another splat writeup or look at Variations, I think Conviction, Loyalty, and/or Stability are the set of mechanical widgets I'm most interested in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-17T18:39:51-07:00","id":1319169,"title":"","content":"I would also like to get a look at Conviction/Loyalty/Stability.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1134-nicias","name":"Nicias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-18T21:38:29-07:00","id":1319403,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the feedback, everyone. I've crafted a few blog entries in response and will submit them shortly. I'm not sure exactly when they'll go up, but I hope you'll like the result once they do! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-19T05:35:10-07:00","id":1319441,"title":"","content":"Thank you Eric!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-19T09:06:41-07:00","id":1319482,"title":"","content":"Links to all previous dev blogs on DtR and to the Onyxpath podcast guest-starring Eric Z are now on the original post for this thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-20T18:26:01-07:00","id":1319840,"title":"","content":"What's the difference between a Deviant and someone augmented through say, the Cheiron organization?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23543-penguinbowler","name":"Penguinbowler","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-20T18:35:46-07:00","id":1319841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penguinbowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1319840#post1319840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's the difference between a Deviant and someone augmented through say, the Cheiron organization?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nutshell, one kept their soul in one piece, one didn't.<br /> <br /> Less Nutshelly, Chieron produces Deviants sometimes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-26T15:04:48-07:00","id":1321044,"title":"","content":"What would a Born Invasive be like?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-26T15:23:20-07:00","id":1321050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1321044#post1321044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What would a Born Invasive be like?</div> </div> </div> </div>While it's certainly not the only way to do it, nanochondria come to mind <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nanochondrion\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nanochondrion</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty","name":"Minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-27T00:12:42-07:00","id":1321120,"title":"","content":"Implanted or 'infected' with something in the womb/at birth.<br /> Invasive parent.<br /> Life-support system.<br /> Nanotech (or analog) seeded in the family line.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-27T00:16:32-07:00","id":1321123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1321120#post1321120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nanotech (or analog) seeded in the family line.</div> </div> </div> </div>I now have the image of nanometer sized clockwork automatons inside someone's bloodstream. I know that's not what you meant, but that's where my brain went.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-01T18:56:59-07:00","id":1321811,"title":"","content":"Deviant is out for manuscript approval!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty","name":"Minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-02T07:24:42-07:00","id":1321875,"title":"","content":"YAHOO!!!!! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I smell a KS sometime later this year <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-08T09:45:52-07:00","id":1322981,"title":"","content":"Not sure if this is solid enough information to warrant going here, but according to Matthew Dawkins in the most recent Onyx Path News (#17), currently Deviant looks to be the most likely CofD game to next get a Kickstarter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12738,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty","user":"Minty","date":". 07-08-2019, 01:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty","name":"Minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-08T12:26:02-07:00","id":1323020,"title":"","content":"If that turns out to be the case, I'd love to see it in a KS before the school year starts <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-08T12:29:19-07:00","id":1323021,"title":"","content":"Huh. Little bit odd. Especially since Hunter2e (presumably) already has its KS art pieces done and ready, unless if they feel Deviant is going to get out of Manuscript Approvals sooner then it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-08T12:33:18-07:00","id":1323024,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it wasn't what I was expecting, either, but I thought I might as well mention it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty","name":"Minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-09T21:38:20-07:00","id":1323371,"title":"","content":"So, this might have been covered elsewhere already, and if so I apologize - does it look like it will be possible to play Deviants of nonhuman origin? I don't mean animals, but more along the lines of, say, and Android or something.<br /> <br /> I can do certain types of Android stories really well with Promethean, but I feel like deviant would fit an entirely different type fairly well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-09T22:08:48-07:00","id":1323376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1323371#post1323371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, this might have been covered elsewhere already, and if so I apologize - does it look like it will be possible to play Deviants of nonhuman origin? I don't mean animals, but more along the lines of, say, and Android or something.<br /> <br /> I can do certain types of Android stories really well with Promethean, but I feel like deviant would fit an entirely different type fairly well.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's beyond the scope of the core. However, I'll make a note of the suggestion for the future. It's important that any &quot;non-human&quot; Deviants still <i>be</i> Deviants (they must still have a damaged soul, human sapience, manipulative appendages, Touchstones, etc.), and I'd want to make sure not to stray too far into Promethean's conceptual/thematic territory. But I've already given a little bit of thought to how I'd do uplifted animals and transferred consciousnesses as Deviants, so some form of android isn't out of the question in a future supplement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-10T03:18:52-07:00","id":1323404,"title":"","content":"I'm wondering how you'd combine animal and robot deviants with the fact that they need souls to become deviants at all.<br /> A Robocop type thing where it's actually a human at the core would be the easiest way to do it, but it's not really fulfilling the premise of a non-human deviant, and it's something I think would be possible for &quot;regular&quot; human deviant characters anyway. I'm thinking either the transfer of a soul from a human, or the incidental creation of a soul in the process. The latter would be extremely interesting but possibly a bit iffy considering that mages supposedly have tried since basically forever and never succeeded. On the other hand it would likely be created &quot;broken&quot; rather than as a fully functional human soul.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-10T20:26:17-07:00","id":1323598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1323404#post1323404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm wondering how you'd combine animal and robot deviants with the fact that they need souls to become deviants at all.<br /> A Robocop type thing where it's actually a human at the core would be the easiest way to do it, but it's not really fulfilling the premise of a non-human deviant, and it's something I think would be possible for &quot;regular&quot; human deviant characters anyway. I'm thinking either the transfer of a soul from a human, or the incidental creation of a soul in the process. The latter would be extremely interesting but possibly a bit iffy considering that mages supposedly have tried since basically forever and never succeeded. On the other hand it would likely be created &quot;broken&quot; rather than as a fully functional human soul.</div> </div> </div> </div>The soul issue is indeed something that would need to be addressed, although a bit of oh-so-mysterious Hand-wavium would probably suffice. As you point out, in cases where these backward Divergences somehow produce souls, they are not whole souls. I can, in fact, see scenarios in which a mage trying to create souls inadvertently creates broken Deviant souls, instead. In truth, I suspect that inhuman anatomy will be much harder to convey mechanically than the general impossibility of creating souls from whole cloth. Deviant isn't Mage, and while the Remade exist in the same world as wizards, vampires, werewolves, and all the rest, its cosmology (such as it is) need not be in perfect alignment with the other lines. In fact, because the Broken are supposed to be the weird, one-off critters of the CofD, I'm mostly okay with them at least occasionally appearing to violate established, fundamental rules (much like God-Machine projects violate known physics, instead relying on arcane physics that are beyond human understanding).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-13T13:40:59-07:00","id":1324260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In fact, because the Broken are supposed to be the weird, one-off critters of the CofD, I'm mostly okay with them at least occasionally appearing to violate established, fundamental rules (much like God-Machine projects violate known physics, instead relying on arcane physics that are beyond human understanding). </div> </div> </div>Deviants can make Cold Iron with magic and measure the blood point confirmed! /s","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24176-borne","name":"Borne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24176_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-13T22:40:42-07:00","id":1324357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Borne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1324260#post1324260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Deviants can make Cold Iron with magic and measure the blood point confirmed! /s</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, Mages can make Siderite, which acts as cold iron against entities with that bane, with magic; <i>Hone the Perfected Form</i> is Matter 3 and one point of mana.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":2757,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","user":"proindrakenzol","date":". 07-14-2019, 01:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-14T05:10:57-07:00","id":1324418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Borne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1324260#post1324260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Deviants can make Cold Iron with magic...</div> </div> </div> </div>Hidden Compartments 3 for a knife, 4 for a sword*. Not sure I can help you with measuring the blood point, since I believe that's more a mechanical unit than an in-world one (unlike Mana, which is both).<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">* Subject to Storyteller approval. May or may not literally involve magic, depending on flavoring. Certain additional restrictions may apply.</span><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-19T17:18:05-07:00","id":1326134,"title":"","content":"Hey guys, new here to the forums and I LOVE how Deviant is shaping up. I have a few questions/thoughts though. . .<br /> <br /> 1. in a narrative sense, why are Deviants &quot;less powerful&quot; than say other major templets. I remember it being stated that in terms of raw spiritual power, they are above lesser templates like Ghouls and Hunters but below the fully formed ones like Mage or Vampire.<br /> <br /> 2. How numerous are the Broken? it's my theory that because Deviant's have to be &quot;built&quot; or made through external sources with with a lot or a little manpower, and that each Broken is pretty much unique, other than those conspiracies that &quot;mass create&quot; them, I would venture to guess that they number a little bit more than Prometheans (my other favorite game line) but far less than the rest of the supernatural citizens like Changelings or even Mummies. <br /> <br /> 3. How organized are the Renegades as opposed to the Devoted? Being Devoted means you have resources and an organization at your back, being Renegade means you're mostly alone other than your cohorts. Again Promethean comes to mind and I would like to see a kind of rudimentary underground messaging system used specifically by Renegades with letters, sign posts, and other markers but not nearly as organized like Mages or Vampires and their undead society. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25493-mr-scissors","name":"Mr.Scissors","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-19T18:35:16-07:00","id":1326143,"title":"","content":"I can't answer with any authority, but my read from the information available is that:<br /> <br /> 1. For the most part the antagonists in a Deviant game are going to be groups of ordinary humans, and giving the Remade as much general power as other splats would take away from how effective a threat baselines can be. There's not a whole lot mortals can do if you can just hop into the Hedge or take on another appearance at the drop of a hat. Also, it seems like the Broken can be plenty powerful on an individual basis, but that means accepting more drawbacks than other splats would have. When a Vampire learns a new dot of a Discipline, that's it. In order for a Deviant to get a new Variation they have to have a Scar as well.<br /> <br /> 2. Probably not a lot! We don't have a lot of information on this, but I think your guess is probably fairly close to what we will see in the book. Deviants are all one-offs, so I imagine that even powerful conspiracies that are devoted to &quot;mass producing&quot; them have significantly more failures than successes.<br /> <br /> 3. I have not heard anything to make me think that there are any greater Renegade social structures than individual cohorts. Personally I don't think it's likely that they even have anything like the signs Prometheans leave for each other because they don't have anything like Azoth to link them together.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty","name":"Minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-22T20:07:58-07:00","id":1326860,"title":"","content":"Deviant is in art direction for the Kickstarter","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty","name":"Minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-23T11:47:07-07:00","id":1327026,"title":"","content":"Another few questions<br /> <br /> - Regarding Renegades and their ability to communicate with each other. The Conspiracies in the game line appear to all be in connection or at least in some sort of pecking order with one another through the &quot;Web of Pain&quot;. Does that mean in some ways the game is reversed where as the Devoted have the &quot;society&quot; and The Renegades have no way to pass info (even in the limited ways like the Created)? <br /> <br /> -Do Deviant's have a way or recognizing each other like the Predator's Tain for Vampires or Numbus for Mages. There has to be a way for Renegades to organize themselves into Cohorts if they don't because not all Deviant's have physical scars. <br /> <br /> - Regarding their Power stat ACCLIMATION, it was stated that only certain Broken get this (those who volunteered or wanted to become a Deviant)? That' mean's only two of the 5 Clades have this extra Supernatural Tolerance?<br /> <br /> \u200b-Lastly, Does growing in Acclimation have other benefits like raising a Variation's Magnitude without needing an accompanying Scar or even perhaps removing a Scar point from a Variation? <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25493-mr-scissors","name":"Mr.Scissors","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-23T11:55:25-07:00","id":1327028,"title":"","content":"For the &quot;low-powered&quot; thing, I wonder also if it has to do with the lack of &quot;inherent&quot; drawbacks that an average Remade (if there is such a thing) has. Vampires have obvious weaknesses and restrictions- you can't go out in daytime, fire deals aggravated damage, plus any specific banes you've got. Werewolves are harmed by silver, and have a physiological and spiritual need to hunt that forces them into certain behaviors. Demons can't use their powers without risking the attentions of the God-Machine. Even Mages, once you strip their spells away, are &quot;only human.&quot;<br /> <br /> A Remade might be &quot;human, but can occasionally look through a wall&quot; or &quot;literally a god in a human-shaped mask.&quot; So they operate on a sliding scale, one that can equal a mortals among mortals game, a minor superpowers vampires game, or a world-shredding mage game. And each step comes with increasing drawbacks to balance the scales. A low-level Deviant can't destroy a city, but they also can live a mostly normal life. And since each one is unique, the players get to design their own &quot;inherent drawbacks&quot; that fit the theme of their character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12970-gellydog","name":"Gellydog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12970_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-23T12:00:30-07:00","id":1327031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.Scissors</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1327026#post1327026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Regarding their Power stat ACCLIMATION, it was stated that only certain Broken get this (those who volunteered or wanted to become a Deviant)? That' mean's only two of the 5 Clades have this extra Supernatural Tolerance?</div> </div> </div> </div>Where did you hear this? I haven't seen anything like that before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty","name":"Minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-23T17:46:19-07:00","id":1327096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Minty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1327031#post1327031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where did you hear this? I haven't seen anything like that before.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought I read that somewhere in this thread that only certain Deviant's get this Power setting. I might be mistaken. That said, other than add supernatural tolerance, does Acclimation have any other mechanical benefits?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25493-mr-scissors","name":"Mr.Scissors","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-23T18:27:26-07:00","id":1327105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.Scissors</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1327096#post1327096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I thought I read that somewhere in this thread that only certain Deviant's get this Power setting. I might be mistaken. That said, other than add supernatural tolerance, does Acclimation have any other mechanical benefits?</div> </div> </div> </div>We know it has something to do with the size of your Stability track, and we know that it does more than just that, and that's about all we know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty","name":"Minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-23T19:27:58-07:00","id":1327114,"title":"","content":"and acclimation is for all deviants (though now you make me doubt...sigh)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-23T22:00:58-07:00","id":1327135,"title":"","content":"A few questions today. I'll see if I can answer a few.<br /> <br /> Renegades are not naturally equipped to form complex societies. Deviants don't have a universal aura that lets them readily identify each other, nor a special connection via something like Pyros. Unseen Sense (Deviants) can help in meeting other Deviants, as can setting your sights on the same target of vengeance (conspiracies tend to make multiple Renegades their enemies). I'm open to the possibility of larger organizations of Renegades, but I haven't come up with a good justification, yet.<br /> <br /> Conspiracies in the Web of Pain aren't all good chums. Some of them oppose each other violently, and others don't have compatible interests. But yes, they do tend to be interconnected, which means Devoted are more likely to have contact with other Devoted.<br /> <br /> Acclimation starts at 0 but can be increased as high as 5 during play. As with other power stats, this carries a pretty high Experiences cost. In addition, you can only increase Acclimation when your Instability is under control. Acclimation feeds into Stability, Clash of Wills, Supernatural Tolerance, activating Controlled Variations, targeting Directed Variations (and certain other Variations), and resisting Involuntary Variations. So, not quite as multifunctional as other power stats, but still pretty useful.<br /> <br /> Regarding low-powered-ness, it's sort of the reverse of what Gellydog mentions. Deviants don't get a bunch of inherent advantages by virtue of being Remade - no Mage Sight, undead resistance to bullets, spending fuel to heal or rise from the dead, etc. At low Threat Level, they're just a little more potent than Blue Book mortals. At mid-to-high Threat Level, they can possess specific capabilities that are beyond what a newly created character in most other gamelines can boast. But even at a high initial Threat Level and with a good ration of Experiences, they're never going to rival the reality-shredding might of an experienced mage or demon. Nor can they easily load up on dozens of dots of Disciplines/Gifts/Contracts/Haunts/etc., because Variations come with new Scars. Additionally, there is no &quot;fuel stat,&quot; which means Broken never get to the point where they have virtually unlimited &quot;MP&quot; with which to power a stream of their favorite powers. Those Scars that only carry a price when you activate one of the entangled Variations (as opposed to ones that mark you even when the Variations are inactive) burn away terribly finite resources like Willpower, health, or Stability.<br /> <br /> It's true that in cases where Instability gets wildly out of control and causes the Deviant to destabilize completely, the Remade's Variations can temporarily exceed their normal limits, but this is to a demon Going Loud what a guy with a suicide vest is to a Marine lobbing a grenade at an enemy position. Going Loud is a potent weapon, deployed voluntarily, if as something of a last resort due to its risks and costs. The onset of the End Stage Condition isn't something a Deviant can carefully time to maximize damage, however. It merely makes the Broken a ticking time bomb that might yet achieve one last act before he explodes. Most of the time, the explosion happens some place where it hurts lots of innocent bystanders, instead, serving only to reinforce the game's revenge tragedy themes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-24T06:51:02-07:00","id":1327177,"title":"","content":"This might not be something you can talk about at present, but I've been wondering something about entangling Variations with Scars. Let's say, for example, that you have three Magnitudes of Rapid Healing entangled with a Scar, and that Scar cannot increase in severity. If you want to increase Rapid Healing to four Magnitudes would you be able to entangle it with a different Scar, or would you be stuck at three? Or can all Scars handle up to five Magnitudes of a Variation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty","name":"Minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-24T07:47:04-07:00","id":1327183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Minty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1327177#post1327177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This might not be something you can talk about at present, but I've been wondering something about entangling Variations with Scars. Let's say, for example, that you have three Magnitudes of Rapid Healing entangled with a Scar, and that Scar cannot increase in severity. If you want to increase Rapid Healing to four Magnitudes would you be able to entangle it with a different Scar, or would you be stuck at three? Or can all Scars handle up to five Magnitudes of a Variation?</div> </div> </div> </div>Great question! Worsening a Scar happens by taking on medium or major Instability in the last five boxes of your Stability track. Assuming the entangled Scar has a 4+ Magnitude version (most do, but not all), you can choose to increase the Magnitude of Rapid Healing when Instability causes its Scar to increase in Magnitude. If you do that, then the Magnitude increase of that Scar is permanent (normally, increases to a Scar's Magnitude due to Instability are temporary, fading when the Instability heals).<br /> <br /> And if the Scar doesn't normally go to Magnitude 4? In that case, there are Deviations, which are add-ons that increase (or, rarely, decrease) the effective Magnitude of a Scar (or Variation). Partially, Deviations allow you to customize or tweak a Scar so that it is more in keeping with your character concept, or to convey an effect that just isn't scalable enough to work as a standalone Scar. But they also exist to deal with the very question you're asking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-24T08:12:40-07:00","id":1327185,"title":"","content":"That is all really exciting to hear. Thank you for taking the time to answer my question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty","name":"Minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-24T13:13:10-07:00","id":1327241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1327135#post1327135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A few questions today. I'll see if I can answer a few.<br /> <br /> Renegades are not naturally equipped to form complex societies. Deviants don't have a universal aura that lets them readily identify each other, nor a special connection via something like Pyros. Unseen Sense (Deviants) can help in meeting other Deviants, as can setting your sights on the same target of vengeance (conspiracies tend to make multiple Renegades their enemies). I'm open to the possibility of larger organizations of Renegades, but I haven't come up with a good justification, yet.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Same reason as changelings. The Lost may come from very different Domains, under very different Keepers and with very different body modifications (kiths). But they are all broken beyond recognition, they all know their formers captors want them back and that their only chance of keeping their freedom and sanity is to cooperate forming groups and societies of mutual support.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2411,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","user":"Raistlin","date":". 07-24-2019, 07:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-24T14:47:53-07:00","id":1327265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1327135#post1327135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding low-powered-ness, it's sort of the reverse of what Gellydog mentions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oops! Haha. Thanks for the explanation!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12970-gellydog","name":"Gellydog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12970_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-24T14:55:41-07:00","id":1327268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1327135#post1327135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unseen Sense (Deviants) can help in meeting other Deviants</div> </div> </div> </div>This is an interesting aside. Unseen Sense is normally off limits to supernatural templates. Is this an indication that Deviants can gain these Supernatural Merits in some form (possibly emulated as Variations), or is Unseen Sense (Deviants) an exception for them, or something else?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-24T16:40:01-07:00","id":1327290,"title":"","content":"@Gellydog: No harm. Just wanted to clarify. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar522_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"522\" data-vbnamecard=\"522\">Stupid Loserman</a>: CofD core has that language, yes, so I might yet get overruled on that basis (we haven't hit editing, yet), but whether or not it gets called Unseen Sense or not, &quot;Deviants Detecting Deviants&quot; is likely to be a low-cost Merit, rather than a Variation or universal ability.<br /> <br /> (Personally, I've always considered that rule less about &quot;but a vampire with Unseen Sense (God-Machine) would be too powerful!&quot; than about &quot;once you're a vampire, 95% of Supernatural Merits carry a huge cost relative to what you could get by purchasing Disciplines, so here's an easy excuse to refund all that wasted XP.&quot; And that differential is even more obvious for, say, mages, where 4 XP gets you the equivalent of several 3-5 dot Supernatural Merits. That gap is much smaller for the Remade. Deviants aren't likely to invest in the Telekinesis Merit when they could have its considerably more potent Variation version, but something like 1 XP for an Unseen Sense as a crude Deviant detector? Seems like a reasonable investment to me.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-24T17:07:03-07:00","id":1327295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1327290#post1327290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Gellydog: No harm. Just wanted to clarify. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span>: CofD core has that language, yes, so I might yet get overruled on that basis (we haven't hit editing, yet), but whether or not it gets called Unseen Sense or not, &amp;quot;Deviants Detecting Deviants&amp;quot; is likely to be a low-cost Merit, rather than a Variation or universal ability.<br /> <br /> (Personally, I've always considered that rule less about &amp;quot;but a vampire with Unseen Sense (God-Machine) would be too powerful!&amp;quot; than about &amp;quot;once you're a vampire, 95% of Supernatural Merits carry a huge cost relative to what you could get by purchasing Disciplines, so here's an easy excuse to refund all that wasted XP.&amp;quot; And that differential is even more obvious for, say, mages, where 4 XP gets you the equivalent of several 3-5 dot Supernatural Merits. That gap is much smaller for the Remade. Deviants aren't likely to invest in the Telekinesis Merit when they could have its considerably more potent Variation version, but something like 1 XP for an Unseen Sense as a crude Deviant detector? Seems like a reasonable investment to me.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Would you mind telling me more about Autourgics? What are they like? What kind of person would want to be Remade while fully understanding what a Deviant is?<br /> Knowing their origins factor would be nice","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-24T17:48:41-07:00","id":1327304,"title":"","content":"and to add on, is being an autourgic renegade like being an integrator from Demon?<br /> <br /> basically no one trusts you because you. in a way, sympathize with the enemy","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-24T17:50:54-07:00","id":1327307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1327295#post1327295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Would you mind telling me more about Autourgics? What are they like? What kind of person would want to be Remade while fully understanding what a Deviant is?<br /> Knowing their origins factor would be nice</div> </div> </div> </div>Origin factor is in the OP: +1 Loyalty; +1 Mag of Overt Variation<br /> <br /> Sample character concepts include self-experimenting scientist, elite athlete, spiritual seeker, transhuman ideologue, and patriotic volunteer. Although being one of the Elect doesn't mean you have a full understanding of what the Divergence means, no one told you that your were signing up for a diet program, or an experimental cancer treatment, or a test of your memory. You knew it would remake you, and your Progenitor probably even went over the potential side-effects with you before you signed on the dotted line, entered the horrifying sci-fi chamber, spent the night in the forbidden temple, or whatever. But whether you accepted the Divergence out of a sense of duty or altruism, or whether you wanted something that would let you distinguish yourself among your peers even if it meant a shorter lifespan (a sort of &quot;super-steroid&quot; for athletes or Nobel-prize-winning intelligence for scientists), you made a calculated decision. You might come to <i>regret</i> that decision, but it was still a decision you made.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-24T18:06:18-07:00","id":1327312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1327307#post1327307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Origin factor is in the OP: +1 Loyalty; +1 Mag of Overt Variation<br /> <br /> Sample character concepts include self-experimenting scientist, elite athlete, spiritual seeker, transhuman ideologue, and patriotic volunteer. Although being one of the Elect doesn't mean you have a full understanding of what the Divergence means, no one told you that your were signing up for a diet program, or an experimental cancer treatment, or a test of your memory. You knew it would remake you, and your Progenitor probably even went over the potential side-effects with you before you signed on the dotted line, entered the horrifying sci-fi chamber, spent the night in the forbidden temple, or whatever. But whether you accepted the Divergence out of a sense of duty or altruism, or whether you wanted something that would let you distinguish yourself among your peers even if it meant a shorter lifespan (a sort of &amp;quot;super-steroid&amp;quot; for athletes or Nobel-prize-winning intelligence for scientists), you made a calculated decision. You might come to <i>regret</i> that decision, but it was still a decision you made.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ooh,forbidden temple. May I ask are there any big difference between those who are remade by magic and those who are remade by science?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24222-acopiltaczet","name":"Acopiltaczet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24222_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-24T18:11:44-07:00","id":1327314,"title":"","content":"Building on that,is there a list of things that are used to make Deviants? Both magical and scientifically, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1094\" data-vbnamecard=\"1094\">Eric Zawadzki</a> ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-24T18:43:40-07:00","id":1327325,"title":"","content":"A while back you mentioned that Invasive Variations tend to turn you into a swiss army knife - floating merit and skill points, storage compartments, that sort of thing. Do any of the other clades' Variations have a mechanical tendency like this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty","name":"Minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-24T19:00:36-07:00","id":1327329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Minty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1327325#post1327325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A while back you mentioned that Invasive Variations tend to turn you into a swiss army knife - floating merit and skill points, storage compartments, that sort of thing. Do any of the other clades' Variations have a mechanical tendency like this?</div> </div> </div> </div>not sure if this could answer your question, but if you mean they each have a sorta &quot;niche&quot; then yeah<br /> <br /> I only know mutants, but they are considered the VERY adaptable mutant","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-24T19:50:46-07:00","id":1327339,"title":"","content":"RE Renegade society: Perhaps, although Conviction and Loyalty do not make for a particularly stable social order.<br /> <br /> RE Divergence methodologies: There will never be a complete list of things that can be used to trigger Divergence. There are as many ways as you can imagine, which is kind of the point of Remade. And the difference between super-science Broken and mystical ones is more a matter of flavor and trappings than mechanical effect (beyond the effects of Clade).<br /> <br /> RE Adaptability: Invasive Variations tend to be very Swiss army knife, while one of their Adaptations makes them highly durable. Almost mirroring this, Mutants have an Adaptation that makes them exceptionally adaptable, while their Clade Variations often make them more durable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-24T19:52:35-07:00","id":1327340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1327339#post1327339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">RE Renegade society: Perhaps, although Conviction and Loyalty do not make for a particularly stable social order.<br /> <br /> RE Divergence methodologies: There will never be a complete list of things that can be used to trigger Divergence. There are as many ways as you can imagine, which is kind of the point of Remade. And the difference between super-science Broken and mystical ones is more a matter of flavor and trappings than mechanical effect (beyond the effects of Clade).<br /> <br /> RE Adaptability: Invasive Variations tend to be very Swiss army knife, while one of their Adaptations makes them highly durable. Almost mirroring this, Mutants have an Adaptation that makes them exceptionally adaptable, while their Clade Variations often make them more durable.</div> </div> </div> </div>thanks Eric","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-24T22:08:33-07:00","id":1327355,"title":"","content":"I want to thank everyone for answering my questions, I'm already loving this game line!<br /> <br /> Anyway, I want to go just a bit further into Deviant &quot;Society&quot;&quot; or the basic makings of a cohort. <br /> <br /> <br /> The thing is, unless you're one of the Devoted, or part of a conspiracy that makes multiple Broken, there is no way, after escaping your captors, of you knowing that there are other Remade &quot;like&quot; you out there. So how would enough Renegades come together to make a cohort? I guess if two or more Renegades were targeting the same Conspiracy, then you would team up. But that is very unlikely based on what I've gathered so far. It sounds like the Broken, like the Created, are some of the rarest major game line supernatural templets. So it would seem that there would be another way for those Broken who aren't Devoted to be able to rat least recognize each other outside of their confines. So what can bring the Broken together?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25493-mr-scissors","name":"Mr.Scissors","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-25T06:14:50-07:00","id":1327401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.Scissors</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1327355#post1327355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want to thank everyone for answering my questions, I'm already loving this game line!<br /> <br /> Anyway, I want to go just a bit further into Deviant &quot;Society&quot;&quot; or the basic makings of a cohort.<br /> <br /> <br /> The thing is, unless you're one of the Devoted, or part of a conspiracy that makes multiple Broken, there is no way, after escaping your captors, of you knowing that there are other Remade &quot;like&quot; you out there. So how would enough Renegades come together to make a cohort? I guess if two or more Renegades were targeting the same Conspiracy, then you would team up. But that is very unlikely based on what I've gathered so far. It sounds like the Broken, like the Created, are some of the rarest major game line supernatural templets. So it would seem that there would be another way for those Broken who aren't Devoted to be able to rat least recognize each other outside of their confines. So what can bring the Broken together?</div> </div> </div> </div>I've always felt that a splat should be as common or as rare as your chronicle demands. That said, I don't think Deviants (or even just Renegades) are as rare as Prometheans. You're dealing with a template that can occur by accidentally coming into contact with supernatural phenomena in just the right context, and some conspiracies are capable of &quot;mass-producing&quot; Remade (albeit not without defects and lots of casualties). That doesn't give me the sense that they're exceptionally rare. I also get the sense that they tend to clump in areas where Progenitor conspiracies operate, so where there is one Renegade, there are likely quite a number of others. An especially sloppy conspiracy with a high turnover rate might generate enough Renegades that they create their own local society of Broken (cohorts are usually several Renegades created by the same conspiracy and united in vengeance against it). &quot;Larger Renegade society&quot; isn't going to be addressed in the core, but it's probably worth exploring in a later supplement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-25T07:03:01-07:00","id":1327410,"title":"","content":"I know this is a dumb question but what part of the the beast kinship chart are deviants on? Descended from the Dark mother, Fundamentally Human, or Kinship not Apply? I'm Guessing Descended, but i could see a case for fundementally human.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23543-penguinbowler","name":"Penguinbowler","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-25T07:30:19-07:00","id":1327420,"title":"","content":"Maybe it depends on your power level. Low level would be fundamentally human, but medium to high power levels would be descended?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-25T17:13:48-07:00","id":1327503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penguinbowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1327410#post1327410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know this is a dumb question but what part of the the beast kinship chart are deviants on? Descended from the Dark mother, Fundamentally Human, or Kinship not Apply? I'm Guessing Descended, but i could see a case for fundementally human.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not the Beast developer, so I don't feel like I can answer this question with anything approaching authority. However, given Deviant's thematic interest in Divergence as an experience that divorces the victim from the rest of humanity, I could have a whole lot of fun using the Children as a way of drawing attention to that loss - almost &quot;Darth Vader tempting Luke with the Dark Side of the Force&quot; levels of doing so. For example, maybe it as Robert D suggests, but it's a case where a Beast starts out regarding you as merely fundamentally human but later considers you descended from the Dark Mother as a way of the story telling you that you've strayed further from humanity than even mere Divergence caused. Or maybe it depends on Stability, with greater Instability increasing your perceived closeness with the Dark Mother. Or Renegade vs. Devoted. Such a delicious opportunity to reinforce the characters' sense of alienation and loss, really.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-25T17:56:15-07:00","id":1327508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1327503#post1327503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not the Beast developer, so I don't feel like I can answer this question with anything approaching authority. However, given Deviant's thematic interest in Divergence as an experience that divorces the victim from the rest of humanity, I could have a whole lot of fun using the Children as a way of drawing attention to that loss - almost &quot;Darth Vader tempting Luke with the Dark Side of the Force&quot; levels of doing so. For example, maybe it as Robert D suggests, but it's a case where a Beast starts out regarding you as merely fundamentally human but later considers you descended from the Dark Mother as a way of the story telling you that you've strayed further from humanity than even mere Divergence caused. Or maybe it depends on Stability, with greater Instability increasing your perceived closeness with the Dark Mother. Or Renegade vs. Devoted. Such a delicious opportunity to reinforce the characters' sense of alienation and loss, really.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really like the idea of Beasts being a corruptive influence to deviants. while they can often really help monsters come to terms with themselves, they also act like they know more than they really do. a deviant is just a time bomb with a shortened detonation time with a beast thinking it's right to encourage it to be monstrous","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","user":"Primordial newcomer","date":". 07-26-2019, 12:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-26T10:36:46-07:00","id":1327606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1327401#post1327401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also get the sense that they tend to clump in areas where Progenitor conspiracies operate, so where there is one Renegade, there are likely quite a number of others. An especially sloppy conspiracy with a high turnover rate might generate enough Renegades that they create their own local society of Brokent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for answering my questions, I really appreciate it! This kind of make's sense, the larger Conspiracies would more likely &quot;attract&quot; Renegades due to their need to be in opposition towards a negative force (or what the Renegade in question considers &quot;negative&quot; or evil). In that way, Deviants aren't linked supernaturally like the Predator's Taint or a Werewolf's sent but more psychologically linked due to their shared mental traits. <br /> <br /> That being said, I kinda feel that despite whatever Clade a Deviant belongs to the same effect happen to their metaphysical soul, it cracks. All Remade souls are broken despite whatever was done to them. And with all Deviants sharing the same spiritual condition as well as certain psychological changes, all have Loyalty and Convictions due to their diminished sense of self identity, than there must be a way for Deviants, if they were to pass each other on the street say, that they would at least feel a inkling of a &quot;kindrid spirit&quot; or someone with a recognizable spiritual condition. That way, it would be easier for any Renegade to form some sort of bond or become cohorts even if there wasn't a major Conspiracy in the given area to which multiple Renegades would be drawn to. <br /> <br /> But this is just my thought on the matter. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25493-mr-scissors","name":"Mr.Scissors","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-27T05:49:22-07:00","id":1327725,"title":"","content":"I don't particularly like the idea of Deviants having some sort of easily recognizable tag, as it lessens their diversity. Deviants stop being these weird, one of a kind anomalies and become a clearly cohesive in-universe group. They come together, as rejects and whatnots with shared experiences and goals. They share symptoms, but outside of the broken-soul thing, nothing magically links a half-insect mutant with a psychic who reached too far into the void.There's enough splats like that already. Could a psychic Remade happen to pick up on thoughts they relate to in another like them? Sure, absolutely. Do Deviants have a metaphysical SKU floating above their heads or a vampire-style Predatory Aura? I rather hope not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24176-borne","name":"Borne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24176_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-27T06:12:44-07:00","id":1327729,"title":"","content":"If anything, Deviants should have *less* ability to detect each other than everyone else around them. Their innate connection to the rest of humanity is gone, they feel nothing but rage and desperate obsession with their fixations so they can feel anything. Other humans get a strange vibe from Deviants because they lack the oneness that the humans take for granted with each other, but Deviants just pass each other without feeling anything, just like their connection with the rest of humanity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-28T13:37:06-07:00","id":1327956,"title":"","content":"It would seem based on what I'm reading that out of all the major templets, that Deviant's might just be the loneliest out of all the supernaturals. In fact, I wouldn't be surprised that a Deviant, Devoted or Renegade (but most likely Renegade), could go about their entire lives not knowing others like themselves, or even the supernatural world beyond themselves exist. Interesting to consider such an isolated character. <br /> <br /> Anyway, I have another question regarding Scars and Variation entanglements. I also read on this forum that a single Scar can entangle multiple Variations. So for example, I have a level 4 Scar, and I have three Variations, one at level 3 and two at level 2. Would something like that work out? If a single Scar can hold several abilities as long as their Magnitude doesn't exceed that Scar level, that could help lesson the drawbacks for said Variations if the Deviant had only one Scar to contend with rather a Scar for EACH Variation. Is this somewhat correct?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25493-mr-scissors","name":"Mr.Scissors","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-28T13:51:37-07:00","id":1327957,"title":"","content":"Personally, after a ton of games about hyper-local, often fairly retro gatherings of the occult, and looking at the kind of troubled-rebels-chasing-conspiracies vibe of Deviants, I would both want and expect Deviant society to be more modern and internet-focused. They don't find each other because they have a vibe; they find each other because they're looking for the same things, and the internet brings together tiny common interest groups. Not so much local hierarchies built around resources and mutual defense, but ad-hoc networks based around overlapping spites, research needs, tactical innovations, and shared enemies. Then, secondarily, they realize they can also trade advice about the &quot;just trying to get by&quot; part of their lives.<br /> <br /> This would also resonate with some of the game's subtexts without mapping to them directly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1134-nicias","user":"Nicias","date":". 07-28-2019, 04:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1134-nicias","name":"Nicias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-29T18:46:23-07:00","id":1328199,"title":"","content":"DEVIANT THE RENEGADES WILL BE THE NEXT KS IM SO HAPPY","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-29T19:55:36-07:00","id":1328211,"title":"","content":"THE TIME HAS COME! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-29T20:46:04-07:00","id":1328216,"title":"","content":"...more importantly, a launch window: late August or September 2019.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-29T20:51:39-07:00","id":1328217,"title":"","content":"I do hope it's more like mid- to late- August 2019. I've been chomping at the bit to see the manuscript ever since the first dev blogs went up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-01T18:24:38-07:00","id":1328848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1327339#post1327339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">RE Renegade society: Perhaps, although Conviction and Loyalty do not make for a particularly stable social order.<br /> <br /> RE Divergence methodologies: There will never be a complete list of things that can be used to trigger Divergence. There are as many ways as you can imagine, which is kind of the point of Remade. And the difference between super-science Broken and mystical ones is more a matter of flavor and trappings than mechanical effect (beyond the effects of Clade).<br /> <br /> RE Adaptability: Invasive Variations tend to be very Swiss army knife, while one of their Adaptations makes them highly durable. Almost mirroring this, Mutants have an Adaptation that makes them exceptionally adaptable, while their Clade Variations often make them more durable.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have a few more questions<br /> Is there a guide to create new Forms on the corebook?<br /> What is a toggled variation? I could swear I saw that term before.<br /> Could you tell me more about the Role of Deviants in the Golden Age of Science Fiction and Enlightenment Dark eras?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-01T20:29:02-07:00","id":1328864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1328848#post1328848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have a few more questions<br /> Is there a guide to create new Forms on the corebook?<br /> What is a toggled variation? I could swear I saw that term before.<br /> Could you tell me more about the Role of Deviants in the Golden Age of Science Fiction and Enlightenment Dark eras?</div> </div> </div> </div>1. No. Perhaps in a future supplement, although it would be a bit tricky.<br /> 2. Toggled is the opposite of Perpetual. It describes a Persistent Variation that isn't active until the Deviant &quot;turns it on,&quot; after which it lasts until the end of the scene. For example, Gigantic is usually Toggled, which means you can grow to huge sizes. If it's Perpetual, it means you're <i>always</i> huge.<br /> 3. I'm going to demure on material in Dark Eras and Contagion Chronicle, for now. They're not my projects to spoil. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-01T22:29:57-07:00","id":1328881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1328864#post1328864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1. No. Perhaps in a future supplement, although it would be a bit tricky.<br /> 2. Toggled is the opposite of Perpetual. It describes a Persistent Variation that isn't active until the Deviant &amp;quot;turns it on,&amp;quot; after which it lasts until the end of the scene. For example, Gigantic is usually Toggled, which means you can grow to huge sizes. If it's Perpetual, it means you're <i>always</i> huge.<br /> 3. I'm going to demure on material in Dark Eras and Contagion Chronicle, for now. They're not my projects to spoil. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>hmm, do toggled variations carry even worse scars than persistent variations?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-02T03:37:04-07:00","id":1328914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1328864#post1328864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1. No. Perhaps in a future supplement, although it would be a bit tricky.<br /> 2. Toggled is the opposite of Perpetual. It describes a Persistent Variation that isn't active until the Deviant &amp;quot;turns it on,&amp;quot; after which it lasts until the end of the scene. For example, Gigantic is usually Toggled, which means you can grow to huge sizes. If it's Perpetual, it means you're <i>always</i> huge.<br /> 3. I'm going to demure on material in Dark Eras and Contagion Chronicle, for now. They're not my projects to spoil. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I asked this a while back and, while some people made some suggestions, I was wondering what kind of concept represents or is represented by a Born Invasive?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-02T20:50:57-07:00","id":1329052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1328881#post1328881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> hmm, do toggled variations carry even worse scars than persistent variations?</div> </div> </div> </div>It depends on whether the Variation is Subtle or Overt. Most Subtle Variations, when Persistent, are Perpetual by default. There's literally no downside to having them on all the time, so why complicate things for the troupe? For Overt Variations (and the few exceptions among Subtle Variations), there's the Relentless Variation Scar, which lets you change a Toggled Persistent Variation into a Perpetual Persistent Variation. This increases the effective Magnitude of a secondary Scar by 1 if it affects an Overt Variation (since not being able to turn these off attracts conspiracy attention), but it doesn't change the effective Magnitude of a secondary Scar if the Variation is Subtle. Being permanently invisible has its ups and downs, for example, but it doesn't cause nearly as many problems as being inescapably Size 10.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1328914#post1328914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I asked this a while back and, while some people made some suggestions, I was wondering what kind of concept represents or is represented by a Born Invasive?</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought the suggestions were pretty spot-on. Nanotech is probably the easiest to grok. Another option would be someone genetically engineered (or predestined) to merge with or use a powerful artifact or alien tech - possibly groomed from birth for the future obligation. Evangelion comes to mind in that you can't just stick any kid in the giant robot; it needs to be one with just the right physiological and psychological attributes. You are the seventh son of a seventh son, and so one day, as a young man, you wake up with a sorcerer's ring on your finger and the power to command angels and banish devils from the Earth; the conspiracy didn't give you your power, in this case, although they may have sought you out as a child so they could bring you into the fold once the inevitable Divergence happened.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-03T12:35:35-07:00","id":1329145,"title":"","content":"Can Deviations allow for effective Magnitude below 1 or above 5 if some effect would push a Variation or Scar that low or high?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty","name":"Minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-03T12:54:53-07:00","id":1329149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Minty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1329145#post1329145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can Deviations allow for effective Magnitude below 1 or above 5 if some effect would push a Variation or Scar that low or high?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. You can't apply a Deviation that would decrease Magnitude below 1 or increase it above 5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-03T13:16:47-07:00","id":1329153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1291157#post1291157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That sounds Coactive to me, but again, it depends on the result. Was the transformation such that the Deviant wound up wielding powers typically attributed to that deity by drawing on his spiritual connection to the entity? Especially if many of his Variations are typical of that Clade? Coactive. If not? Possibly another Clade.</div> </div> </div> </div>What level of Magnitude would you give to a variation allowed the Deviant bring a soul back from the Underworld? and whats sample Scars could be associated with it..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-03T13:17:53-07:00","id":1329154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1329149#post1329149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No. You can't apply a Deviation that would decrease Magnitude below 1 or increase it above 5.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would it also be safe to assume that things are set up in such a way that, for example, the Relentless Variation Scar could not end up with a secondary Scar that was already at Magnitude 5 that was entangled to an Overt Variation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty","name":"Minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-04T11:46:58-07:00","id":1329309,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4621_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4621\" data-vbnamecard=\"4621\">Nicolas Milioni</a>: Deviant doesn't include the ephemeral entities rules in its core, so an Orpheus-style jaunt into the Underworld isn't likely. If you're talking about resurrecting the dead, though, that's Magnitude 5 (albeit with limits). As to the question about Scars, virtually any Scar can be entangled with any Variation, as long as the Variation's Magnitude is equal to or less than the Magnitude of the Scar. So a Magnitude 5 Variation is going to entangle with only the most severe Scars.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12738\" data-vbnamecard=\"12738\">Minty</a>: It would be safe to assume that, yes.<br /> <br /> Seriously, folks, I can't tell you how excited I am for the Kickstarter to begin. Manuscript previews will answer so many of your questions and much more thoroughly than I can do here.<br /> <br /> *goes back to writing up proposed Kickstarter stretch goal rewards*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-04T11:57:15-07:00","id":1329311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1329309#post1329309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span>: Deviant doesn't include the ephemeral entities rules in its core, so an Orpheus-style jaunt into the Underworld isn't likely. If you're talking about resurrecting the dead, though, that's Magnitude 5 (albeit with limits). As to the question about Scars, virtually any Scar can be entangled with any Variation, as long as the Variation's Magnitude is equal to or less than the Magnitude of the Scar. So a Magnitude 5 Variation is going to entangle with only the most severe Scars.<br /> <br /> <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span>: It would be safe to assume that, yes.<br /> <br /> Seriously, folks, I can't tell you how excited I am for the Kickstarter to begin. Manuscript previews will answer so many of your questions and much more thoroughly than I can do here.<br /> <br /> *goes back to writing up proposed Kickstarter stretch goal rewards*</div> </div> </div> </div>I've been very excited for this ks too!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-07T17:03:47-07:00","id":1329812,"title":"","content":"A thought: While it makes sense from a gameplay perspective, from an in-universe perspective how/why is it exactly that being loyal to a conspiracy or not changes which of Loyalty or Conviction you want higher?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-07T20:05:33-07:00","id":1329829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1329812#post1329812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A thought: While it makes sense from a gameplay perspective, from an in-universe perspective how/why is it exactly that being loyal to a conspiracy or not changes which of Loyalty or Conviction you want higher?</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps its a matter of which is psychologically most challenging to adhere too. While Devoted to a Conspiracy, it is constantly around you, reinforcing its ties to you, so Loyalty is a simple, easy and not as satisfying an anchor. While a Renegade, it is easy to hate, easy to blame and strike at the source of your pain, but to set aside that anger is the greater challenge, the more difficult choice, and the most rewarding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12074,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","user":"Robert D","date":". 08-07-2019, 11:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-08T05:32:32-07:00","id":1329877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1295316#post1295316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Conspirators are the most common Conviction Touchstones among Renegades, but Remade can find plenty of other objects for their rage. It need not even be anyone associated with the Divergence. It can be the dirty cop who has been shaking down the Broken's neighborhood, or the asshole ex who has been stalking the Deviant's Loyalty Touchstone, or that bully from high school who *really* needs to get what he deserves, or those fools at the university who laughed at his outlandish theories. If the Storyteller wants to bring in antagonists from other gamelines (or just monsters of the week), these can also become Conviction Touchstones.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it common to change Conviction touchstones often, or is it easy to do so at least? It depends of the Renegade I suppose, but if you just kill the stalker ex-boyfriend then what do you rage against next?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-08T12:36:19-07:00","id":1329952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1329877#post1329877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it common to change Conviction touchstones often, or is it easy to do so at least? It depends of the Renegade I suppose, but if you just kill the stalker ex-boyfriend then what do you rage against next?</div> </div> </div> </div> I believe the Devs said earlier that you get a new Conviction fairly soon after killing the last one. That means if you go on a rampage, you could potentially gatling several in quick succession.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24176-borne","name":"Borne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24176_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-08T17:21:39-07:00","id":1329995,"title":"","content":"I wonder if there\u2019s a downside to that, then; other than any narrative consequences of everyone thinking you\u2019re a murderer, including the cops.<br /> <br /> On the other hand you\u2019re just as much in a moral dilemma if you deliberately keep the Conviction touchstone alive but constantly make their life miserable and suffering.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-08T17:32:07-07:00","id":1329997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1329877#post1329877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it common to change Conviction touchstones often, or is it easy to do so at least? It depends of the Renegade I suppose, but if you just kill the stalker ex-boyfriend then what do you rage against next?</div> </div> </div> </div>Deviants can have 5 Touchstones at a time. If you have an &quot;empty&quot; slot, then you can choose a new Touchstone (of either type) once per chapter. The new Touchstone starts out Wavering, meaning it doesn't provide the full benefits of a Touchstone. To affirm a Wavering Touchstone, you have to take some action in its service that would count as fulfilling it, at which point it is no longer Wavering. Touchstones can also become Wavering by acting contrary to the Touchstone or by failing to act in its service (Faltering).<br /> <br /> Although a Merit can expand the maximum number of Touchstones slightly, the cap is there for two reasons. First, more than that makes it hard for players and STs to keep track of them and keep them in focus - much the same reason why characters in other lines can't have an unlimited number of Aspirations. Second, Touchstones provide significant mechanical benefits - Beats, Willpower, and resistance to supernatural control - so the ability to select an unlimited number of them has the potential to get out of control. I felt that left two options - place a hard limit the number of Touchstones, or impose an Experiences cost on new Touchstones. Of those choices, the latter interacted badly with the Sanctity of Merits rule (either violating it ourtright or making the threat of losing Touchstones in-play a paper tiger instead of the existential threat it's meant to be). The former was always going to be arbitrary, but it did a better job reinforcing the game's themes around Touchstones, and it was simpler at the table (no one can set up an infinite Experience-generating engine by buying Touchstones to earn more beats to buy more Touchstones).<br /> <br /> Simple question. Long answer. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Regarding the in-world explanation for Conviction/Loyalty in Renegades/Devoted, there isn't yet an &quot;official&quot; reason (Robert D.'s seems workable, though), but it would make for a good exploration in a Devoted handbook or a Players Guide.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member