age/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-13T06:51:41-07:00","id":1335487,"title":"","content":"BTW, game's tagline is &quot;A Storytelling Game of Vengeance.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-13T10:15:03-07:00","id":1335543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1335487#post1335487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">BTW, game's tagline is &quot;A Storytelling Game of Vengeance.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, nice! Where did you see that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty","name":"Minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-13T10:25:16-07:00","id":1335548,"title":"","content":"On the CofD fan-server: <br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=682\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-13T10:29:52-07:00","id":1335550,"title":"","content":"Be kind of weird for it to lack the adjective.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-13T10:49:28-07:00","id":1335552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1335402#post1335402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Characters receive total Magnitude of Variations based on the chronicle's threat level, ranging from 2 to 15 (plus 1 Scar-free Magnitude of Variation based on Origin). Players choose enough Scars to entangle all the starting Variations. Yes, it is quite possible (especially in a high-threat level game) for some characters to start with a few high-Magnitude Scars, while others start with several low-Magnitude Scars. And there are some advantages and disadvantages to both of these strategies. High-Magnitude Scars are largely attractive because high-Magnitude <i>Variations</i> are attractive, but high-Magnitude Scars are also a pretty serious hassle, with multiple high-Magnitude Scars becoming difficult to manage.</div> </div> </div> </div> This was exactly the answer I was hoping for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-13T15:56:14-07:00","id":1335623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1335481#post1335481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure I follow. Are you talking about Standard Deviations (which increase the effective Magnitude of other Scars)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Talking about the Controlled Scars mentioned in the notes for Uncontrolled whose effects are to make the entangled Variations have an activation cost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-13T20:35:52-07:00","id":1335652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1335623#post1335623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Talking about the Controlled Scars mentioned in the notes for Uncontrolled whose effects are to make the entangled Variations have an activation cost.</div> </div> </div> </div>It sounds like you might be referring to the Uncontrollable effect of Power Build-Up? If that's the case, Involuntary Scars were still in an early form during the initial round of playtests, and, quite frankly, they disintegrated under minimal pressure.<br /> <br /> First, the original Scar Resistance roll formula was Acclimation + Scar Resistance - Scar Magnitude - Instability penalty. This pretty much guaranteed that any poor wretch with an Involuntary Variation could never prevent it from activating or regain control of it once it did. This turned out to be at least one character in every playtest group, and it was definitely the most frequent topic of...critical feedback. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Additionally, once activated, there was no mechanic for getting an Involuntary Scar back under control until the end of the scene. This was especially bad for Directed Variations, and genuinely catastrophic for Lash (the attack Variation), which was how one character accidentally killed a Loyalty Touchstone in the first chapter of the playtest \u2013 it just kept attacking at random, and eventually the dice made the obvious decision about who should die. That was\u2026not very fun.<br /> <br /> Finally, there were too many easy ways to neuter Involuntary Scars so that they were way less trouble than Controlled or Persistent Scars of equal Magnitude. This didn\u2019t require an attempt to power-game or anything. The power curve (disadvantage curve?) simply wasn\u2019t steep enough.<br /> <br /> The premise of Involuntary Scars appears in a lot of the inspirational media (so much so that Dave carved out a niche for them from the game\u2019s inception), but a rework was clearly in order. The changes have hopefully resolved the issues above, but I\u2019d like a bit more playtest data before I consider Involuntary Scars truly fixed.<br /> <br /> Let me know if you\u2019re referring to something else, and I'm sorry if I seem a bit dense. I\u2019ve made a lot of posts in this thread, so it\u2019s sometimes challenging to remember what I\u2019ve spoiled.<br /> <br /> On the bright side, a lot will make far more sense once we preview entire chapters to Kickstater backers, since you'll have a big-picture view of the structure of Variations/Scars that I just can't give you, yet. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> ETA: Looking at your question again, you might also be talking about Controlled Scars in general (all of which assign a &quot;cost&quot; for activating the entangled Variations - whether it's Willpower, health, Instability, vulnerability to distractions, some form of &quot;power-up&quot; or &quot;cool-down&quot; period, etc.). I was moderately surprised by how few Controlled Scars came into play during the initial round of playtests. We may have done too good a job making it seem like the real fun of the game is a combination of powers you can't control and burdens you can't rid yourself of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":1094,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","user":"Eric Zawadzki","date":". 09-14-2019, 01:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-13T23:10:45-07:00","id":1335669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1335652#post1335652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">ETA: Looking at your question again, you might also be talking about Controlled Scars in general (all of which assign a &amp;quot;cost&amp;quot; for activating the entangled Variations</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct, this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-16T20:05:15-07:00","id":1336139,"title":"","content":"Thursday the 19th at 12 noon US Eastern time!<br /> <br /> !!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T11:04:01-07:00","id":1336246,"title":"","content":"&quot;How could you do me like that ?<br /> I took ya family in<br /> <br /> I put some cash in ya pocket<br /> made you a man again<br /> and now you let tha fear put your ass in a place<br /> complicated to escape<br /> It's a fools fate&quot;<br /> Tupac Shakur<br /> In honor of the stability preview theonyxpath.com/stability-deviant-the-renegades/","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4621,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","user":"Nicolas Milioni","date":". 09-17-2019, 02:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T12:15:51-07:00","id":1336273,"title":"","content":"So years ago a friend of mine wanted to make a splat based around Parasite Eve. Having never played the game, I listened to him explain it and mapped it out to what I think a Chronicles game would do. I don't remember exactly what I came up with, but I can say I'm glad we eventually dropped it, because Stability-and-it's-relationship-to-Scars was the trait I was trying to make and I definitely did not make this.<br /> <br /> Also, again-Madoka MG's anyone?<br /> <br /> &quot;I don't feel the pain anymore!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T12:30:50-07:00","id":1336281,"title":"","content":"One last dev blog before the Kickstarter!!! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/stability-deviant-the-renegades/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/OPP-Metal.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/stability-deviant-the-renegades/\" target=\"_blank\"> Stability [Deviant: The Renegades] &ndash; Onyx Path Publishing </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/stability-deviant-the-renegades/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://theonyxpath.com/stability-deviant-the-renegades/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T12:35:53-07:00","id":1336283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1336273#post1336273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;I don't feel the pain anymore!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Hack in alternate version of the End Stage condition that creates a persistent NPC-only character type and you can pretty much play that story arc to its conclusion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/526-schizopop","name":"schizoPOP","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T13:20:47-07:00","id":1336294,"title":"","content":"I am really pleased that it is not only possible to develop new or stronger powers in the middle of a scene, but that it seems that the most likely cause of such a thing would be the death of a Loyalty Touchstone. <br /> At first I was concerned about the starting Instability every Story, but after looking over this again it does not seem that there is rollover like there is with physical damage, so getting a Minor Instability while your track is full of Minor Instability doesn't convert the leftmost one to Medium.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty","name":"Minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T15:04:41-07:00","id":1336328,"title":"","content":"So, assuming this isn't another of those &quot;written back in July&quot; deals, you're pretty much <i>always </i>going to have that Scar Resistance penalty. I'm not sure how I feel about that.<br /> <br /> If your Instability doesn't roll over, as implied, it kind of makes getting rid of your minor Instability a Sisyphean and unrewarding task, as any progress you make will be undone very quickly. On the other hand, if Instability <i>does</i> roll over, it feels like managing it could become a top priority in a very mechanistic way.<br /> <br /> The implications of the small track and perpetual buildup are my only real issue with these rules, though. They look very good overall.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T15:25:45-07:00","id":1336336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1336328#post1336328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, assuming this isn't another of those &quot;written back in July&quot; deals, you're pretty much <i>always </i>going to have that Scar Resistance penalty.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're always going to start a story with it until you get some Acclimation, but you literally get rid of minor Instabilities by doing the things you built your character's Anchors around and this is a game where those fill in for most Aspirations.<br /> <br /> Remember that Faltering is acting <i>against</i> your Touchstones, not just failing to actively pursue their affirmation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T15:53:14-07:00","id":1336349,"title":"","content":"Considering the rules for marking Instability are a copy-paste of how marking damage works, I\u2019m pretty darn sure it rolls over.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T16:35:27-07:00","id":1336367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1336349#post1336349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering the rules for marking Instability are a copy-paste of how marking damage works, I\u2019m pretty darn sure it rolls over.</div> </div> </div> </div>I assumed that the first time I read over the post, as well, but it does not actually include anything about Minor Instability converting to Medium or Medium to Major if the rightmost box is already full. It's possible that it just didn't make it to this version of the rules, but that portion of the damage rules was not copy-pasted over.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty","name":"Minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T17:12:43-07:00","id":1336383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1336336#post1336336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're always going to start a story with it until you get some Acclimation, but you literally get rid of minor Instabilities by doing the things you built your character's Anchors around and this is a game where those fill in for most Aspirations.</div> </div> </div> </div> Virtue, Vice, and Aspirations recover Willpower and grant you Beats, which are important, but not vital, whereas Instability is a relentless countdown to your <a href=\"https://www.sakugabooru.com/post/show/14244\" target=\"_blank\">Cronenbaby moment</a> (that also penalizes you on the way there).<br /> <br /> Now, I'm largely familiar with 1e, and I don't know how often Aspirations and such are supposed to come up, but my concern is that the per-story Instability buildup will push my players to interact with their Touchstones more because of the mounting penalties than anything else. All the other ways of accruing Instability seem fine to me, since they're point-by-point and mostly driven by player choice and action.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying this quirk of the system is <i>bad</i>. It just doesn't look great from where I'm standing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T17:32:46-07:00","id":1336388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1336383#post1336383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Virtue, Vice, and Aspirations recover Willpower and grant you Beats, which are important, but not vital, whereas Instability is a relentless countdown to your <a href=\"https://www.sakugabooru.com/post/show/14244\" target=\"_blank\">Cronenbaby moment</a> (that also penalizes you on the way there).<br /> <br /> Now, I'm largely familiar with 1e, and I don't know how often Aspirations and such are supposed to come up, but my concern is that the per-story Instability buildup will push my players to interact with their Touchstones more because of the mounting penalties than anything else. All the other ways of accruing Instability seem fine to me, since they're point-by-point and mostly driven by player choice and action.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying this quirk of the system is <i>bad</i>. It just doesn't look great from where I'm standing.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Looks like working as intended to me. A Deviant has to interact with humanity and can't move on from what was done to them. The fact your Progenitor put a ticking time bomb in your soul is certainly something to be mad about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T17:47:55-07:00","id":1336393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1336383#post1336383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Virtue, Vice, and Aspirations recover Willpower and grant you Beats, which are important, but not vital, whereas Instability is a relentless countdown to your <a href=\"https://www.sakugabooru.com/post/show/14244\" target=\"_blank\">Cronenbaby moment</a> (that also penalizes you on the way there).</div> </div> </div> </div>Again: it's a &quot;relentless countdown&quot; that here is otherwise tripped solely by player action or power failure.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now, I'm largely familiar with 1e, and I don't know how often Aspirations and such are supposed to come up, </div> </div> </div>Forget how often they're supposed to come up for a moment: a normal player character (from the bluebook or the other gamelines) has <i>three</i> and a Deviant character gets <i>one</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> but my concern is that the per-story Instability buildup will push my players to interact with their Touchstones more because of the mounting penalties than anything else. </div> </div> </div>Vampire 2e's means of dealing with frenzy is that a successful roll gives you a Condition that applies a mounting penalty to subsequent rolls to resist frenzy until you fall to frenzy, kill somebody, or have a meaningful interaction with one of your Touchstones. Killing people still risks your Humanity at most levels and frenzy often escalates situations in a way that threatens similar outcomes. Losing your last Touchstone has you either scrambling for a month to find a replacement or immediately entering the sleep of the dead for weeks at minimum.<br /> <br /> Changeling 2e has spending a scene interacting with one of your Touchstones as the only way to heal Clarity damage besides resolving Clarity Conditions and that track can start as low as <i>two boxes</i> before you go Comatose, a state of affairs which is both exactly what it sounds like and the opposite of a desirable outcome to characters struggling with their perceptions and the possibility of extradimensional re-abduction. Losing your last Touchstone heightens the risk that your character will take Clarity damage just from dreaming of their time in Arcadia and immediately inflicts them with an irrational delusion until they manage to set up a replacement relationship, on top of removing most means of healing Clarity damage beyond the lower bounds of the Trait.<br /> <br /> Both of those games also have the mounting disconnect your character has with other people and/or reality as the main concern their respective stats hold at bay. This kind of upkeep is not new.<br /> <br /> Deviant is built around characters whose self-concept is sufficiently fucked that they need their Touchstones to hold themselves together. You start out with multiple Touchstones for free where other gamelines have that as an extra thing you need to take a Merit for, and the game's failure states specifically include &quot;you've completely disconnected from all your Touchstones&quot; due to the way Loyalty and Conviction work.<br /> <br /> If your players aren't invested in their characters' Touchstones then that is a <i>different problem</i> than their still needing to engage with them for the maintenance purposes that the mechanics provide.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T17:51:13-07:00","id":1336395,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12738\" data-vbnamecard=\"12738\">Minty</a>: The relevant section got left out accidentally because I cut the example text for the blog (we try to keep them under 2k), and it was sandwiched between two examples. Instability upgrades just like Health damage does. Sorry for the confusion. And yes, it's no accident that losing a Loyalty Touchstone tends to seriously f' up a Deviant (and give her ready access to greater power to use against you right after you seriously pissed her off); there's a reason they tend to be hyper-protective of them.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar97_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"97\" data-vbnamecard=\"97\">The MG</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a>, and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar180_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"180\" data-vbnamecard=\"180\">Leliel</a>: I want to see some further playtests of Stability to make sure it's a real and constant threat, rather than a paper tiger or a completely fun-destroying PITA. We did a fair amount of tinkering on it after pre-KS playtests (Scar Resistance rolls were once further penalized by the Magnitude of the Scar <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" />), and I'll continue tinkering with this system based on post-KS feedback and playtests until it works as intended. A couple data points that might be of interest:<br /> <br /> - Approximately 1 in 3 of Scars use Scar Resistance rolls, so the penalty to these doesn't affect every Deviant.<br /> - The Stabilizer Merit the blog mentions curbs Instability penalties on a 1-for-1 basis, making it a key purchase for Remade with a combination of a high-Magnitude Variation, low Acclimation, and Scars that call for Scar Resistance rolls.<br /> - The goal is for minor Instability to be pretty much a constant for Broken with high-Magnitude Variations, although it's fairly easy to clear with Touchstone work. Medium Instability is much less common but requires serious effort to remove - either taking a significant personal risk for the sake of a Loyalty Touchstone or permanently accepting a new Scar. Major Instability is rare and serious, and the only ways to deal with it are to accept a new Scar (which merely downgrades it) or to kill a Conviction Touchstone (which is an ugly solution to one's personal problems).<br /> <br /> I appreciate the sincere feedback offered in good faith. I always want to make the best game I can, after all! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T20:26:59-07:00","id":1336442,"title":"","content":"Are Guardians/Nemeses supposed to have 2 Conviction, 2 Loyalty or max of the opposite kind (Loyalty for renegades, Conviction for devoted)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T21:07:11-07:00","id":1336470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1336393#post1336393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again: it's a &quot;relentless countdown&quot; that here is otherwise tripped solely by player action or power failure.</div> </div> </div> </div> And, again, it's a different and more pressing incentive than recovering Willpower.<br /> <br /> I appreciate the rundown of 2e social mechanics. Have you had the chance to test them out in play? I'd be very interested in hearing how often, say, Clarity damage triggers, or how Touchstone interactions have slotted into the story of your games.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1336395#post1336395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I appreciate the sincere feedback offered in good faith. I always want to make the best game I can, after all! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div> I can't really call it feedback when I haven't even tried it out. It's more of &quot;a thing I'm not sold on&quot; that's getting disproportionate airtime.<br /> <br /> Alright, last note on the topic: do you have any examples of scenes and interactions that could count for Instability recovery (particularly via Conviction Touchstones)?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T21:31:46-07:00","id":1336483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deinos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1336442#post1336442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are Guardians/Nemeses supposed to have 2 Conviction, 2 Loyalty or max of the opposite kind (Loyalty for renegades, Conviction for devoted)?</div> </div> </div> </div>A Guardian has more Loyalty than Conviction, and a Nemesis has more Conviction than Loyalty. The sum of Conviction and Loyalty cannot exceed 5 (a Merit exists that slightly increases this). There will be more detail once we get into the KS.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1336470#post1336470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright, last note on the topic: do you have any examples of scenes and interactions that could count for Instability recovery (particularly via Conviction Touchstones)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Fulfilling Conviction is actually pretty easy. Let's say you go to the public records office and find blueprints of the conspiracy building where your Conviction Touchstone works. That's sufficient. Tailing one of her associates so that you can rough him up and convince him to cough up information that you can use against her? Also fine. Face-to-face confrontations certainly count, but the key question is whether you're taking tangible steps on the path to destroying your sworn enemies. If you are, you heal a minor Instability.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-18T04:43:22-07:00","id":1336528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.Scissors</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1331916#post1331916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Earlier on this tread, there was the discussion regarding Beasts and their relationship with Deviants (A Beast goading a renegade to &quot;embrace&quot; their monstrous side not knowing that it will backfire on them big time). I want to post an idea that Hunters might be the only splat that could theoretically could work well with Deviants.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know, deviants don't strike me as too far off from beasts -- they both have soul issues, and the balance of family ties &amp; hunger is not very different from the balance of loyalty &amp; conviction. Likewise, hooking a deviant and their touchstones up with an otherworldly safe place could be pretty helpful, if the beast isn't one himself. &quot;They show the transformed kindness even when \u2014 especially when \u2014 she\u2019s incapable of showing it to herself, and they have her back even if they don\u2019t always agree with her choices.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-18T04:47:19-07:00","id":1336529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1336483#post1336483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A Guardian has more Loyalty than Conviction, and a Nemesis has more Conviction than Loyalty. The sum of Conviction and Loyalty cannot exceed 5 (a Merit exists that slightly increases this). There will be more detail once we get into the KS.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah okay, so it doesn't have to be 5/0 or 0/5. Thank you for the fast reply. Lotta possibilities for characterization.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-18T10:21:36-07:00","id":1336590,"title":"","content":"So how hard <i>is</i> it supposed to be to become and stay a Guardian? Because right now it looks like it just takes two to four chapters (depending on Origin) of swapping out Touchstones to become one and then one session to have a buffer against Faltering.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-18T16:45:06-07:00","id":1336704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1336590#post1336590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So how hard <i>is</i> it supposed to be to become and stay a Guardian? Because right now it looks like it just takes two to four chapters (depending on Origin) of swapping out Touchstones to become one and then one session to have a buffer against Faltering.</div> </div> </div> </div>In a vacuum, it's pretty easy. Self-Made do it early quite often. But Guardians aren't an end state like Beast's Inheritances. A couple dead Loyalty Touchstones can rip you out of that status, and one good traitor could turn you into one of the Devoted (a story-based transformation with guidance, not a mechanically mandated one, btw). I'll limit it to that, for now, since the Kickstarter is just around the corner, and this will make more sense if you're given the full context.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-18T18:52:49-07:00","id":1336735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1032843-what-we-know-so-far-deviant-the-renegades?p=1336704#post1336704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In a vacuum, it's pretty easy. Self-Made do it early quite often. But Guardians aren't an end state like Beast's Inheritances. A couple dead Loyalty Touchstones can rip you out of that status, and one good traitor could turn you into one of the Devoted (a story-based transformation with guidance, not a mechanically mandated one, btw). I'll limit it to that, for now, since the Kickstarter is just around the corner, and this will make more sense if you're given the full context.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I must have missed something what is a Guardian?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1383-yrtalien","name":"yrtalien","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-18T19:04:22-07:00","id":1336737,"title":"","content":"A Renegade with higher Loyalty than Conviction, which helps with Scars and Instability in some way beyond what\u2019s been teased yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-18T23:58:20-07:00","id":1336790,"title":"","content":"Devoted don't have Guardians; instead they have Nemeses, who have their Conviction higher than Loyalty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-19T07:24:42-07:00","id":1336863,"title":"","content":"Happy KS day, when it launches in a few hours at least. Everyone ready to finally get looking at the manuscript? And maybe an official sub forum for the line? I didn't participate in the Beast one so no idea when they got theirs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":